t; it might get worse and you'd die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T09:33:22-07:00","id":1235965,"title":"","content":"We\u2019re playing with them in various games this week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T09:48:59-07:00","id":1235971,"title":"","content":"Did they bring back the regeneration charms (Bruise Relief Method or Halt the Scarlet Flow, if I remember right)? 'cos I would like to see how they made that gel with the new combat system.<br /> <br /> Great show by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4972-hurum","name":"hurum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T09:53:55-07:00","id":1235974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1235942#post1235942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*coughs*AURA*coughs* *COUGHS*underwhelmingcharms*COUGHS**coughs*wouldn' teverinamillionyearsplayaDBusingDBcharmsratherthan MAandEvocations*</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the charms are fine though. They could be a little stronger but it's about the level they should be at. MA and evocations aren't much better for DBs unless you learn the dragon styles. Though, it does essentially make the strongest DB's martial artists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T10:15:34-07:00","id":1235986,"title":"","content":"The strongest DBs were always the Immaculate martial artists, and Aura is what allows Dragon-Blooded access to stronger abilities than what they would otherwise been allowed to have. <br /> <br /> I really don\u2019t see how Aura is worse than the headache that was surcharges. <br /> <br /> And this discussion should be taking place in another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T10:30:56-07:00","id":1235993,"title":"","content":"Yeah, let's keep it on Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T10:37:17-07:00","id":1235997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1235986#post1235986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this discussion should be taking place in another thread.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to make that thread I said I wouldn't, I think. There's more interest in it than I thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T10:41:47-07:00","id":1236006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hurum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1235971#post1235971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did they bring back the regeneration charms (Bruise Relief Method or Halt the Scarlet Flow, if I remember right)? 'cos I would like to see how they made that gel with the new combat system.<br /> <br /> Great show by the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they did. We can talk about that hopefully on the next episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T10:56:58-07:00","id":1236014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1235986#post1235986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The strongest DBs were always the Immaculate martial artists, and Aura is what allows Dragon-Blooded access to stronger abilities than what they would otherwise been allowed to have.<br /> <br /> I really don\u2019t see how Aura is worse than the headache that was surcharges.<br /> <br /> And this discussion should be taking place in another thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just like to apologize for the disruptive phrasing of my post. I didn't consider my words and the place I was saying them, and derailed the thread. My apologies to everyone here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T12:16:43-07:00","id":1236057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackwingedheaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1235597#post1235597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the preview into Lunar charms! I know my group has been chomping at the bit for Lunars-related stuff, so this will be great news for them. I think it's hilarious that two of the example characters from the podcast were a polar bear totem who fights with a hammer and a wasp totem, since one of the major NPCs of my first long Exalted game was a polar bear totem who fought with a hammer and one of the PCs in my last Exalted game was a wasp-totem. Great minds!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I always picture Massive Deadly Hybrids when I think about making Lunars. I wanted something from the North and Polar Bear seemed to fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24236-reformedninja","name":"ReformedNinja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T12:52:12-07:00","id":1236077,"title":"","content":"Speaking of massive. How does the Grow Legendary Size charm work? Only on your Spirit Shape or can you toss it on DBT as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:00:28-07:00","id":1236082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236077#post1236077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of massive. How does the Grow Legendary Size charm work? Only on your Spirit Shape or can you toss it on DBT as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a Strength charm that allows you to take the form of a Legendary size animal. I personally think the cost is a little high. it's like 15 motes + 1 wp to activate and you must immediately pay 4 additional motes. At the start of your turn you have to pay an additional 4 motes for every turn or revert back to human form. So right out of the gate you pay 19 motes + 1wp to go legendary size. You get 5 motes back a turn and 4 have to go immediately back to maintain the transformation.<br /> <br /> On the surface it seems like a big price to pay but I need to test it and see if the benefits of being that large and not being able to be withered down offset the high cost. I trust the developers on this, but I'm gonna test it out before I make a final verdict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24236-reformedninja","name":"ReformedNinja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:12:40-07:00","id":1236094,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... That is very pricey, but from my own 3rd ed game, I saw that turning into a legendary size creature was generally the best strategy, better than DBT or any other form. So saying yes, it's very good, but it's exhausting to sustain for long, is a more fun way to balance it than needing the power level of elephants, tyrant lizards, etc.<br /> <br /> The only issue is that before the whole party could ride the Lunar long distance s, and this means they won't be able to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:15:12-07:00","id":1236096,"title":"","content":"There can be ways to mitigate the costs of staying Huge. Hearthstones, artifacts with appropriate Evocations, advanced Charms...<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t understand the point of paying an immediate additional cost rather than folding it into the initial cost. Not unless the act of growing huge is useful as a brief effect, such as for breaking out of a clinch or scaring the shit out of someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:16:00-07:00","id":1236097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReformedNinja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236082#post1236082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a Strength charm that allows you to take the form of a Legendary size animal. I personally think the cost is a little high. it's like 15 motes + 1 wp to activate and you must immediately pay 4 additional motes. At the start of your turn you have to pay an additional 4 motes for every turn or revert back to human form. So right out of the gate you pay 19 motes + 1wp to go legendary size. You get 5 motes back a turn and 4 have to go immediately back to maintain the transformation.<br /> <br /> On the surface it seems like a big price to pay but I need to test it and see if the benefits of being that large and not being able to be withered down offset the high cost. I trust the developers on this, but I'm gonna test it out before I make a final verdict.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's one hell of a deal breaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:17:25-07:00","id":1236099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236094#post1236094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... That is very pricey, but from my own 3rd ed game, I saw that turning into a legendary size creature was generally the best strategy, better than DBT or any other form. So saying yes, it's very good, but it's exhausting to sustain for long, is a more fun way to balance it than needing the power level of elephants, tyrant lizards, etc.<br /> <br /> The only issue is that before the whole party could ride the Lunar long distance s, and this means they won't be able to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do have to add this. If you are out of combat it's 4 motes per hour. Same deal, when you get 5 back you spend 4. Turning into a Yeddium and being a ride for the rest of the party can be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24236-reformedninja","name":"ReformedNinja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:22:43-07:00","id":1236106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReformedNinja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236082#post1236082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a Strength charm that allows you to take the form of a Legendary size animal. I personally think the cost is a little high. it's like 15 motes + 1 wp to activate and you must immediately pay 4 additional motes. At the start of your turn you have to pay an additional 4 motes for every turn or revert back to human form. So right out of the gate you pay 19 motes + 1wp to go legendary size. You get 5 motes back a turn and 4 have to go immediately back to maintain the transformation.<br /> <br /> On the surface it seems like a big price to pay but I need to test it and see if the benefits of being that large and not being able to be withered down offset the high cost. I trust the developers on this, but I'm gonna test it out before I make a final verdict.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does it work out of combat or is it only a combat charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:24:37-07:00","id":1236109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReformedNinja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236082#post1236082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a Strength charm that allows you to take the form of a Legendary size animal. I personally think the cost is a little high. it's like 15 motes + 1 wp to activate and you must immediately pay 4 additional motes. At the start of your turn you have to pay an additional 4 motes for every turn or revert back to human form. So right out of the gate you pay 19 motes + 1wp to go legendary size. You get 5 motes back a turn and 4 have to go immediately back to maintain the transformation.<br /> <br /> On the surface it seems like a big price to pay but I need to test it and see if the benefits of being that large and not being able to be withered down offset the high cost. I trust the developers on this, but I'm gonna test it out before I make a final verdict.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://<br /> &#91;url&#93;https://getyarn.io/yarn-clip/embed-test/8e35de5a-822e-4079-bdb9-7750d1141ec9&#91;/url&#93;\" target=\"_blank\">https://&lt;br /&gt; &amp;#91;url&amp;#93;https://getyarn....&amp;#91;/url&amp;#93;</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:57:09-07:00","id":1236126,"title":"","content":"I kind of feel that Legendary Size, particularly if it's accessible at Essence 1, <i>needs</i> to be expensive to be balanced. The benefits of Legendary Size are pretty extensive: <br /> 1) You can't be crashed except by very big attacks (10+ <i>post soak</i> damage pools),<br /> 2) You can't take more than (attacker's Str)+3 levels of damage (before charms).<br /> 3) You can't be grappled, and your own grappling attacks are made unopposed, barring special magic that makes the opponent capable of grappling huge creatures.<br /> 4) You don't take onslaught penalties to your defense from smaller creatures.<br /> 5) You can't be smashed or knocked back. <br /> <br /> All of that is <i>pretty potent</i>. That said, I could see it getting less impressive at higher Essence. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12730_4.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12730\" data-vbnamecard=\"12730\">PneumaPilot</a> , was there anything in the playtest document you noticed about making the Legendary Size charm cheaper at higher Essence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T14:05:00-07:00","id":1236131,"title":"","content":"If you can use the initial growth to make an unopposed grappling gambit, that could very well be worth a temporary growth without the additional 4 motes. Especially if you\u2019re using it to break free of a clinch; 15m to reverse a hold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T14:45:02-07:00","id":1236155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReformedNinja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236082#post1236082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a Strength charm that allows you to take the form of a Legendary size animal. I personally think the cost is a little high. it's like 15 motes + 1 wp to activate and you must immediately pay 4 additional motes. At the start of your turn you have to pay an additional 4 motes for every turn or revert back to human form. So right out of the gate you pay 19 motes + 1wp to go legendary size. You get 5 motes back a turn and 4 have to go immediately back to maintain the transformation.<br /> <br /> On the surface it seems like a big price to pay but I need to test it and see if the benefits of being that large and not being able to be withered down offset the high cost. I trust the developers on this, but I'm gonna test it out before I make a final verdict.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 15m cost matches most warstriders' attunement costs, and 4m/hour is what you give up in hearthstone to power a warstrider. Other costs and benefits don't match up as well (though 4m/turn and -4 penalty to attacks against human-scale opponents match a bit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T14:47:57-07:00","id":1236157,"title":"","content":"Obviously I haven't seen it in context, but <i>15m, 1wp, +4m/turn</i> seems excessive, particularly if you have to spend the first +4m on the turn of activation.<br /> <br /> Surely there's some more elegant solution, or at least one that doesn't screw you outside of combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 07-17-2018, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T15:04:22-07:00","id":1236163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReformedNinja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236099#post1236099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have to add this. If you are out of combat it's 4 motes per hour. Same deal, when you get 5 back you spend 4. Turning into a Yeddium and being a ride for the rest of the party can be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's fine then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surely there's some more elegant solution, or at least one that doesn't screw you outside of combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, ReformedNinja said that outside combat is 4m an hour.<br /> <br /> So, slightly less than your mote regen either way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T15:34:14-07:00","id":1236177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236126#post1236126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of feel that Legendary Size, particularly if it's accessible at Essence 1, <i>needs</i> to be expensive to be balanced. The benefits of Legendary Size are pretty extensive:<br /> 1) You can't be crashed except by very big attacks (10+ <i>post soak</i> damage pools),<br /> 2) You can't take more than (attacker's Str)+3 levels of damage (before charms).<br /> 3) You can't be grappled, and your own grappling attacks are made unopposed, barring special magic that makes the opponent capable of grappling huge creatures.<br /> 4) You don't take onslaught penalties to your defense from smaller creatures.<br /> 5) You can't be smashed or knocked back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll also add that the forms not only have Legendary Size, but also high combat pools, massive soak, and often other useful merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T15:46:13-07:00","id":1236179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236163#post1236163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, ReformedNinja said that outside combat is 4m an hour.<br /> <br /> So, slightly less than your mote regen either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but the primary benefits of Legendary Size \u2013 all of the benefits, really, aside from elevated Feat pf Strength minima \u2013 lie in combat, don't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T15:52:47-07:00","id":1236182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236179#post1236179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but the primary benefits of Legendary Size \u2013 all of the benefits, really, aside from elevated Feat pf Strength minima \u2013 lie in combat, don't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they all lie in combat, then why express a concern with being screwed outside of combat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T15:58:19-07:00","id":1236183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236182#post1236182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they all lie in combat, then why express a concern with being screwed outside of combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you seriously asking this? Or just being facetious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T16:07:46-07:00","id":1236189,"title":"","content":"No, nonono, I don't like this, this is not a good look on me. Maybe later; it's been an odd kind of day.<br /> <br /> Errrr bpbpbrrr I wonder if there are any distinct Charms that key off of assuming Legendary size. With that kind of (provisional, probably subject to change) mote cost, I wonder if such Charms might be effective as Permanent enhancements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 07-17-2018, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T16:18:04-07:00","id":1236192,"title":"","content":"When you come back, maybe consider fixing the link in your previous post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T16:27:25-07:00","id":1236197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236192#post1236192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you come back</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going somewhere, I just opted to withdraw a particular kind of response (or at least defer it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">consider fixing the link in your previous post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Urrgghh, my kingdom for effective video clips that come from somewhere besides YouTube. I swear, I am this close to going through with that crazy notion I always had before I actually made videos, in which I personally edit a library of private soundbites and one-liners, to deploy as called for.<br /> <br /> It's supposed to link to a clip of Jim Carrey as the Grinch proclaiming &quot;but that's what these tests are for&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T16:38:08-07:00","id":1236201,"title":"","content":"I think that the legendary size costs should be taken in context. You have access to all the action pools of the creature, dice in excess of your own dice pools are counted as bonus dice you don't have to pay motes for, and in addition to all those merits and special abilities and latent abilities that you can learn, you can also apply your charms to those attacks.<br /> <br /> We're not just talking about a Tyrant Lizard for example. We're talking about a Tyrant Lizard that can use Charms and boost its special abilities with Excellencies. You might be able to spot an example right now of where this could get very scary very quickly, and that's without even thinking about charms for the Physical Attributes!<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's pretty costly too! That seems like it makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":23657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","user":"VioletDreamer","date":". 07-17-2018, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T16:45:12-07:00","id":1236203,"title":"","content":"Plus, anyone see Antman and the Wasp?<br /> <br /> \u201cI slept for three days.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T18:01:01-07:00","id":1236225,"title":"","content":"I don't know if you can grow huge reflexively (I doubt it) or if it must be a Miscellaneous shapeshifting action (which may or may not change your species at the same time).<br /> <br /> It's likely a miscellaneous action, or a special combat action for shapeshifting, but either way, I hope it has a special dispensation to flurry with a feat of strength action without the usual flurry penalties. Because surely, growing huge and strong underneath something you wish to lift up (or keep from falling) would <i>only</i> help your efforts rather than hinder them, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T18:30:57-07:00","id":1236240,"title":"","content":"Ok ok, let's talk about the defining issue here...<br /> <br /> Can lunars still turn into a swarm?<br /> <br /> If so, can that be a swarm of jaguars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T19:23:31-07:00","id":1236258,"title":"","content":"There's so much power and versatility in gaining Legendary Size at the drop of a hat, I'm totally okay with the cost (again, with the possible exception of the immediate +4m cost). Especially if it's really an Essence 1 Charm, because that leaves so much room for improvement.<br /> <br /> You become a monster on the battlefield even before figuring in the special traits and features of the particular animal you became. And if you didn't become an animal, Vance told me that moonsilver armor and weapons grow with you instead of vanishing into Elsewhere.<br /> <br /> You can presumably break free of bindings and clinches instantly, while automatically succeeding at a clinch against your opponent. If some Charm allows you to flurry a shapeshifting action with a grapple gambit, you could do both in the same turn for a complete reversal, and you don't even need to stay at that size once the clinch is established... though naturally it's advantageous if you do.<br /> <br /> You can lift massive weights, performing great feats of strength or demolition, and throwing massive objects at your enemies. You can also carry multiple allies away to safety.<br /> <br /> Shock and awe! It's probably a great opportunity for Threaten actions and helps with forcing damaged battle-groups to rout.<br /> <br /> Protean Charms that key off of being bigger than your opponent, or just big enough to casually wreck the environment with your mighty mass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T20:03:18-07:00","id":1236271,"title":"","content":"Lunar characters start at Essence 1, yes? Is there any method for them to gain access to higher essence charms early?<br /> <br /> If not, how do just the essence 1 charms look? Pretty cool? Will we be sad that we can't have some &quot;basic capability&quot; until later?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T20:43:39-07:00","id":1236280,"title":"","content":"I imagine that the Nine Attribute Heart's Blood Charms are Essence 2 at the highest, but with Attribute minimums at least as high as 4, so you can have the ones that most resonate with your character concept without easily getting all or even most of them.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they all start at Essence 1, and each one after the first is treated as having a higher minimum by one dot, capping at Essence 5. Make a journey of your Sacred Hunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T20:46:02-07:00","id":1236281,"title":"","content":"Query: The replace Dex with Strength Melee charm, what is its activation cost and category? (Reflexive, simple etc)?<br /> <br /> Many thanks for posting your thoughts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T20:56:59-07:00","id":1236282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236281#post1236281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query: The replace Dex with Strength Melee charm, what is its activation cost and category? (Reflexive, simple etc)?<br /> <br /> Many thanks for posting your thoughts!</div> </div> </div> </div>Cost: \u2014<br /> Type: Permanent","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T21:02:49-07:00","id":1236283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236282#post1236282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cost: \u2014<br /> Type: Permanent</div> </div> </div> </div>Errm. Wow. That\u2019s .... <br /> <br /> *Composes self* <br /> <br /> Is the Kickstarter for this soon, by any chance? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T21:37:59-07:00","id":1236290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236283#post1236283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Errm. Wow. That\u2019s ....<br /> <br /> *Composes self*<br /> <br /> Is the Kickstarter for this soon, by any chance? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They've said before that they doubt it'll be this year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T22:03:53-07:00","id":1236296,"title":"","content":"On which note, I'm pretty sure the teasers from this playtest will prevent a number of obsessive fits I might otherwise have lapsed into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T22:17:55-07:00","id":1236301,"title":"","content":"Thank the Gods for that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThe very existence of flame-throwers proves that some time, somewhere, someone said to themselves, You know, I want to set those people over there on fire, but I'm just not close enough to get the job done.\u201d George Carlin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/123-trax","name":"Trax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar123_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T23:18:56-07:00","id":1236314,"title":"","content":"Now I think the real question is this:<br /> <br /> Any sign of these Buy-In Lunar Bond Charms yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T03:10:08-07:00","id":1236345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236271#post1236271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar characters start at Essence 1, yes? Is there any method for them to gain access to higher essence charms early?<br /> <br /> <br /> If not, how do just the essence 1 charms look? Pretty cool? Will we be sad that we can't have some &amp;quot;basic capability&amp;quot; until later?</div> </div> </div> </div>We talked about this a fair bit in the episode. No way to get higher-Essence Charms early, but the Essence 1 Charms cover most of the awesome stuff right out of the gate. I was super excited to make an Essence 1 character. Nothing really missing, but plenty to look forward to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T05:43:45-07:00","id":1236381,"title":"","content":"Can we all take a moment to appreciate that \u201cbasic capability\u201d no longer includes the concept of \u201cperfect defenses\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T05:49:28-07:00","id":1236382,"title":"","content":"I assume that any Lunar capacity to subdivide into a swarm of small creatures or multiply into a battle-group of medium-sized creatures would be in Dexterity.<br /> <br /> I hope that the path to get there involves Shadow Clone substitution dodges / attempts to enter concealment.<br /> <br /> Given how battle-groups can attack multiple targets at once, the path will almost certainly include an extra attack Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:14:12-07:00","id":1236412,"title":"","content":"Keep this kind of quality up and this will be the first Exalted 3e book I back on Kickstarter. I've been out of Exalted for quite a long time and have been reluctant to get back into it and I told myself that Lunars would be the make or break book for me, as they have been my favorite type, flavor wise not mechanically, since 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:46:21-07:00","id":1236427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236345#post1236345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We talked about this a fair bit in the episode. No way to get higher-Essence Charms early, but the Essence 1 Charms cover most of the awesome stuff right out of the gate. I was super excited to make an Essence 1 character. Nothing really missing, but plenty to look forward to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this helped any by the range of options that any given single Attribute might afford at Essence 1? Not at character creation, sure, but the fact that it takes fewer lines of character development to have a greater range of options?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T09:18:14-07:00","id":1236439,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> I\u2019m not terribly sure I understand the question. Can you elaborate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T09:27:19-07:00","id":1236442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236439#post1236439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> I\u2019m not terribly sure I understand the question. Can you elaborate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars only have nine Attributes, compared to 25 Abilities for Solar Charms. I presume that any given Attribute covers a wider range of applications (even if it doesn't have as many written Charms) than an Ability; you have to raise fewer stats to gain access to a larger range of options.<br /> <br /> I presume that Strength alone gives access to things that are comparable towhat a Solar would need to separately invest in Melee, Brawl, Athletics, possibly a bit of Resistance or Survival, maybe even some Ride or Sail? Sure there are probably a lot of non-comparables, but that's at least part of it?<br /> <br /> After all, you've already said that Wits is where some things to develop animal familiars are, and I have to assume that it also includes some things beneficial to social interaction, so how many Abilities would a Solar need to build up to gain access to the same range of options?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T09:49:14-07:00","id":1236448,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah! There are LOTS of toys in every area available at character creation! It is very broad indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:40:25-07:00","id":1236471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236182#post1236182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they all lie in combat, then why express a concern with being screwed outside of combat?</div> </div> </div> </div> Because stomping around as a titan is still cool, and because 4m/hour is a steep cost for looking cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236189#post1236189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, nonono, I don't like this, this is not a good look on me.</div> </div> </div> </div> It isn't, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T12:04:50-07:00","id":1236504,"title":"","content":"You know, I think that there are international laws against opening fire on a person in retreat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:06:45-07:00","id":1236524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236471#post1236471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because stomping around as a titan is still cool, and because 4m/hour is a steep cost for looking cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a rather subjective statement. I would say 4m/hour is paltry since I get to stomp around as a behemoth! Also, it means you can do it indefinitely since you're still recovering 1m/hour (down from the normal 5m/h). Finally, 4m/hour is what everyone else in-game loses by socketing a greater hearthstone into a warstrider to do their &quot;titan stomping around&quot;!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:13:00-07:00","id":1236528,"title":"","content":"Exactly how customisable are Hybrid Body Transformation and Deadly Beastman Transformation? The versions of the charms Eska has seem to suggest that you're discouraged from making your Warform be focused on being an evasive fast fighter, with the &quot;unavoidable -1 defense penalty&quot;, but her Hybrid Body Transformation seems like a player might be able to choose which merits the charm applies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11594-namillus","name":"Namillus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:47:51-07:00","id":1236546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236504#post1236504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I think that there are international laws against opening fire on a person in retreat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes, even when you say I'm sorry, what you originally said was sufficient that people will go <i>&quot;Good, you should be.&quot;</i> That's not firing on someone in retreat. It's making it clear that, <i>yes,</i> you very much needed to apologize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T18:13:14-07:00","id":1236639,"title":"","content":"What can you say about Lunar excellencies? Do you have to buy them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T19:02:10-07:00","id":1236643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236639#post1236639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can you say about Lunar excellencies? Do you have to buy them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your question has been added to our show notes for the next episode! Quick answer: No","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T21:37:01-07:00","id":1236672,"title":"","content":"There's something no one has talked or asked about, and I'm almost afraid to ask.<br /> <br /> One of the most drastic changes to the Lunar Exalted should be in the realm of Crafts and Medicine, as these are traditionally places where they have been extremely weak. Weaker than Dragon-Blooded, and vastly overshadowed by Alchemicals.<br /> <br /> First Edition explicitly featured a side-bar that took up one-third of a page, entitled The Narrow Path, which essentially equated Heart's Blood shapeshifting and all Lunar Charms, suggesting that Lunar Charms would be incapable of allowing Lunar Exalted to excel outside of the sorts of things that shapeshifting directly enabled, like combat, stealth, and travel. This edition had no Appearance Charms at all.<br /> <br /> Second Edition abandoned such overt surrender, but lacked a coherent vision for what Lunar Charms ought to be, and committed very few Charms to the fields of making things or treating wounds. The writers were so uninspired, they deliberately re-used a Dragon-Blooded Charm name and concept and admitted to it in the Charm itself. Somehow, Lunars actually LOST much of their ability to heal other people, as the Mother's Touch Charm didn't return in any fashion.<br /> <br /> <br /> I remember Robert Vance being excited about finishing a Lunar crafting Charm concept that only Lunars could pull off, and also suggesting (if not promising) that Lunar crafting would actually be superior to Dragon-Blooded Craft.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've long hoped that Lunar Intelligence would feature a &quot;logical puzzle-solving&quot; branch of Charms that would equally express feats like picking locks, deciphering codes and foreign languages, and crafting tools to meet a need. This might or might not also include the Lunar Exalted's own heist-planning Charm, like Master Plan Meditation and Vault-Emptying Whirlwind Heist, or retroactive prepared-planning Charms like <i>Miracle of the Solar Exalted's</i> Ever-Ready Innovation Discipline.<br /> <br /> Robert hinted at a Charm for retroactive traps, at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't even know what to hope Lunar healing would look like, let alone imagine how it compares to Dragon-Blooded Medicine.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-19-2018, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T23:08:55-07:00","id":1236682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236672#post1236672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something no one has talked or asked about, and I'm almost afraid to ask.<br /> <br /> One of the most drastic changes to the Lunar Exalted should be in the realm of Crafts and Medicine, as these are traditionally places where they have been extremely weak. Weaker than Dragon-Blooded, and vastly overshadowed by Alchemicals.<br /> <br /> First Edition explicitly featured a side-bar that took up one-third of a page, entitled The Narrow Path, which essentially equated Heart's Blood shapeshifting and all Lunar Charms, suggesting that Lunar Charms would be incapable of allowing Lunar Exalted to excel outside of the sorts of things that shapeshifting directly enabled, like combat, stealth, and travel. <b>This edition had no Appearance Charms at all.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That was for... special reasons. The statement about not wanting to hose Lunars with ugly totems still sears in my brainmeats to this very day...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second Edition abandoned such overt surrender, but lacked a coherent vision for what Lunar Charms ought to be, and committed very few Charms to the fields of making things or treating wounds. The writers were so uninspired, they deliberately re-used a Dragon-Blooded Charm name and concept and admitted to it in the Charm itself. Somehow, Lunars actually LOST much of their ability to heal other people, as the Mother's Touch Charm didn't return in any fashion.<br /> <br /> <br /> I remember Robert Vance being excited about finishing a Lunar crafting Charm concept that only Lunars could pull off, and also suggesting (if not promising) that Lunar crafting would actually be superior to Dragon-Blooded Craft.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've long hoped that Lunar Intelligence would feature a &quot;logical puzzle-solving&quot; branch of Charms that would equally express feats like picking locks, deciphering codes and foreign languages, and crafting tools to meet a need. This might or might not also include the Lunar Exalted's own heist-planning Charm, like Master Plan Meditation and Vault-Emptying Whirlwind Heist, or retroactive prepared-planning Charms like <i>Miracle of the Solar Exalted's</i> Ever-Ready Innovation Discipline.<br /> <br /> Robert hinted at a Charm for retroactive traps, at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>I don't even know what to hope Lunar healing would look like, let alone imagine how it compares to Dragon-Blooded Medicine.</b><br /> <br /> . </div> </div> </div>Kind of like the Alchemical healing Charms where you could hug someone healthy, I'd imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T00:56:42-07:00","id":1236688,"title":"","content":"I remember now... a more cogent form of the concern that I expressed in my first post is getting the whole Charm set in this manner. Or rather, getting any given thing that I would have been a delightful surprise if discovered directly in the book. It does seem unlikely that they'll detail hundreds of Charms, but there's always the possibility that any given one that is described will diminish the experience of seeing it first hand. That and the emergent patterns; those are definitely something that I want to find out for myself.<br /> <br /> I'm going to withdraw from the discussion. That's not a knock on it happening, just a recognition of my own preferences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T03:35:22-07:00","id":1236711,"title":"","content":"What tricks does a Lunar have for patching up someone else?<br /> <br /> For crafting?<br /> <br /> For eating a ludicrous number of cakes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-19-2018, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T04:40:52-07:00","id":1236720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236711#post1236711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What tricks does a Lunar have for patching up someone else?<br /> <br /> For crafting?<br /> <br /> For eating a ludicrous number of cakes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha! I don\u2019t know about that last one, but we\u2019ve got the other two in the show notes for the next ep.!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T04:51:26-07:00","id":1236722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236720#post1236720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know about that last one\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i>Masters of Jade</i> featured a mention of a Lunar who was trying to stop her Solar mate from getting tangled up in the Guild, so when he was commissioned to bake a great number of cakes for them, she snuck in and ate them. <i>All of them</i>. Dozens of cakes. <br /> <br /> She also got an illustration in the Ex3 Core's blurbs for the different Abilities.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T04:53:22-07:00","id":1236723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236720#post1236720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haha! I don\u2019t know about that last one, but we\u2019ve got the other two in the show notes for the next ep.!</div> </div> </div> </div>We already have that one covered, actually: Titan up! Eat hundreds of cakes, Titan down! Keep that slim waist...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T04:57:18-07:00","id":1236725,"title":"","content":"-Can- Lunars' shapeshifting let them eat arbitrarily large numbers of cakes? What if they turn into a Tyrant Lizard and eat a large bakery's worth of cakes? Would they have an epic stomach-ache when they transform back into human form? What if they become an ant? Do they gain weight, ever? Can they just shapeshift their sins away?<br /> <br /> These are the <b>real</b> questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T06:09:20-07:00","id":1236736,"title":"","content":"I think you just pull a Thulsa Doom, turn into a giant snake, unhinge your jaw, swallow all the cakes, then hibernate as your body slowly digests them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T06:50:40-07:00","id":1236745,"title":"","content":"Notably, Horo the Wise Wolf vomited up the man she had swallowed alive and whole (still alive and whole, as she intended) before shrinking back down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T07:05:04-07:00","id":1236754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236682#post1236682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of like the Alchemical healing Charms where you could hug someone healthy, I'd imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was just one of their medical tricks.<br /> <br /> Also, I would like to think it isn\u2019t too much to hope that Lunar healing might somehow involve the Medicine Ability to the extent that their Strength and Dexterity attack Charms involve a combat Ability, or their Evasion Charms involve the Dodge Ability. They still need Craft to make stuff, and Lore and Occult to make artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T11:25:31-07:00","id":1236843,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m also curious about Lunar craft, medicine, lore, etc. type stuff, but, since people have already asked about that, I\u2019d like to know about the following things:<br /> <br /> You mentioned charms that can switch up your attribute arrangement and Hybrid Body and stuff, but do Lunars have a charm that lets them change how they look without gaining another shape? Like swapping genders or changing your nose shape or your hair color, length, and style? Or is that just a sub function of the charm that lets you swap around your attributes?<br /> <br /> Do Lunars have charms for inflicting mutations on people and, if so, what are the requirements? Can I get someone to swear an oath where, if they break it, they turn into a newt (or whatever)?<br /> <br /> Do Lunars have anything for creating and using fear? Are there charms that interact with dreams? How do their mystic charms work? I\u2019d like to hear more about the Trickster and Shaman aspects of Lunars.<br /> <br /> How does the Bond look? How scary is a Lunar if they\u2019re with their bonded Solar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T11:35:19-07:00","id":1236844,"title":"","content":"Also, is there a sidebar or something that discusses what to do when a Lunar steals someone\u2019s shape and then proceeds to act wildly out of character while in the presence of those who know that person? Because, in previous editions, normal people basically weren\u2019t allowed to question whether that character was who they were pretending to be and that always struck me as weird. It\u2019s like, if I live in the Realm and my best friend suddenly can\u2019t remember me and has a radical personality shift, running for the nearest Immaculate Monk and telling them about the Anathema that ate your buddy should be a legit reaction (even if your buddy is actually suffering from a brain tumor or what have you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T11:37:59-07:00","id":1236845,"title":"","content":"Also, have you found anything that looks screwy or doesn\u2019t seem to play right? You don\u2019t need to tell us what it is, but I would like to hear that any flaws are getting noted and sent back for repairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T12:07:31-07:00","id":1236851,"title":"","content":"Is Lunar character gen pretty similar to Solar character gen or quite different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T12:37:45-07:00","id":1236863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236754#post1236754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was just one of their medical tricks.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it seemed to map well onto one of the Lunars' two past medical tricks from 1e, which formerly just... gave bonus dice to resist infection. Hurrah. Thematically resonant, but mechanically, beyond disappointing. That's an easy enough fix - just beef up the mechanical side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I would like to think it isn\u2019t too much to hope that Lunar healing might somehow involve the Medicine Ability to the extent that their Strength and Dexterity attack Charms involve a combat Ability, or their Evasion Charms involve the Dodge Ability. They still need Craft to make stuff, and Lore and Occult to make artifacts. </div> </div> </div>Also, Ride. There must be some use for it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T13:42:09-07:00","id":1236882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236863#post1236863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And it seemed to map well onto one of the Lunars' two past medical tricks from 1e, which formerly just... gave bonus dice to resist infection. Hurrah. Thematically resonant, but mechanically, beyond disappointing. That's an easy enough fix - just beef up the mechanical side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think that the Alchemical\u2019s nanites\u2019 performance should be at all influenced by the Alchemical\u2019s Craft or Medicine scores?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T14:00:50-07:00","id":1236890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236882#post1236882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that the Alchemical\u2019s nanites\u2019 performance should be at all influenced by the Alchemical\u2019s Craft or Medicine scores?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe there could be room for it, like how Stamina affects the benefits of Solar Ox-Body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T19:09:21-07:00","id":1236978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236688#post1236688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember now... a more cogent form of the concern that I expressed in my first post is getting the whole Charm set in this manner. Or rather, getting any given thing that I would have been a delightful surprise if discovered directly in the book. It does seem unlikely that they'll detail hundreds of Charms, but there's always the possibility that any given one that is described will diminish the experience of seeing it first hand. That and the emergent patterns; those are definitely something that I want to find out for myself.<br /> <br /> I'm going to withdraw from the discussion. That's not a knock on it happening, just a recognition of my own preferences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I respect that choice and know exactly what you're talking about.<br /> <br /> But I have been waiting for amazing Lunars for roughly 17 years, the first several of which I spent vehemently arguing in favor of on one official forum or another, whenever I wasn't attempting to write a new Charmset myself.<br /> <br /> I'm not inclined to wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T08:05:16-07:00","id":1237146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236844#post1236844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is there a sidebar or something that discusses what to do when a Lunar steals someone\u2019s shape and then proceeds to act wildly out of character while in the presence of those who know that person? Because, in previous editions, normal people basically weren\u2019t allowed to question whether that character was who they were pretending to be and that always struck me as weird. It\u2019s like, if I live in the Realm and my best friend suddenly can\u2019t remember me and has a radical personality shift, running for the nearest Immaculate Monk and telling them about the Anathema that ate your buddy should be a legit reaction (even if your buddy is actually suffering from a brain tumor or what have you).</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it would be the same as the Solar Charm Perfect Mirror where: &quot;Characters are not entitled to see through the disguise unless the Solar behaves in a grossly inaccurate way&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T10:55:03-07:00","id":1237199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237146#post1237146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine it would be the same as the Solar Charm Perfect Mirror where: &amp;quot;Characters are not entitled to see through the disguise unless the Solar behaves in a grossly inaccurate way&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Lunar isn\u2019t disguised, and the corebook doesn\u2019t allow you to even attempt to recognize the Lunar\u2019s Tell if you haven\u2019t seen it before.<br /> <br /> Then again, you don\u2019t need a dice roll to believe that someone isn\u2019t who they say they are. The disguise check is more about seeing WHO the imposter is underneath the disguise, or at least confirming that it is a disguise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T11:20:10-07:00","id":1237208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237199#post1237199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the Lunar isn\u2019t disguised, and the corebook doesn\u2019t allow you to even attempt to recognize the Lunar\u2019s Tell if you haven\u2019t seen it before.<br /> <br /> Then again, you don\u2019t need a dice roll to believe that someone isn\u2019t who they say they are. The disguise check is more about seeing WHO the imposter is underneath the disguise, or at least confirming that it is a disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying the lunar is disguised. I'm saying that if a lunar wearing someone's form acted out of character it would probably be similar to the rules for Perfect Mirror. I'm not sure how that was not clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T19:41:41-07:00","id":1237374,"title":"","content":"Spotting a shapeshifted Lunar for something other than what it appears to be is treated as a roll to recognize a disguised character (p. 224), with a flat difficulty of 7. This can\u2019t be attempted unless the observer is already aware of a unique tell or physical give-away that the Lunar possesses in his true human form, which subtly translates in some way into his other shapes.<br /> <br /> Acting out of character when impersonating someone the witness knows would prompt this check as normal, if the witness is capable of making it at all.<br /> <br /> Even a witness who fails to spot the Tell, however, is perfectly capable of believing that the suspicious individual is either actually a Lunar in disguise, or perhaps being controlled by some curse or spirit, or addled by a drug or disease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-20-2018, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T06:30:29-07:00","id":1237472,"title":"","content":"I have a Major Principle of pedantry, and so I must mention that Solar Brawl has Lightning Strikes Twice already. The Lunars didn't steal that trick from Solars, they just doppelgangered it, like they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T09:39:33-07:00","id":1237523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236844#post1236844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is there a sidebar or something that discusses what to do when a Lunar steals someone\u2019s shape and then proceeds to act wildly out of character while in the presence of those who know that person? Because, in previous editions, normal people basically weren\u2019t allowed to question whether that character was who they were pretending to be and that always struck me as weird. It\u2019s like, if I live in the Realm and my best friend suddenly can\u2019t remember me and has a radical personality shift, running for the nearest Immaculate Monk and telling them about the Anathema that ate your buddy should be a legit reaction (even if your buddy is actually suffering from a brain tumor or what have you).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the province of the Orichalcum Rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T13:26:56-07:00","id":1237569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Because, in previous editions, normal people basically weren\u2019t allowed to question whether that character was who they were pretending to be and that always struck me as weird.</i> </div> </div> </div>They weren't? I don't remember anything about specifically. I do remember Changing Moons got a bonus on rolls to be convincing, implying that you're not automatically convincing.<br /> <br /> Tbh, I don't think it really needs specific rules; I think the ST can decide how difficult it is based on the context: if you see someone walking down the street, you're not going to assume it's a Lunar, but if your husband suddenly can't remember your name or those of his children and is acting really weird and making notes about the Realm troops down the street, you probably get to roll to realise he's someone else.<br /> (Which I guess is what Isator is saying)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-21-2018, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T16:45:32-07:00","id":1237616,"title":"","content":"The answer will be in the next episode","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T18:34:04-07:00","id":1237637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237616#post1237616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer will be in the next episode</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a date to expect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T19:52:08-07:00","id":1237669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237637#post1237637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a date to expect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope not; I didn't wash my hair today. &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T20:56:17-07:00","id":1237677,"title":"","content":"Haha! We always release new episodes late Sunday night so that people will have them for their Monday commute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T21:35:36-07:00","id":1237684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237677#post1237677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haha! We always release new episodes late Sunday night so that people will have them for their Monday commute.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what will the podcast be covering monday? How in depth with the charms are you allowed to get?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T05:00:50-07:00","id":1237728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237684#post1237684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what will the podcast be covering monday? How in depth with the charms are you allowed to get?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we are doing an overview of 9 character archetypes (3 each for physical, social, and mental), covering the depth and breadth of the Charms available to you for each archetype (and giving some examples), as well as answering all of the questions that have been asked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T05:59:34-07:00","id":1237738,"title":"","content":"Oh! What's this? 9 character archetypes you say? Not one-role-fits all castes? Interesting! That is a sweet departure from tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T08:05:00-07:00","id":1237758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237738#post1237738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! What's this? 9 character archetypes you say? Not one-role-fits all castes? Interesting! That is a sweet departure from tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>He doesn't appear to be saying that Lunars will have nine new &quot;face&quot; characters in the next book, just that his group will be testing nine characters. Not all of whom will necessarily be in the same...<br /> <br /> Circle? Pack? Are they still calling Lunars in groups &quot;Packs&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T08:40:52-07:00","id":1237766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237758#post1237758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He doesn't appear to be saying that Lunars will have nine new &quot;face&quot; characters in the next book, just that his group will be testing nine characters. Not all of whom will necessarily be in the same...<br /> <br /> Circle? Pack? Are they still calling Lunars in groups &quot;Packs&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Circle. <span style=\"color:white\">10char</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T09:18:22-07:00","id":1237772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237766#post1237766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Circle. <span style=\"color:white\">10char</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t have minded Packs.<br /> <br /> I still think calling meetings \u201cThings\u201d would be unwise, because of how few people would know or believe that was a word for meetings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T17:55:07-07:00","id":1237850,"title":"","content":"For example, I\u2019ll be structuring a discussion about mental attribute Charms around \u201cthe crafter\u201d, \u201cthe sorcerer\u201d, and \u201cthe beast master\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":12730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","user":"PneumaPilot","date":". 07-22-2018, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T18:43:24-07:00","id":1237858,"title":"","content":"Do any of those concepts involve healing?<br /> <br /> I just looked back at Lunar Charms from both previous editions, including Glories: Luna and the Ink Monkeys.<br /> <br /> There's not a single Lunar healing Charm that involves the Medicine Ability. Knowing anything about medical treatment does absolutely nothing to make Lick Wounds, Mother's Touch, Scorpion and Toad Assumption, Burgeoning Wyld Infliction, or Flesh-Sculpting Art more effective.<br /> <br /> The Medicine Ability only ever interacts with Charms like Mystic Butterfly Fraud or Counting the Elephant's Wrinkles when Medicine is the most relevant Ability to the illusion or memory. You can also roll it for Cobra Eye Method's Soporific Nectar technique, unless you want to roll Survival instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lunars always needed attack Abilities for attack and parry values, always needed social Abilities for influence dice pools, always used Resistance at least for resisting poisons and diseases and other effects if not for donning armor. They never got away from needing Craft, Occult, or Lore for their respective activities and especially not for making artifacts.<br /> <br /> Why was Medicine always so incompatible with related Charms? In fact, rendered rather useless by them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-22-2018, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T18:46:31-07:00","id":1237860,"title":"","content":"Good question. I\u2019ll have to look more into that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T19:30:09-07:00","id":1237864,"title":"","content":"The new episode is up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T19:55:30-07:00","id":1237868,"title":"","content":"Enjoying it so far!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T20:44:19-07:00","id":1237876,"title":"","content":"Also, I do pronounce the b in subterfuge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T21:31:52-07:00","id":1237883,"title":"","content":"Undaunted Behemoth Avatar is how Essence 4 Lunars avoid the per-turn costs of Towering Beast Shape. Mountainous Spirit Expression is how you make smaller forms bigger rather than assuming naturally large forms.<br /> <br /> Steel Paw Style makes a triumphant return from the pits of First Edition as the much-anticipated Stamina Charm that lets you parry with Stamina instead of Dexterity, when using medium, heavy, or natural weapons.<br /> <br /> Invulnerable Moonsilver Carapace returns. Effectively a suit of heavy armor, with the usual -2 Mobility, but its soak cannot be reduced below your Stamina. It can also fuse with armor you're already wearing, freeing up motes attuned to it.<br /> <br /> There's a Stamina Charm to increase your soak after you get hit but before damage is rolled.<br /> <br /> A sorcerer can trap sorcerous motes in her anima, allowing her to stop shaping, do something else, and pick it back up again. Another Charm allows your shadow to continue shaping and casting a spell while you do anything else besides attacking.<br /> <br /> A Lunar can cast possessing spirits out into nearby animals, or force spirits to respect her.<br /> <br /> Creation-Spanning Passion allows you and someone else, with mutual Defining Intimacies, dream about each other every night to learn about each other's conditions/situations.<br /> <br /> Lunar crafters can gain crafting points by healing people (yay, I anticipated this), navigating, using a tool you made to contest a fact, or eating another crafter.<br /> <br /> Lunar crafters can enjoy a full free Excellency by including parts of a creature she killed.<br /> <br /> Wits Animal Ken Charms have the &quot;ride or be ridden&quot; Charms. You can share your tattoos with your familiar, and turn them into &quot;an Essence fountain&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T21:36:13-07:00","id":1237885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237883#post1237883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Lunar can cast possessing spirits out into nearby animals, or force spirits to respect her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Jesus was not a take I expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T21:41:38-07:00","id":1237886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237885#post1237885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Jesus was not a take I expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to cherry-pick specific miracles and ignore the vaster power of God, its the Water Aspects who can casually walk across the surface of water so turbulent it threatens to capsize fishing boats.<br /> <br /> For the Lunar Exalted, this trick seems as much about Diana/Artemis as Jesus, since I imagine the Lunar hunts those possessed animals and eats them afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T01:01:10-07:00","id":1237912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237738#post1237738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! What's this? 9 character archetypes you say? Not one-role-fits all castes? Interesting! That is a sweet departure from tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237758#post1237758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He doesn't appear to be saying that Lunars will have nine new &quot;face&quot; characters in the next book, just that his group will be testing nine characters. Not all of whom will necessarily be in the same...<br /> <br /> Circle? Pack? Are they still calling Lunars in groups &quot;Packs&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1237850#post1237850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, I\u2019ll be structuring a discussion about mental attribute Charms around \u201cthe crafter\u201d, \u201cthe sorcerer\u201d, and \u201cthe beast master\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, they are not in the book. They are still cool. They should be in the book. Or <i>a</i> book, at least, at sometime.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also that &quot;Salt&quot; story seed was sweetness. I'ma gonna go read those seeds.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 07-23-2018, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T01:58:55-07:00","id":1237917,"title":"","content":"aeharbo did a nice transcript of the Podcast on Discord, which I quickly compiled <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HoeoobTknddd9Hf2suCMPBXH5v2z_8COljirfxPa9GY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> I'll update this a bit later, but I left editing rights on for peeps with the link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key