:"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T23:02:36-07:00","id":1238142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238130#post1238130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! But what's psychic surgery?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a scam practice where hucksters palm chicken livers so they can pretend to pull &quot;cancers&quot; out of your body without having to cut you open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T23:25:43-07:00","id":1238147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238130#post1238130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! But what's psychic surgery?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LjF1sUZEy2U\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LjF1sUZEy2U\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LjF1sUZEy2U\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LjF1sUZEy2U </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T00:23:55-07:00","id":1238153,"title":"","content":"Question regarding Lunar excellencies. It's been mentioned that the Lunar's have several charms involving swapping attributes (ie. using Str instead of Dex for calculating attack rolls). My questions are thus:<br /> <br /> If you're substituting an attribute for a different attribute via a charm, which attribute does the excellency initially apply too? Example, the Lunar uses a charm to use Str instead of Dex for calculating attack rolls. If the Lunar also uses an excellency to further bolster the roll, does the excellency apply too Dex, or does it now use Str instead? My gut tells me Str, but I thought I'd ask anyways.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T04:18:17-07:00","id":1238170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238153#post1238153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question regarding Lunar excellencies. It's been mentioned that the Lunar's have several charms involving swapping attributes (ie. using Str instead of Dex for calculating attack rolls). My questions are thus:<br /> <br /> If you're substituting an attribute for a different attribute via a charm, which attribute does the excellency initially apply too? Example, the Lunar uses a charm to use Str instead of Dex for calculating attack rolls. If the Lunar also uses an excellency to further bolster the roll, does the excellency apply too Dex, or does it now use Str instead? My gut tells me Str, but I thought I'd ask anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's a good one. And I don't think that is covered in the playtest we received. I'll have to take another look at that section and get back to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T04:23:58-07:00","id":1238172,"title":"","content":"The logical conclusion is &quot;you base it all on the attribute being used&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T04:31:58-07:00","id":1238173,"title":"","content":"Do you still need to stunt to add the 2nd Attribute to the Excellency? And does the stunt have to be appropriate to the 2nd Attribute? I suspect thinking of the umpteenth way of saying &quot;I hit him with my Appearance&quot; or whatever getting old quickly.<br /> <br /> Thanks for doing all this by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4972-hurum","name":"hurum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T04:41:00-07:00","id":1238175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hurum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238173#post1238173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you still need to stunt to add the 2nd Attribute to the Excellency? And does the stunt have to be appropriate to the 2nd Attribute? I suspect thinking of the umpteenth way of saying &amp;quot;I hit him with my Appearance&amp;quot; or whatever getting old quickly.<br /> <br /> Thanks for doing all this by the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that\u2019s still the way it works. I personally think it\u2019s a cool mechanic, and with the crazy ways that battles progress, I don\u2019t think you\u2019d end up doing the same combination on every action, but I can see where there may be some concern - especially since we\u2019re talking about such a big bonus being precluded on these stunts. We\u2019ll have to specifically put this to the test a bunch of times to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T05:13:43-07:00","id":1238182,"title":"","content":"I guess that's a limitation of lunars. Occasionally you might need to switch it up, use a different secondary attribute that you might not have as many dots in.<br /> <br /> Or, y'know, just describe your fights like you're directing Queen's Blade or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T05:32:41-07:00","id":1238185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238172#post1238172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The logical conclusion is &quot;you base it all on the attribute being used&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, that's what my gut is telling me. However, the attribute swap is possible due to a charm you're committing motes to, so I could see it going either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T05:47:22-07:00","id":1238187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238185#post1238185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I said, that's what my gut is telling me. However, the attribute swap is possible due to a charm you're committing motes to, so I could see it going either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Steel Paw Style and its Strength counterpart don\u2019t cost anything to use. Robert Vance himself posted to confirm this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T05:53:27-07:00","id":1238189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238185#post1238185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, that's what my gut is telling me. However, the attribute swap is possible due to a charm you're committing motes to, so I could see it going either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attribute swap charms are permanent and uncosted.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236282#post1236282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236281#post1236281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query: The replace Dex with Strength Melee charm, what is its activation cost and category? (Reflexive, simple etc)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cost: \u2014<br /> Type: Permanent</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 07-24-2018, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T06:29:59-07:00","id":1238200,"title":"","content":"I think the Excellencies will be based on your actual scores, not Charm Swapped scores.<br /> <br /> The swaps probably affect specific dice pools or scores, like replace Dex with Strength for attack pools, or replace Dex with Stamina for your Defense, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T06:57:59-07:00","id":1238208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238187#post1238187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? Steel Paw Style and its Strength counterpart don\u2019t cost anything to use. Robert Vance himself posted to confirm this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, this doesn't change anything though. My question still stands. The fact that at least one other person thinks the excellency will be based off the original attributes, means it's something that needs clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T07:03:28-07:00","id":1238209,"title":"","content":"The thing is... Your cap is based on what builds your roll.<br /> If you change the attribute, the cap accompanies it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T08:10:36-07:00","id":1238231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238209#post1238209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is... Your cap is based on what builds your roll.<br /> If you change the attribute, the cap accompanies it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes this is what I meant.<br /> <br /> If you now attack with Str+Brawl, you get Str Excellency first.<br /> <br /> What I was trying to say I was against is:<br /> <br /> I have the Dex&gt;Str Swap Charm. I am rolling Str+Brawl. I use the Str Exc and Stunt to include Dex. I wont Str+Str(Swapped Dex). I will just do Str+Dex(unswapped)<br /> <br /> Or if I am rolling Dex+Larceny to pick a lock. If I use the Exc, it will be a unswapped Dex Excellency, not a Str Excellency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T08:30:26-07:00","id":1238235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238209#post1238209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is... Your cap is based on what builds your roll.<br /> If you change the attribute, the cap accompanies it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s interesting. Do you have a page reference for that?<br /> <br /> So if a Solar uses Blinding Battle Feint to roll Dex+Stealth instead of Wits+Awareness for Join Battle, that character couldn\u2019t then use a Stealth Excellency to boost it to the new max from the changed roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T08:57:14-07:00","id":1238247,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m wondering if Steel Paw Style lets you use your Stamina Excellency to improve your Parry Value when you are in an animal form.<br /> <br /> If it does, how?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T09:49:19-07:00","id":1238257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238247#post1238247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m wondering if Steel Paw Style lets you use your Stamina Excellency to improve your Parry Value when you are in an animal form.<br /> <br /> If it does, how?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another good question. My own head-canon would be either use your normal parry (with the substitution) or the animals listed parry, whichever is greater. In essence, animal forms wouldn't benefit from the charm because of how animals are designed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T09:50:23-07:00","id":1238258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238235#post1238235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s interesting. Do you have a page reference for that?<br /> <br /> So if a Solar uses Blinding Battle Feint to roll Dex+Stealth instead of Wits+Awareness for Join Battle, that character couldn\u2019t then use a Stealth Excellency to boost it to the new max from the changed roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's two different pieces of evidence as to why you would absolutely have to use Dex + Stealth excellency to enhance the roll you specify. <br /> <br /> First, on page 251 there's the blurb about charm dice cap that says &quot;Many Charms raise a character\u2019s dice pool or static values. The magic of the Solar Exalted cannot add more dice to a roll than the relevant (Attribute + Ability) total a\ufb00ected by the Charms. For example, a Solar with Dexterity 4, Melee 3 could not add more than seven dice to a Melee attack roll, while a Solar with Dexterity 5, Melee 5 could add up to 10 dice. &quot;<br /> <br /> Second, the basic incompatibility of excellencies from one ability to another. in the description of both supplemental and reflexive charms states that they can't be used to enhance actionas from outside their abilities. And in the breakdown of what an excellency is, it states that &quot;if the Excellency is being used to enhance a dice roll it is considered supplemental. If it is being used in a defense it is considered re\ufb02exive&quot; <br /> <br /> Therefore an excellency can only be used to enhance an action where it's ability has been rolled. IE if you sub in Dex+stealth for join battle, your dice cap is Dex + Stealth. It simply doesn't matter what it would normally be because you're not making a wits+awareness roll.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T20:27:42-07:00","id":1238491,"title":"","content":"One question regarding the embiggening line of charms - is there any restriction on the forms that can use them? One problem with Emperor Ox was it was limited to your spirit shape, and even the Ink Monkey charms to permit the use of DBT (and then the &quot;in dbt, but human&quot; knack) were really hacky. With the current approach favoring DBT as an option instead of a necessity, am I right in presuming there isn't a limit beyond the mote tax?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T10:35:20-07:00","id":1238621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238491#post1238491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question regarding the embiggening line of charms - is there any restriction on the forms that can use them? One problem with Emperor Ox was it was limited to your spirit shape, and even the Ink Monkey charms to permit the use of DBT (and then the &quot;in dbt, but human&quot; knack) were really hacky. With the current approach favoring DBT as an option instead of a necessity, am I right in presuming there isn't a limit beyond the mote tax?</div> </div> </div> </div>They told us: Towering Beast Form for pre-big shapes, Mountainous Spirit Expression to make anything else bigger.<br /> <br /> But tiny forms like mice seem to only get as big as people. Maybe you need a custom reinvention of Titan Mouse Menagerie to become Bugzilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T10:58:12-07:00","id":1238627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238621#post1238621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They told us: Towering Beast Form for pre-big shapes, Mountainous Spirit Expression to make anything else bigger.<br /> <br /> But tiny forms like mice seem to only get as big as people. Maybe you need a custom reinvention of Titan Mouse Menagerie to become Bugzilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>This came across a little unclearly in the podcast\u2014you can take cat or grasshopper-sized things and boost them up to Legendary Size with Mountainous Spirit Expression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T10:59:31-07:00","id":1238628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238247#post1238247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m wondering if Steel Paw Style lets you use your Stamina Excellency to improve your Parry Value when you are in an animal form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it does, how? </div> </div> </div>Same way it does in human form. Your dice caps don't change when you shapeshift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T11:03:47-07:00","id":1238629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238235#post1238235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s interesting. Do you have a page reference for that?<br /> <br /> So if a Solar uses Blinding Battle Feint to roll Dex+Stealth instead of Wits+Awareness for Join Battle, that character couldn\u2019t then use a Stealth Excellency to boost it to the new max from the changed roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no Join Battle Excellency.<br /> <br /> There is (Ability) Excellency. If you're rolling Steatlh for Join Battle and want to use an Excellency, then it will be the Stealth Excellency.<br /> <br /> Your dicepool combination for the action will determine your dice cap and which Excellency you will use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T11:04:26-07:00","id":1238630,"title":"","content":"Something else I'm curious about, how do the charms that create beastmen work? The dev's mentioned something about a rite and or trial the mortals must pass. I'm curious about the mechanics of this &quot;trial/rite&quot;. I'd also like to know if the Lunar are required to mirror the beastmen to their totem. Or could a bear totem Lunar preparing for a war in the West, create shark beastmen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T12:48:29-07:00","id":1238664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238629#post1238629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no Join Battle Excellency.<br /> <br /> There is (Ability) Excellency. If you're rolling Steatlh for Join Battle and want to use an Excellency, then it will be the Stealth Excellency.<br /> <br /> Your dicepool combination for the action will determine your dice cap and which Excellency you will use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! Good to know! I thought it should work this way, but then that previous post got me worried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T13:01:37-07:00","id":1238670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238627#post1238627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This came across a little unclearly in the podcast\u2014you can take cat or grasshopper-sized things and boost them up to Legendary Size with Mountainous Spirit Expression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Robert, sorry if I interpreted this incorrectly. At the end of the charm it said a tiny or miniscule size the effects are suppressed. I took that as meaning they don't get the full size. Could you explain what is meant by &quot;effects are suppressed&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT... I see ... the effects of Tiny and Minuscule are suppressed... my bad<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24236-reformedninja","user":"ReformedNinja","date":". 07-25-2018, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24236-reformedninja","name":"ReformedNinja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T13:08:40-07:00","id":1238671,"title":"","content":"Do you guys plan to share that Archery Martial Arts someone came up with? I've been wanting to make my own but lazy about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T15:23:01-07:00","id":1238704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238671#post1238671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you guys plan to share that Archery Martial Arts someone came up with? I've been wanting to make my own but lazy about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first three Charms are up on Fivepoles.com. We\u2019ll be adding more by and by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T19:18:03-07:00","id":1238752,"title":"","content":"If you have Dexterity 5, is there any point in learning Steel Paw Style or the Strength/attack version? (What's the Strength version called, anyway?*)<br /> <br /> Is there an Intelligence version that substitutes for any other Attribute on a crafting roll, and a Perception version that substitutes for Wits on Join Battle rolls?<br /> <br /> Is the Charm that lets you use Strength for rushing and resisting disengages (and, I assume, disengaging and resisting rushes) another Permanent Charm that substitutes for Dexterity, or an activated effect that boosts movement actions with your Strength in some way?<br /> <br /> <br /> *There are various options. First Edition has Steel Paw Style's original twin, Body Weapon Technique, but Tyrant Lizard Strike is probably more appropriate, or Horrifying Might, or Tiger Claw Swat.<br /> <br /> <br /> We've been told that Strength and Dexterity are going to feature Simple-type Charms for attacks to prevent over-combination, and I imagine Robert took advantage of that to make some exclusive to one or two of the four attack Abilities.<br /> <br /> A Melee-exclusive attack Charm could be Dance of the Living Blade, Ferocious Biting Sword, Spinning Blade Attack, and Lightning Sword Method.<br /> <br /> For Archery and/or Thrown, there's Skillful Ricochet Attack, Two-Target Method, Knowing the Arrow's Path, Riding the Secret Wind, Body-Pinning Style, Deadly Assassin's Shot, Silver Waterfall Technique, Rain of Feathered Doom, Finding the Needle's Eye, Arrow-Breaking Shot... it sounds like there's already Wind-Wings Carry Technique and Arrow-Shaping Method.<br /> <br /> For Brawl (and Martial Arts?) grappling, there's Bear Embrace Method, Mighty Bear Crush, Spine-Breaking Technique, Throat-Baring Hold, Roused Bear Throw, Jaws of the River Dragon, and Flesh-Tearing Entanglement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T19:53:02-07:00","id":1238761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238752#post1238752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have Dexterity 5, is there any point in learning Steel Paw Style or the Strength/attack version? (What's the Strength version called, anyway?*)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. They're meant to encourage high-Stamina/Strength, lower-Dexterity builds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there an Intelligence version that substitutes for any other Attribute on a crafting roll </div> </div> </div>No, but the Intelligence crafting Charms are Attribute-agnostic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and a Perception version that substitutes for Wits on Join Battle rolls? </div> </div> </div>Yep! And a whole tree that comes out of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is the Charm that lets you use Strength for rushing and resisting disengages (and, I assume, disengaging and resisting rushes) another Permanent Charm that substitutes for Dexterity, or an activated effect that boosts movement actions with your Strength in some way? </div> </div> </div>It's permanent, but has a little bonus effect that you can spend motes to use. Movement rolls are less all-pervasive than attack rolls and Defense, so it gets a bit more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T20:30:35-07:00","id":1238771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238761#post1238761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. They're meant to encourage high-Stamina/Strength, lower-Dexterity builds.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the unlikely event that someone bought those and then somehow maxed-out Dexterity, I suppose a storyteller could just refund the substitutors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, but the Intelligence crafting Charms are Attribute-agnostic. </div> </div> </div>Okay. Crafters better make sure to get the Dexterity Excellency, then, and possibly the Strength Excellency for metal-working.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yep! And a whole tree that comes out of it. </div> </div> </div>That's cool, but what does that mean for a Lunar who favors and invests in Wits instead of Perception?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's permanent, but has a little bonus effect that you can spend motes to use. Movement rolls are less all-pervasive than attack rolls and Defense, so it gets a bit more. </div> </div> </div>So it's something that someone double-dipping in Strength and Dexterity for maximum, Sonic the Hedgehog mobility would want to buy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-25-2018, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T21:07:22-07:00","id":1238777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238771#post1238771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's cool, but what does that mean for a Lunar who favors and invests in Wits instead of Perception?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means that they don't get supreme advantages for favoring and investing in a god stat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T22:20:08-07:00","id":1238790,"title":"","content":"I'm all for more options between players that don't delve into picking weapons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I remember you talking about a Perception Charm that lets you use Perception+Awareness to roll for Join Battle. A whole tree for that definitely sounds fitting for a Sniper Lunar I plan to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T22:56:31-07:00","id":1238801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238627#post1238627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This came across a little unclearly in the podcast\u2014you can take cat or grasshopper-sized things and boost them up to Legendary Size with Mountainous Spirit Expression.</div> </div> </div> </div>More specifically, I'd like to be able to get my Attack on Titan in a humanoid form (be it human, DBT, whatev), even if it is Advanced Shenanigans in the charmset or has a heavy mote tax. Or mimic a Macross scene with a Lunar skald making use of the natural amplification afforded by being the size of a goddamn house, that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T05:47:13-07:00","id":1238881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1238671#post1238671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you guys plan to share that Archery Martial Arts someone came up with? I've been wanting to make my own but lazy about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://fivepoles.com/category/martial-arts/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://fivepoles.com/category/martial-arts/\" target=\"_blank\"> fivepoles.com&nbsp;-&nbsp;fivepoles Resources and Information. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://fivepoles.com/category/martial-arts/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://fivepoles.com/category/martial-arts/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> fivepoles.com is your first and best source for all of the information you&rsquo;re looking for. From general topics to more of what you would expect to find here, fivepoles.com has it all. We hope you find what you are searching for! </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That is the direct link to all 4 of the new Martial Arts Charms we've submitted. Enjoy! Oh, and let us know how it goes using it at the table. We'd love to hear about it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T10:01:31-07:00","id":1238969,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I appreciate that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T11:56:21-07:00","id":1239011,"title":"","content":"So the swarm charms sound really cool what with creating a number of duplicates of yourself.<br /> <br /> But the set number of duplicates makes me wonder, will we also be able to do the whole &quot;turn into a cloud of locusts (or such)&quot; thing that was basically the extent of swarm stuff in 2nd edition?<br /> <br /> Also, am I understanding it correctly that Mountainous Spirit Expression will work with human or Hybrid Body shapes this edition? Before (in 2e), only animal shapes could grow huge, so this would be a very cool change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Let us take men and give them the favor of the gods and use them as our champions against the Primordials, that we might overthrow them and play for ourselves the Games of Divinity.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2272-senresk","name":"senresk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T12:02:08-07:00","id":1239012,"title":"","content":"I'm also interested in how the Swarm charms works. You make Essence+1 copies of yourself? But do they get their own actions or are you still limited to one per turn. How do you work with regards to charm use and essence? Everyone and their mom has made a version of this charm in the past, but I'm interested in how Lunars actually dance around this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T12:13:39-07:00","id":1239015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>senresk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239011#post1239011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the swarm charms sound really cool what with creating a number of duplicates of yourself.<br /> <br /> But the set number of duplicates makes me wonder, will we also be able to do the whole &quot;turn into a cloud of locusts (or such)&quot; thing that was basically the extent of swarm stuff in 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Transforming into a swarm is a Charm building off the &quot;create duplicates of yourself&quot; Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, am I understanding it correctly that Mountainous Spirit Expression will work with human or Hybrid Body shapes this edition? Before (in 2e), only animal shapes could grow huge, so this would be a very cool change. </div> </div> </div>Correct. If you can turn into it, you can turn it into a daikaiju.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T12:21:02-07:00","id":1239018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239015#post1239015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transforming into a swarm is a Charm building off the &quot;create duplicates of yourself&quot; Charm.<br /> <br /> Correct. If you can turn into it, you can turn it into a daikaiju.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds great! Thanks for the quick answer!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Let us take men and give them the favor of the gods and use them as our champions against the Primordials, that we might overthrow them and play for ourselves the Games of Divinity.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2272-senresk","name":"senresk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T12:42:13-07:00","id":1239024,"title":"","content":"No-one seems to have posted it, so here's a transcript of some of the things from the podcast:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HoeoobTknddd9Hf2suCMPBXH5v2z_8COljirfxPa9GY/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HoeoobTknddd9Hf2suCMPBXH5v2z_8COljirfxPa9GY/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HoeoobTknddd9Hf2suCMPBXH5v2z_8COljirfxPa9GY/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HoeoobTknddd9Hf2suCMPBXH5v2z_8COljirfxPa9GY/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T12:44:26-07:00","id":1239025,"title":"","content":"Can I just say, I like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Caste and Favored Excellencies are free at Attribute 3+, other are free at Attribute 4+ or 2 Charms bought</span></span> </div> </div> </div>It might discourage people from building Lunars in a way that's silly but optimal at character gen; ie favour an attribute at 1 so you can buy it later for cheap, and put your points into non-favoured attributes.<br /> People will want to have their Caste and Favoured attributes at 3 as soon as possible, so probably at character gen.<br /> <br /> Also, the fact you get it for free at 4 points with most attributes, plus the fact that the cap for pumping your static values is generally the same at 4 or 5 (because it's +2 Parry, Resolve or whatever for both, without stunts), means people will be encouraged to get attributes to 4, but not massively encouraged to get them to 5.<br /> <br /> Hopefully that'll lead to people playing characters that don't have so many 5s, but spread it out a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-26-2018, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T15:07:12-07:00","id":1239054,"title":"","content":"The one Charm that lets you craft mundane clothes which can mutate the user, lets you make a robe of feathers that becomes a pair of wings. A helmet that grants Enhance Sight.<br /> <br /> The Charm to change your scent, just going by the concept alone, seems to be for proactively thwarting Investigation case-scene rolls by people with sharp senses of smell. Also, Survival-based tracking rolls relying on the sense of smell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T19:09:23-07:00","id":1239151,"title":"","content":"So, someone, I think, mentioned Lunars being able to do the Dragonheart &quot;dragonslayer&quot; scam at one point, where the hero &quot;rescues&quot; a village from a &quot;dragon&quot; when both are in on it, mentioning a Lunar could do both sides of it.<br /> <br /> Does the clone tree basically end up with upgrades that give the clones access to the Lunar's full shapeshifting options? So Clone 1 becomes giant hybrid animal monster who is &quot;driven off&quot; by the Lunar (or killed, possibly, if there's not particularly problematic backlash to the Lunar for doing so)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T20:37:25-07:00","id":1239175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OpMegs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239151#post1239151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, someone, I think, mentioned Lunars being able to do the Dragonheart &quot;dragonslayer&quot; scam at one point, where the hero &quot;rescues&quot; a village from a &quot;dragon&quot; when both are in on it, mentioning a Lunar could do both sides of it.<br /> <br /> Does the clone tree basically end up with upgrades that give the clones access to the Lunar's full shapeshifting options? So Clone 1 becomes giant hybrid animal monster who is &quot;driven off&quot; by the Lunar (or killed, possibly, if there's not particularly problematic backlash to the Lunar for doing so)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone mentioned on the podcast that upgrade charms let you make a clone in a different form. I'm assuming there are restrictions on this, because being able to spawn a battlegroup of Yeddim instantly seems like a potential problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T21:02:09-07:00","id":1239185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239175#post1239175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Someone mentioned on the podcast that upgrade charms let you make a clone in a different form. I'm assuming there are restrictions on this, because being able to spawn a battlegroup of Yeddim instantly seems like a potential problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a reasonable restriction might include not being able to do that with Legendary Size shapes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T21:05:21-07:00","id":1239186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239185#post1239185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps a reasonable restriction might include not being able to do that with Legendary Size shapes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think Aurochs have that rule, and a stampede of war cows is still...shocking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T00:47:50-07:00","id":1239219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239186#post1239186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think Aurochs have that rule, and a stampede of war cows is still...shocking.</div> </div> </div> </div>The swarm charms limit the number of clones to that of your Essence rating. So even an E5 Lunar could only manage a stampede of 6 Aurochs including himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T00:51:22-07:00","id":1239220,"title":"","content":"I thought they said essence + 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T02:56:56-07:00","id":1239233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239220#post1239220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought they said essence + 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T04:02:01-07:00","id":1239249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239233#post1239233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, must have misheard your example. Definitely possible since I listen just before I go to bed. Still, 10 Aurochs at E5 is still a pretty limited stampede. Now 10 mammoths will definitely have an impact!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T06:17:31-07:00","id":1239271,"title":"","content":"That's the default charm. They didn't tell us what the other two charms did. Might be as simple as creating a Battle Group for one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T08:37:18-07:00","id":1239320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239271#post1239271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the default charm. They didn't tell us what the other two charms did. Might be as simple as creating a Battle Group for one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it's possible, but unlikely. Corey specifically mentioned the max number of clones a Lunar could make. It wouldn't make much sense to mention the max number, when another charm would provide a greater number.<br /> <br /> On a side note, 10 Aurochs would constitute a size 1 battlegroup anyways. So if you just want a battlegroup, it's possible already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T18:43:14-07:00","id":1239518,"title":"","content":"Another question; what are the attribute requirements like? I remember that people complained in 2e that most Lunar charms needed 4 or 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T19:30:52-07:00","id":1239532,"title":"","content":"If you were to use a hybrid form to give yourself a soak-improving thick hide, would the increased soak from DBT stack with that? How does armor interact with these kinds of transformation charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T22:34:14-07:00","id":1239907,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, I'm a bit bothered by Lunar's having sorcery-enhancing charms. While it's true Lunar's can't access Solar Circle Sorcery, it means that Lunar's are better then Solar's at Terrestrial and Celestial Sorcery. Solar's are stated repeatedly to be the masters of sorcery in general, not just the masters of Solar Circle Sorcery. In the end, as a ST, I only have 2 options. Either invalidate both the Lunar Sorcery Charms, or create a few for Solar's!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T22:38:13-07:00","id":1239908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239907#post1239907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, I'm a bit bothered by Lunar's having sorcery-enhancing charms. While it's true Lunar's can't access Solar Circle Sorcery, it means that Lunar's are better then Solar's at Terrestrial and Celestial Sorcery. Solar's are stated repeatedly to be the masters of sorcery in general, not just the masters of Solar Circle Sorcery. In the end, as a ST, I only have 2 options. Either invalidate both the Lunar Sorcery Charms, or create a few for Solar's!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A few not keyed to familiars I assume or math? Cuz we have those...(Also, Solars can go straight to sorcery, Lunars I believe need to spend charms to get there?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T00:45:55-07:00","id":1239928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239907#post1239907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, I'm a bit bothered by Lunar's having sorcery-enhancing charms. While it's true Lunar's can't access Solar Circle Sorcery, it means that Lunar's are better then Solar's at Terrestrial and Celestial Sorcery. Solar's are stated repeatedly to be the masters of sorcery in general, not just the masters of Solar Circle Sorcery. In the end, as a ST, I only have 2 options. Either invalidate both the Lunar Sorcery Charms, or create a few for Solar's!</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars are better, because they have better dice pools thanks to their larger dice cap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T01:11:07-07:00","id":1239930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239908#post1239908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A few not keyed to familiars I assume or math? Cuz we have those...(Also, Solars can go straight to sorcery, Lunars I believe need to spend charms to get there?)</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the one keyed to familiars?<br /> I assume by math you're referring to the Miracles sorcery dice-trick charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I'm going to say something that I don't think people will like...<br /> I don't think those two Lunar sorcery charms sound all that useful. Certainly less than the DB ones (but of course, the DB ones are balanced to only be used for Terrestrial spells; they'd be way more powerful when used with Celestial or Solar spells). <br /> I don't think Solars are seriously being let down by not having them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T02:00:47-07:00","id":1239944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239928#post1239928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are better, because they have better dice pools thanks to their larger dice cap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attribute + Ability isn't a higher cap than Attribute + Attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T02:58:44-07:00","id":1239958,"title":"","content":"I don't expect every action ever to be stunted. This is not, in my experience, how games actually work.<br /> <br /> In addition, I see spell-casting stunted a lot less than attacks, and never after the first round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-29-2018, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T03:12:35-07:00","id":1239963,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but if that was required to use your full excellency you'd probably see it a lot more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T03:48:19-07:00","id":1239969,"title":"","content":"I don't consider that a good thing.<br /> <br /> But, you are correct that it'd be more common. I don't think it'd be on all rolls though, because players won't always be able to think of one; nor do I think the Devs intend it to be, otherwise the excellency wouldn't require a stunt at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T06:13:59-07:00","id":1240004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239958#post1239958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't expect every action ever to be stunted. This is not, in my experience, how games actually work.<br /> <br /> In addition, I see spell-casting stunted a lot less than attacks, and never after the first round.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tell my players, \u201cAssume you automatically get to add two dice for a Stunt, unless you consciously chose to phone it in. If you do phone it in, I\u2019ll subtract your automatic two dice. If you wow us, I\u2019ll give you the extra successes of a 2 or 3 point Stunt.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:00:05-07:00","id":1240019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239958#post1239958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't expect every action ever to be stunted. This is not, in my experience, how games actually work.<br /> <br /> In addition, I see spell-casting stunted a lot less than attacks, and never after the first round.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to echo PneumaPilot, and add words from the corebook (pg- 187) itself:<br /> <br /> Stunts may be used as often as desired\u2014<b>and to be clear, the average player can and should use a stunt to enhance almost every action her character takes. Storytellers are encouraged to err in the player\u2019s favor when deciding what is or isn\u2019t a stunt.</b><br /> <br /> The devs have even been quoted saying &quot;stunt everything&quot; on more then one occasion. I've worked with my players, two of them are new to Exalted, and they know I feel they should stunt every action. They're not required to, but simply describing an action with a bit of flare is a small price to pay for 2 bonus dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 07-29-2018, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:05:54-07:00","id":1240021,"title":"","content":"With lunars I can see it being a little harder to get their cap up, because they don't <i>just </i>need to stunt. They need to stunt in a way that incorporates the other attribute.<br /> <br /> Like, stunting a strength based action with a description of how you're really swole will get you two dice, but not let you add any more from charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:12:45-07:00","id":1240027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239907#post1239907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, I'm a bit bothered by Lunar's having sorcery-enhancing charms. While it's true Lunar's can't access Solar Circle Sorcery, it means that Lunar's are better then Solar's at Terrestrial and Celestial Sorcery. Solar's are stated repeatedly to be the masters of sorcery in general, not just the masters of Solar Circle Sorcery. In the end, as a ST, I only have 2 options. Either invalidate both the Lunar Sorcery Charms, or create a few for Solar's!</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars can learn Terrestrial Circle Sorcery right away, and Celestial Circle Sorcery right after that. They can also favor the cost of buying those initiations and every possible spell.<br /> <br /> At present, it seems that Lunars will need to learn at least two Charms before they initiate into Celestial (or possibly even Terrestrial) sorcery, and that they will not be able to favor the costs.<br /> <br /> This is on top of the Lunar inability to acquire a third sorcerous shaping ritual, as Solar Exalted can.<br /> <br /> It's because Dragon-Blooded can only learn one shaping ritual that they were given Dragon-Sorceror Puissance. It's probably because they don't have the Twilight anima power that they get Five Winds Raiment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:13:08-07:00","id":1240028,"title":"","content":"Swole and Pretty, that's what you're going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:15:21-07:00","id":1240030,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Swole and Pretty, how well can a Lunar play at being Flex Mentallo, Hero of the Beach?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:20:25-07:00","id":1240032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240027#post1240027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars can learn Terrestrial Circle Sorcery right away, and Celestial Circle Sorcery right after that. They can also favor the cost of buying those initiations and every possible spell.<br /> <br /> At present, it seems that Lunars will need to learn at least two Charms before they initiate into Celestial (or possibly even Terrestrial) sorcery, and that they will not be able to favor the costs.<br /> <br /> This is on top of the Lunar inability to acquire a third sorcerous shaping ritual, as Solar Exalted can.<br /> <br /> It's because Dragon-Blooded can only learn one shaping ritual that they were given Dragon-Sorceror Puissance. It's probably because they don't have the Twilight anima power that they get Five Winds Raiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like it changes anything. Solars can't supernal celestial sorcery so they'll need to spend it on spells or charms in between circles.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T08:01:55-07:00","id":1240054,"title":"","content":"AFAIK it's not like sorcery enhancing spells are outside the solar wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> It's just that nobody wrote any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T08:57:50-07:00","id":1240068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240027#post1240027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars can learn Terrestrial Circle Sorcery right away, and Celestial Circle Sorcery right after that. They can also favor the cost of buying those initiations and every possible spell.<br /> <br /> At present, it seems that Lunars will need to learn at least two Charms before they initiate into Celestial (or possibly even Terrestrial) sorcery, and that they will not be able to favor the costs.<br /> <br /> This is on top of the Lunar inability to acquire a third sorcerous shaping ritual, as Solar Exalted can.<br /> <br /> It's because Dragon-Blooded can only learn one shaping ritual that they were given Dragon-Sorceror Puissance. It's probably because they don't have the Twilight anima power that they get Five Winds Raiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing you said alters the situation at all. Lunar's dedicated to sorcery still out-perform Solar's dedicated to sorcery in the first 2 circles. So I'm still in a situation of creating sorcery charms for Solars, or invalidating those of Lunars. Normally I don't mind creating charms, but those are usually unique to specific individuals. Creating charms that will be accessible by all Solars, across all of my games, is a bit more daunting. My initial thoughts on the Lunar and Solar sorcery charms are as follows:<br /> <br /> 1) The first sorcery-enhancing charm Lunar's have allows them to capture/store sorcerous motes in their animas. This actually sounds like a charm that I might convert for all exalts. Tailor it's capability down a bit for Dragonbloods, and up a bit for Solars. It would give all exalts a bit more versatility in sorcery.<br /> <br /> 2) The second charm allows the Lunar's shadow to perform a shaping-sorcery action, freeing the Lunar to do other things except an attack action. This charm does feel very Lunar-y to me. So I'd like to leave this one unique to Lunars.<br /> <br /> 3) Coming up with a Solar sorcery charm isn't something I've had time to really consider yet. I've been busy with other things. My initial thoughts are a charm that enhances a Solar's ability to counter-spell other sorcerers. A charm that allows the Solar to treat all spells as known for the purposes of the counter-spell action, and possibly provides additional benefits if the Solar actually does know the spell he's countering. Like I said though, this is my initial thought, without having had the time to actually give it a lot of thought. I'll probably start another thread when I'm ready to fully workout Solar sorcery charms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T08:59:42-07:00","id":1240069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240068#post1240068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing you said alters the situation at all. Lunar's dedicated to sorcery still out-perform Solar's dedicated to sorcery in the first 2 circles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, because the Solar has more spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:03:25-07:00","id":1240072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240069#post1240069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, because the Solar has more spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>More spells doesn't equal better casting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:09:08-07:00","id":1240075,"title":"","content":"True, but I don't feel it's fair to say that a Lunar with 8 spells and 2 sorcery-buffing charms (96xp) out-performs a Solar with 11 spells and 1 sorcery-buffing charm (96xp) at sorcery overall.<br /> (This doesn't count any other prerequisite charms Lunars will need to get Sorcery, but I don't expect them to be particularly onerous.)<br /> <br /> (Plus, in a straight roll to cast, neither of the Lunar charms actually helps you get more successes, unlike the Solar one. I don't think the Solar one is worth using for casting though, too pricey).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-29-2018, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:27:10-07:00","id":1240086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239930#post1239930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the one keyed to familiars?<br /> I assume by math you're referring to the Miracles sorcery dice-trick charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I'm going to say something that I don't think people will like...<br /> I don't think those two Lunar sorcery charms sound all that useful. Certainly less than the DB ones (but of course, the DB ones are balanced to only be used for Terrestrial spells; they'd be way more powerful when used with Celestial or Solar spells).<br /> I don't think Solars are seriously being let down by not having them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah, Math is refering to the Lore Charm that boosts sorcery. In Miracles there's the occult charm where you can pay for spirits to manifest, and I think something else. And then there's the one where you get a dice trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:30:06-07:00","id":1240091,"title":"","content":"Hm...I wonder. If your shadow is casting a spell, can you cast another one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:34:07-07:00","id":1240094,"title":"","content":"If I can only Cantana or Empty Voices your army but you can Death Ray or Rain of Doom mine, how am I better at sorcery?<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded don\u2019t get Dragon-Sorceror Puissance until Essence 3, at which point Celestial Exalted can achieve Celestial Circle Spells, and having an easier time casting Flight of the Brilliant Raptor doesn\u2019t make a Dragon-Blood a better sorcerer than someone who can cast Cantana or summon Octavian.<br /> <br /> Therefore, it stands to reason that Lunars can\u2019t get these awesome sorcery-buffing Charms until Essence 5, when Solar sorcerers are throwing around Total Annihilations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-29-2018, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:37:40-07:00","id":1240098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240091#post1240091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm...I wonder. If your shadow is casting a spell, can you cast another one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since you can\u2019t attack while it does, and you can\u2019t make two shaping actions at a time, I doubt it.<br /> <br /> The point seems to be that you can have your shadow cast the spell while you rise from prone, disengage, rush, Full Defense, Defend Other, Ready a weapon, or shapeshift into a different form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:42:56-07:00","id":1240103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240086#post1240086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nah, Math is refering to the Lore Charm that boosts sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, I remember that. Maths is the true path to power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:52:12-07:00","id":1240106,"title":"","content":"Anyway, I'm still looking forward to the playtesters exploring the usefulness of activating Towering Beast Form for one instant and NOT paying the immediate cost to remain in the form.<br /> <br /> I want to know how the transformation may interact with a feat of strength to lift something. If you have a Charm that allows you to flurry a shapeshifting action with an attack action in the same turn, will Towering Beast Form / Mountainous Spirit Expression's momentary transformation enable to you life and then THROW a massive object at your enemies?<br /> <br /> Currently, there are no Heavy-weight Thrown weapons. Do the playtest documents speak at all about using massive rocks and fallen trees as Heavy improvised Thrown weapons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T10:06:56-07:00","id":1240109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240094#post1240094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I can only Cantana or Empty Voices your army but you can Death Ray or Rain of Doom mine, how am I better at sorcery?<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded don\u2019t get Dragon-Sorceror Puissance until Essence 3, at which point Celestial Exalted can achieve Celestial Circle Spells, and having an easier time casting Flight of the Brilliant Raptor doesn\u2019t make a Dragon-Blood a better sorcerer than someone who can cast Cantana or summon Octavian.<br /> <br /> Therefore, it stands to reason that Lunars can\u2019t get these awesome sorcery-buffing Charms until Essence 5, when Solar sorcerers are throwing around Total Annihilations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why you're bringing up Dragon-Sorcerer Puissance, unless you are inferring Lunar sorcery charms are locked behind Essence 5 (when Solar's get Solar Sorcery)? Is that what you're hoping for? Also, I have yet to find in any of the published material that states &quot;Solar's are the masters of sorcery once they reach Essence 5 or get access to Solar Circle Sorcery&quot;. All I'm finding is repeated statements like &quot;Solar's are masters of sorcery,&quot; &quot;Solar's are undisputed masters of sorcery&quot;, &quot;Solar's are unmatched in sorcery&quot;. I'll keep looking though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T10:35:49-07:00","id":1240122,"title":"","content":"Sounds like Solar propaganda to me. They're probably using Linguistics charms on you. Solars do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T10:48:37-07:00","id":1240132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240122#post1240122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like Solar propaganda to me. They're probably using Linguistics charms on you. Solars do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>LoL, thanks for that! Gave me a good laugh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T11:42:58-07:00","id":1240156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240109#post1240109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure why you're bringing up Dragon-Sorcerer Puissance, unless you are inferring Lunar sorcery charms are locked behind Essence 5 (when Solar's get Solar Sorcery)? Is that what you're hoping for? Also, I have yet to find in any of the published material that states &quot;Solar's are the masters of sorcery once they reach Essence 5 or get access to Solar Circle Sorcery&quot;. All I'm finding is repeated statements like &quot;Solar's are masters of sorcery,&quot; &quot;Solar's are undisputed masters of sorcery&quot;, &quot;Solar's are unmatched in sorcery&quot;. I'll keep looking though.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you aren\u2019t saying that Charms like Dragon-Sorceror Puissance are the reason you find that Solar supremacy at sorcery is being threatened, then what are you complaining about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T18:21:16-07:00","id":1240270,"title":"","content":"Still waiting for an answer.<br /> <br /> Solars and Dragon-Blooded get to favor the cost of buying Occult dots, sorcerous initiation Charms, and Spells.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded need four prerequisite Occult Charms before they can buy the only sorcerous initiation Charm available to them: Terrestrial Circle Sorcery. They can only learn one shaping ritual.<br /> <br /> A Solar can learn Terrestrial Circle Sorcery immediately, with no prerequisites. When an Essence 3 Dragon-Blood is trying to squeeze as much power as possible out of Terrestrial Circle Spells, the Solar is casting magic on an entirely different scale with Celestial Circle Sorcery, and fueling those spells with a second shaping ritual. When a Solar reaches Essence 5, the Dragon-Blood has absolutely nothing which can compare to Solar Circle Sorcery fueled by three shaping rituals.<br /> <br /> There might not be a Solar Charm exactly like Five Winds Raiment, but Twilight Caste Solars have something similar as an anima power. Solars can also use Spirit-Draining Mandala to fuel shaping costs, and Lore's Heaven-Turning Calculations to boost the effects of spells.<br /> <br /> If the Lunar Exalted work like the Dragon-Blooded (save for being incapable of favoring Sorcery Initiations or Spell purchase costs), but on a higher level, then when they're Essence 5 and trying to squeeze as much utility out Terrestrial and Celestial Circle Spells as possible, the Solar Exalted are changing the face of the world within a matter of hours using Solar Circle Spells.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter how easily I can summon Octavian on the night of the new moon if the Solar summoned Ligier during the last Calibration. My Incomparable Body Arsenal won't protect me from a Death Ray.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T19:27:23-07:00","id":1240285,"title":"","content":"Anyway, another testing point idea occurred to me.<br /> <br /> It seems totally legal for a Solar who is clinching an opponent to use Mountain-Crossing Leap Technique to take that opponent three range bands straight up. From there, she could simply release the hold and allow her victim to take falling damage, or she could use Crashing Wave Throw to hurl her victim even higher into the air for an even greater fall. Or punch him higher with a Heaven Thunder Hammer savaging attack, but that ought to be less efficient.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's a combination of an Athletics Charm with Brawl Charms. For Lunars, this combination would be all Strength Charms.<br /> <br /> How does the combination of the Lunar jumping Charm and the Lunar grapple-throwing Charm compare to Mighty Ram Impact and its upgrades?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T19:42:24-07:00","id":1240293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240270#post1240270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still waiting for an answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize some of us have other things going on don't you? As for my answer, you were the one implying a charm like Dragon-Sorcerer Puissance was balanced against other exalts gaining Celestial Circle Sorcery. I then asked if you believe the Lunar charms should be balanced against Solar's gaining access to Solar Circle Sorcery, meaning Essence 5. So, in point of fact, I'm the one still waiting for an answer! Do you believe the Lunar's sorcery charms should be locked behind Essence 5?<br /> <br /> Spirit-Draining Mudra is extremely limited since it requires you to have used Spirit-Caging Mandala on a spirit beforehand. Heaven-Turning Calculations is a valid sorcery enhancing charm, but it's problematic due to not being apart of the Occult tree. Also it requires significant investment to purchase with a high ability requirement, Essence 3, and a minimum of 4 lore charms. Perhaps to balance the Lunar sorcery charms, they should be placed under an attribute that doesn't effect sorcery, like Manipulation?<br /> <br /> I also recall questions being asked of the original developers, why Solar's didn't have any sorcery enhancing charms when Exalted 3E was released. I don't remember if it was Morke or Holden, but the response had something to do with sorcery in-setting was something exalts accessed later, and therefore none of them had charms associated with it. It seems the new devs have changed that policy, and while I'm not opposed to that at all. It does mean Solar's have been short-changed. Also, while I feel like a broken record having to tell you this over and over, no where does it say Solars are the masters of sorcery because of Solar Circle Sorcery. It is a general label applied to all sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T01:54:20-07:00","id":1240354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240019#post1240019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to echo PneumaPilot, and add words from the corebook (pg- 187) itself:<br /> <br /> Stunts may be used as often as desired\u2014<b>and to be clear, the average player can and should use a stunt to enhance almost every action her character takes. Storytellers are encouraged to err in the player\u2019s favor when deciding what is or isn\u2019t a stunt.</b><br /> <br /> The devs have even been quoted saying &quot;stunt everything&quot; on more then one occasion. I've worked with my players, two of them are new to Exalted, and they know I feel they should stunt every action. They're not required to, but simply describing an action with a bit of flare is a small price to pay for 2 bonus dice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I play in the same group as Wizard, and after more than 10 years with Exalted game we have stunt fatigue I think. Very rarly do we stunt these days, and it tends to be the same 2 players that will stunt the most often because they want the dice.<br /> <br /> I find the stunt mechanic cool for a while, and then just a chore to describe actions for dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T02:18:22-07:00","id":1240365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240293#post1240293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also recall questions being asked of the original developers, why Solar's didn't have any sorcery enhancing charms when Exalted 3E was released. I don't remember if it was Morke or Holden, but the response had something to do with sorcery in-setting was something exalts accessed later, and therefore none of them had charms associated with it. It seems the new devs have changed that policy, and while I'm not opposed to that at all. It does mean Solar's have been short-changed. Also, while I feel like a broken record having to tell you this over and over, no where does it say Solars are the masters of sorcery because of Solar Circle Sorcery. It is a general label applied to all sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think other exalts having ways to make their level of sorcery better compared to solars who just have access to every circle of sorcery is an interesting tradeoff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T06:36:51-07:00","id":1240413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240354#post1240354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I play in the same group as Wizard, and after more than 10 years with Exalted game we have stunt fatigue I think. Very rarly do we stunt these days, and it tends to be the same 2 players that will stunt the most often because they want the dice.<br /> <br /> I find the stunt mechanic cool for a while, and then just a chore to describe actions for dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that unfortunate. Describing cool stunts that entertain the whole group, and then receive a mechanical award, is one of my favorite things about Exalted. Multiple times, I've had someone who wasn't even going for a 2/3-point stunt, but just wanted a normal stunt, but described something that either awed or cracked up the whole group!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240365#post1240365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think other exalts having ways to make their level of sorcery better compared to solars who just have access to every circle of sorcery is an interesting tradeoff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can sympathize, but disagree with you. All published material claims Solar's are the masters of sorcery. That same material claims Lunar's are masters shapeshifters, and Sidereal's are masters of ancient, and secret martial arts. I doubt Lunar fans would be happy if most of their shapeshifting charms were locked behind Essence 5. Nor would Sidereal fans like to be told they can't learn Sidereal Martial Arts until Essence 5. So telling a Solar he's the master of sorcery only after he hits E5 is equally as silly from my perspective. I'm advocating that Solar's get 1, maybe 2 charms in Occult to enhance sorcery. Considering both Dragonbloods and Lunar's have access to similar charms, I'm not asking for much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T06:54:27-07:00","id":1240417,"title":"","content":"I personally have no particular problem with Solars getting 1 or 2 charms to enhance sorcery (and, as was pointed out... actually they do have 2 charms that enhance sorcery. One is dull but good, the other is ridiculously good and has a ton of prereqs). I don't think it's necessary, but neither is it much of an issue.<br /> <br /> I just object to the thing that was said (not by you, by others) that having 2 sorcery charms is worth paying 25% more XP for every spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I play in the same group as Wizard, and after more than 10 years with Exalted game we have stunt fatigue I think. Very rarly do we stunt these days, and it tends to be the same 2 players that will stunt the most often because they want the dice.<br /> <br /> I find the stunt mechanic cool for a while, and then just a chore to describe actions for dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely. There's one guy who still stunts because he likes it. And he comes up with much better stunts, because he's doing it for fun, not to get more dice. (He's also the worst at mechanics, so it balances out and doesn't make him more powerful.)<br /> <br /> But mostly, yeah you're right.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, honestly, when I ask 6 players to roll Awareness, I don't really want to wait for everyone to think of a sentence expressing how they're really good at noticing stuff that OOC they don't know so can't describe, in a way that's different to the other 6 players.<br /> <br /> Attacks are fine, and people do stunt those about half the time.<br /> <br /> I have found we stunt way more when doing fights or conversations over email in downtime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-30-2018, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T07:05:49-07:00","id":1240421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240354#post1240354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I play in the same group as Wizard, and after more than 10 years with Exalted game we have stunt fatigue I think. Very rarly do we stunt these days, and it tends to be the same 2 players that will stunt the most often because they want the dice.<br /> <br /> I find the stunt mechanic cool for a while, and then just a chore to describe actions for dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, I'm sorry you are finding yourselg fatigued by stunting. That sounds like a not fun place to be in. However, stunting is much less about getting dice as it is about making a cool scene. You don't have to reach for 3 point stunts every time. But don't let it become like PF. &quot;I swing my sword.&quot; That would suck more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:00:32-07:00","id":1240436,"title":"","content":"Yeah I mean it's not wrongbadfun to just go &quot;I wither that guy&quot;, if that's what your group likes. But at least 1-point stunts are a neat way to make people at least go &quot;I angrily swing my sword straight at his jugular&quot;, which doesn't take much more time, but is a lot more immersive.<br /> I agree that it can feel cumbersome to persistently try to get 2 or 3 point stunts, which probably isn't something people should do unless they find it to be a lot of fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:06:20-07:00","id":1240488,"title":"","content":"Tbh, when I was running 3e before with a couple of Lunar PCs, I just let them add the second attribute without a stunt if it was reasonable (like adding strength to the calculation with attacks, or adding appearance to the calculation when trying to charm people) because it was quicker and less hassle.<br /> Probably I should have checked each time, but it would have slowed the game down, and with 6 players combats weren't that fast anyway (though faster than 2nd ed... partly because without mote rewards, there was less laboured stunting just to get those precious motes/wp).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:48:12-07:00","id":1240507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240354#post1240354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I play in the same group as Wizard, and after more than 10 years with Exalted game we have stunt fatigue I think. Very rarly do we stunt these days, and it tends to be the same 2 players that will stunt the most often because they want the dice.<br /> <br /> I find the stunt mechanic cool for a while, and then just a chore to describe actions for dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Random suggestion from the Internet, but you could try changing up the stunt mechanics a bit. <br /> <br /> Rather than rewarding for a cool microstory about swinging your sword, reward for explaining how the opposition can't do anything to stop you. Or explain how your Craft-created arsenal enhances your actions. Or what it feels like to channel the Essence. Maybe allow for a stunt to carry for several turns, or for one player's stunt to carry the whole Circle for a turn or two (but reward the stunter, or best stunter, with the Willpower)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T14:17:50-07:00","id":1240582,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't see the need. People stunt when they think of something cool. Oh, and on pretty much all social attacks. Otherwise, they don't. And that's fine... Except when it comes to Lunar excellencies, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T14:23:34-07:00","id":1240585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240582#post1240582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't see the need. People stunt when they think of something cool. Oh, and on pretty much all social attacks. Otherwise, they don't. And that's fine... Except when it comes to Lunar excellencies, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was never a huge fan of stunting as a basic requirement of the system. I'm just not good at coming up with those kind of descriptions on the fly. Every once in awhile I can think up a good one but I find I spend as much time or more between rounds thinking up how to describe what I'm about to do rather than what I'm actually going to do on my turn. In shorter rounds this means that I end up not figuring out things like <i>how many dice do I roll here?</i>or <i>How many motes does this cost</i>. Not an issue with more simple actions of course, but still. <br /> <br /> However, this probably isn't the thread to be rehashing stunt vs no stunt.<br /> <br /> Was there a new podcast yesterday? Did it have any lunar stuff again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T14:46:26-07:00","id":1240596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240585#post1240585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was never a huge fan of stunting as a basic requirement of the system. I'm just not good at coming up with those kind of descriptions on the fly. Every once in awhile I can think up a good one but I find I spend as much time or more between rounds thinking up how to describe what I'm about to do rather than what I'm actually going to do on my turn. In shorter rounds this means that I end up not figuring out things like <i>how many dice do I roll here?</i>or <i>How many motes does this cost</i>. Not an issue with more simple actions of course, but still.<br /> <br /> However, this probably isn't the thread to be rehashing stunt vs no stunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could try swapping it out for a better version of success-converters from 1e. In addition to adding dice, you could swap out up to (Attribute) dice and just count them as successes without rolling. I suppose the effect on unrolled values like defenses would be akin to Reed in the Wind's increased defense cap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:19:26-07:00","id":1240644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239907#post1239907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, I'm a bit bothered by Lunar's having sorcery-enhancing charms. While it's true Lunar's can't access Solar Circle Sorcery, it means that Lunar's are better then Solar's at Terrestrial and Celestial Sorcery. Solar's are stated repeatedly to be the masters of sorcery <b>in general</b>, not just the masters of Solar Circle Sorcery. In the end, as a ST, I only have 2 options. Either invalidate both the Lunar Sorcery Charms, or create a few for Solar's!</div> </div> </div> </div>Where can you point to find the phrase &quot;sorcery in general&quot;, or anything like it?<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted have been hailed as the best shapeshifters among the Exalted, but that shouldn't be taken to mean they can perform every imaginable form of shapeshifting, much less every form better than others.<br /> <br /> For example, we have been told not to expect rubber-man stretching Charms from Lunar Exalted, but we know for a fact that grotesque limb-extension is something that Liminal Exalted do.<br /> <br /> We know that Lunar Exalted can't take the Heart's Blood of demons (though they can the appearance), and that Infernals are slated to have Shintai transformations.<br /> <br /> So long as Solar Exalted can learn sorcery sooner than anyone else (no prerequisite Charms), as fast as the fastest learners (ie: Favoring costs), acquire three shaping rituals of any combination their player desires (without any native Charms filling in for flavorful but splat-universal rituals), and uniquely cast Solar Circle Sorcery, then how can they be anything but the best sorcerers in the world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-30-2018, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:38:06-07:00","id":1240650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240585#post1240585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there a new podcast yesterday? Did it have any lunar stuff again?</div> </div> </div> </div>We interviewed Eric Minton on the new episode. It\u2019s up now. He had some very interesting things to say! Check it out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T19:19:32-07:00","id":1240683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240644#post1240644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can you point to find the phrase &quot;sorcery in general&quot;, or anything like it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar's being masters of sorcery is a general statement, because it lacks any specific descriptors. It's doesn't say Solar's are the masters of Solar Circle Sorcery, or Celestial Circle, or Terrestrial Circle. It doesn't say Solar's are masters of any particular types of sorcerous spells, rituals, or initiations. It's simply states &quot;Solar's are the masters of sorcery&quot;. It's a general statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240644#post1240644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So long as Solar Exalted can learn sorcery sooner than anyone else (no prerequisite Charms)</div> </div> </div> </div>Just yesterday you were saying Solar's access to Solar Circle Sorcery was the reason for Solar mastery of sorcery. You even went as far as to call out specific spells in specific situations as examples. So what logic does mentioning a lack of prerequisite charms have? By your logic, Solar's are required to spend 300 XP to to attain their theme of &quot;master of sorcery&quot;. Dragonbloods and Lunars have to spend, what, 10-30 XP on prereq charms to access their sorcery enhancing charms. Seems a bit imbalanced to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240644#post1240644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as fast as the fastest learners (ie: Favoring costs)</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong, but doesn't all exalts currently previewed have this in some form or another? It's a serious question by the way. I know Dragonbloods can favor sorcery, so has something different been said about Lunars?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240644#post1240644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">acquire three shaping rituals of any combination their player desires (without any native Charms filling in for flavorful but splat-universal rituals)</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the corebook, it's possible for anyone to learn more shaping rituals. I distinctly recall Vance saying it was possible as well, and that it was the ST who had to be careful with balance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240644#post1240644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">uniquely cast Solar Circle Sorcery, then how can they be anything but the best sorcerers in the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, because I'm pretty sure the devs mentioned Infernals will have access to Solar Circle Sorcery. I'm not sure about Abyssals, I remember something about them losing access to Solar Sorcery across the splat, but were unique in their ability to access the 3rd tier of Necromancy in this edition. I might be mis-remembering this though. Regardless, Solar Circle Sorcery isn't unique to Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 07-30-2018, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T19:34:39-07:00","id":1240690,"title":"","content":"Possibly a bit of a relic by now, but 1e Sidereals we\u2019re linked to mages (and magic) back in the hoary days of the mid 90s. I suspect that is where the Sidereals connection with Sorcery came about. <br /> <br /> And if they have to be better at something and worse at something I guess it would make sense, using twisted past logic, for them to be better at Sorcery and worse at Necromancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T19:48:45-07:00","id":1240693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240683#post1240683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar's being masters of sorcery is a general statement, because it lacks any specific descriptors.</div> </div> </div> </div>When have you seen specific descriptors about Sidereals being the best at martial arts, or the masters of destiny? Getimians will be able to do things to destiny that Sidereals never could.<br /> <br /> The Terrestrial Exalted are masters of the elements, and even then, there are things they just can't do with the elements.<br /> <br /> Can you point to any specific descriptors of Lunar Exalted mastery of shapeshifting?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just yesterday you were saying Solar's access to Solar Circle Sorcery was the reason for Solar mastery of sorcery. </div> </div> </div>So you just forgot all the other shit I said Solars enjoyed with sorcery, then?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know Dragonbloods can favor sorcery, so has something different been said about Lunars? </div> </div> </div>Last we heard, Lunar Exalted could not favor sorcery through any Attribute, but the developers are paying special attention to how this balances out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> According to the corebook, it's possible for anyone to learn more shaping rituals. </div> </div> </div>The corebook mentions that, with storyteller approval, it might be possible for a particular mortal sorcerer to learn more than the one ritual they purchase through a merit. Nothing suggests that Exalted can gain rituals through a merit rather than a Charm, and in fact emphasis is put on the fact that most Exalted gain rituals through Charms.<br /> <br /> Also, the main text says that Solar Exalted are not limited to choosing more of the rituals of their original initiation archetype; their experiences can allow them to choose different ones appropriate to their story. But side-bar does not say that those experiences alone are enough to give a Solar an extra ritual except through buying a Charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really, because I'm pretty sure the devs mentioned Infernals will have access to Solar Circle Sorcery. </div> </div> </div>Infernals are ultimately Solars. What's your point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T21:18:22-07:00","id":1240713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240693#post1240693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When have you seen specific descriptors about Sidereals being the best at martial arts, or the masters of destiny? Getimians will be able to do things to destiny that Sidereals never could.</div> </div> </div> </div>When did I, or the corebook say Sidereals were the best at martial arts, or the masters of destiny? I haven't infringed on any abilities the Getimian's might possess. I haven't even mentioned them in any of my posts. As for Sidereals, all I've said was &quot;they are masters of ancient, and secret martial arts.&quot; Which is straight from the corebook, and is heavily implying the descriptor of &quot;Sidereal Martial Arts&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240693#post1240693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Terrestrial Exalted are masters of the elements, and even then, there are things they just can't do with the elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, not something I or the corebook said. It's not even claimed in the WFHW as far as word search can find.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240693#post1240693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you point to any specific descriptors of Lunar Exalted mastery of shapeshifting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, Exalted Core pg- 47 &quot;Play one of the Lunar exalted if you want to be a master shapeshifter, wearing a thousand stolen forms.&quot; The descriptors right their at the end, wearing stolen forms. This implies a core concept of their shapeshifting requires them to steal forms. Seems pretty accurate from what we've heard in previews.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240693#post1240693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you just forgot all the other shit I said Solars enjoyed with sorcery, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not. I answered each point in turn.... Did you not read my entire post?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240693#post1240693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last we heard, Lunar Exalted could not favor sorcery through any Attribute, but the developers are paying special attention to how this balances out.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you did read further! I hadn't heard Lunar's couldn't favor sorcery. I'd honestly find that rather unfortunate if it holds throughout the development process. It still doesn't justify your belief that Lunar sorcery charms are balanced against the Solar's access to Solar Circle Sorcery. Unless those Lunar charms are Essence 5 charms. By the way, still waiting for your answer on that question?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240693#post1240693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The corebook mentions that, with storyteller approval, it might be possible for a particular mortal sorcerer to learn more than the one ritual they purchase through a merit. Nothing suggests that Exalted can gain rituals through a merit rather than a Charm, and in fact emphasis is put on the fact that most Exalted gain rituals through Charms.<br /> <br /> Also, the main text says that Solar Exalted are not limited to choosing more of the rituals of their original initiation archetype; their experiences can allow them to choose different ones appropriate to their story. But side-bar does not say that those experiences alone are enough to give a Solar an extra ritual except through buying a Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Ask the Dev thread:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1216365#post1216365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can gain additional shaping rituals at the Storyteller's discretion, but there's no centralized universal mechanic for doing so. The rules for gaining a shaping ritual by creating a sorcerous relic provide a good polestar for how difficult/expensive that should be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240693#post1240693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infernals are ultimately Solars. What's your point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no. They have completely different theme's, powers, and mechanics. Current word from the Devs is they'll be even weirder then they were last edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T21:34:21-07:00","id":1240714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240693#post1240693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When have you seen specific descriptors about Sidereals being the best at martial arts, or the masters of destiny?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. In the core book under page 48.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T21:46:01-07:00","id":1240719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240714#post1240714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh. In the core book under page 48.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstood the context.<br /> <br /> He's complaining about a lack of &quot;qualifiers&quot; that warn people when a splat's &quot;mastery&quot; might be less than all-encompassing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T21:55:58-07:00","id":1240720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240719#post1240719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You misunderstood the context.<br /> <br /> He's complaining about a lack of &quot;qualifiers&quot; that warn people when a splat's &quot;mastery&quot; might be less than all-encompassing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, each mastery has words under it. Solars and sidereals both have the master of MA but sidereals are considered peerless. Yeah yeah gementians blah blah. My point is for solars it implies more that they used sorcery as a tool to craft wonders. Which would be more in line with sorcereous workings which they are the best at. They also still have the best sorcery and crafting. I don't think they need much in the way of sorcery augments because it would blow their Solar circle magic way out of bounds to what it already is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T01:04:33-07:00","id":1240755,"title":"","content":"Honestly &quot;masters of sorcery&quot; could easily mean &quot;they can take sorcery as far as it can go&quot; ie, get solar circle. <br /> <br /> And like, that's it. That's could easily be all they meant by that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T06:16:52-07:00","id":1240824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1239532#post1239532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were to use a hybrid form to give yourself a soak-improving thick hide, would the increased soak from DBT stack with that? How does armor interact with these kinds of transformation charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t see why the soak wouldn\u2019t stack, and Robert said that moonsilver artifacts change size along with Lunars when they grow huge, so it stands to reason that at least moonsilver armor will always change shape, too.<br /> <br /> Other materials might change enough to fit your Hybrid Form, but I have no claims to base this on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T06:22:20-07:00","id":1240829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240719#post1240719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's complaining about a lack of &quot;qualifiers&quot; that warn people when a splat's &quot;mastery&quot; might be less than all-encompassing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less complaining, and more participating in a friendly debate at this point. I've always viewed debates as a way to compare/contrast differing views, as well as exchange information. For instance, I had forgotten about Heaven-Turning Calculations. I feel I can be forgiven for that, since it's so deep in a tree that doesn't typically interact with sorcery. I'll have to keep that charm highlighted just to point out to new players from now on. I also learned Lunar's may have no way to favor sorcery. Personally, I hope they change this decision. My point is, debates can raise new and interesting perspectives. I've actually halted any work on creating a new Solar sorcery-enhancing charm while we debate the issue. Also, while you may not care, I've been enjoying our debate. Though we have pretty handily derailed this thread. I'll create a new one when I get off work this afternoon, or you're welcome to if you like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240720#post1240720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, each mastery has words under it. Solars and sidereals both have the master of MA but sidereals are considered peerless. Yeah yeah gementians blah blah. My point is for solars it implies more that they used sorcery as a tool to craft wonders. Which would be more in line with sorcereous workings which they are the best at. They also still have the best sorcery and crafting. I don't think they need much in the way of sorcery augments because it would blow their Solar circle magic way out of bounds to what it already is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well their is no mention of Sidereals being &quot;peerless&quot; that I can find. Not saying they're not, just that it doesn't exist in current published material. I wouldn't dismiss Getimians so lightly, because if the Sidereals do have a peer in martial arts, it's them. I believe if the devs had intended for Solar's to be masters of sorcerous workings instead of sorcery, they would simply have said so. Also, you're assuming I can't devise a Solar sorcery-buffing charm that has little or no effect on Solar Circle Sorcery. I can think of one or two ways to limit it just off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240755#post1240755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly &quot;masters of sorcery&quot; could easily mean &quot;they can take sorcery as far as it can go&quot; ie, get solar circle.<br /> <br /> And like, that's it. That's could easily be all they meant by that.</div> </div> </div> </div>In point of fact, I think this is exactly what the old devs meant. As I mentioned in another post, I recall to old devs being asked about the lack of sorcery enhancing charms for Solars. Their response was something like &quot;sorcery was something, in-setting, that exalts developed later, and that no exalt was really going to have sorcery enhancing charms.&quot; I'm sure I'm butchering what was actually said. The point was Solar's didn't have any Occult charms that buffed sorcery, because no one was intended too. Perhaps that's why the one real charm that does it for Solars, is in Lore. However, the new devs have obviously changed that policy. Which is absolutely fine. It does mean Solar's have gotten the short-stick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T06:28:41-07:00","id":1240831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240829#post1240829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well their is no mention of Sidereals being &quot;peerless&quot; that I can find. Not saying they're not, just that it doesn't exist in current published material. I wouldn't dismiss Getimians so lightly, because if the Sidereals do have a peer in martial arts, it's them. I believe if the devs had intended for Solar's to be masters of sorcerous workings instead of sorcery, they would simply have said so. Also, you're assuming I can't devise a Solar sorcery-buffing charm that has little or no effect on Solar Circle Sorcery. I can think of one or two ways to limit it just off the top of my head..</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Core<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those who remember the Sidereals of old agree on one thing: they were martial artists whose genius was without compare. Only the Solar Exalted could boast equal prowess, and then only under the tutelage of a Sidereal mentor. Their mystical fighting systems, the Sidereal Martial Arts, are the whispered legends and ultimate secret styles of the martial arts world. </div> </div> </div>Genius without compare generally means peerless.<br /> <br /> Edit- Whoops I forgot where I read that it was all the way in the MA section under mastery.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mastery: This keyword denotes Charms that have a greater effect when used by those Exalted who are masters of mortal Abilities: the Solar and Abyssal Exalted. The Sidereal Exalted, peerless masters of the martial arts, have their own esoteric methods for accessing these effects. </div> </div> </div>Also, any sorcery-buffing charm is going to apply to every circle equally. Especially when it's just a die increase.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 07-31-2018, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T06:35:40-07:00","id":1240833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240831#post1240831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From the Core<br /> <br /> Genius without compare generally means peerless.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but Getimians didn't exist back then. They're a new thing. Literally something new in the setting, not just this edition. As I said, if Sidereals have a peer, it's them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T07:25:16-07:00","id":1240847,"title":"","content":"The sidereals are peerless, but not unrivalled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T07:35:04-07:00","id":1240854,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lunars-preview-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\">Also this just dropped</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T07:43:16-07:00","id":1240860,"title":"","content":"Lol, the next sentence says Solar(oid)s can equal their prowess, under tutelage, granted, but still. Equal prowess means having peers?<br /> <br /> Semantics and word games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T19:22:18-07:00","id":1241120,"title":"","content":"Query: Did the replace-Dex-With-Str for Attack charm allow use of unarmed strikes? I\u2019m considering a Martial Artist and was wondering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T19:25:24-07:00","id":1241121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240860#post1240860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lol, the next sentence says Solar(oid)s can equal their prowess, under tutelage, granted, but still. Equal prowess means having peers?<br /> <br /> Semantics and word games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, they don't get sutra effects from what vance said in the dev thread. So they certainly don't have the same power when it comes to using SMA. They also can't teach it so while they get near comparable prowess, it's not the same. We'll have to wait when sidereals comes out and SMA is in to see how different sutra and non-sutra bonuses are. It could be the difference between mastery and none, or it could be the difference between a celestial martial artist and terrestrial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T19:29:21-07:00","id":1241122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241120#post1241120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query: Did the replace-Dex-With-Str for Attack charm allow use of unarmed strikes? I\u2019m considering a Martial Artist and was wondering.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's like the stamina charm, it should.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T19:58:03-07:00","id":1241131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241122#post1241122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's like the stamina charm, it should.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be a strange omission but since I don\u2019t have the Charm text I thought I\u2019d check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T05:46:20-07:00","id":1241260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1240860#post1240860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lol, the next sentence says Solar(oid)s can equal their prowess, under tutelage, granted, but still. Equal prowess means having peers?<br /> <br /> Semantics and word games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Consider previous editions, where Sidereals could devise esoteric martial arts that Solars could learn, but could not create themselves.<br /> <br /> There's no reason to assume 3rd edition is going to do away with that when Kung-Fu History Monks is a Siddie <i>thing</i>, and unlike Lunars Sids have had a pretty coherent mission and vision since day one.<br /> <br /> In relation to the Lunars vs. Solars in sorcery department, then, it's not so strange for Lunars to have charms that Solars do not in relation to sorcery, but Solars are still accessing a third circle and rolling more dice on average. (<i>NO, you are not going to stunt two attributes on every single Shape Sorcery roll.)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T08:21:25-07:00","id":1241314,"title":"","content":"Well yeah, Sidereals are peerless in Sidereal Martial Arts, as they should be, but in Martial Arts, Solars are right there on top, as they should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T08:33:02-07:00","id":1241321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241314#post1241314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yeah, Sidereals are peerless in Sidereal Martial Arts, as they should be, but in Martial Arts, Solars are right there on top, as they should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they aren't unless you take brawl. Which is back to being separate from ma. Both solars and sidereals have access to mastery and sidereals have sma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T08:47:28-07:00","id":1241327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241321#post1241321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except they aren't unless you take brawl. Which is back to being separate from ma. Both solars and sidereals have access to mastery and sidereals have sma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Word from the developers some time back was that all Sidereals will likely be slated to treat MA as favored even if they didn't tag Brawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:29:36-07:00","id":1241342,"title":"","content":"I think they also said something about Sids being able to access SMA effects solars can't, with like sutras or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:58:07-07:00","id":1241358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241327#post1241327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Word from the developers some time back was that all Sidereals will likely be slated to treat MA as favored even if they didn't tag Brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point with that though is that brawl and ma are two different things. Sidereals are going to be the best at MA because none of it is innate. You learn or develop a style and everyone who's strong enough gets to learn it. Compared to brawl which is just a beat down.<br /> <br /> I imagine the fact that lunars have abilities that just enhance any unarmed attack is why they don't get mastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T10:12:55-07:00","id":1241364,"title":"","content":"I would like to point out that this derail is much less about speculating about the new Lunar book than it is complaining about the dev\u2019s balance decisions for Solars and Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T10:36:35-07:00","id":1241376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241364#post1241364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to point out that this derail is much less about speculating about the new Lunar book than it is complaining about the dev\u2019s balance decisions for Solars and Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried to bring it back around. It is interesting that the stamina lunar charm doesn't rely on abilities. They'll probably be able to combo native charms with ma if it's a feature and not an exception. Unless the charms mention specific brawl attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T10:54:55-07:00","id":1241383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241321#post1241321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except they aren't unless you take brawl. Which is back to being separate from ma. Both solars and sidereals have access to mastery and sidereals have sma.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What a silly argument.<br /> <br /> A particular Sidereal that does not take MA is no better at it than any mortal.<br /> <br /> Whats your point?<br /> <br /> Also Solars have access to Mastery 100%, while whether that is true or not for Sidereals is yet to be seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T10:59:42-07:00","id":1241386,"title":"","content":"If you want to talk about how Lunars stand up against Sidereals, or how they stand up against Solars, that'd fit. But if you want to talk about Solars vs Sidereals, you should probably start a new thread. It doesn't have anything to do with the Lunar playtest.<br /> <br /> So back to that: Does the stuff revealed in the playtest inspire anyone with any particular concepts?<br /> <br /> The echolocation charm in the preview makes me think of a vampire bat-Lunar, which I've considered before. A lot of vampire trappings, necromancer, from the north, etc, but not actually undead. With the swarm charms mentioned in the playtest, you could become a swarm of bats. I have no idea if that'd be good, but it'd be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:03:44-07:00","id":1241393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241383#post1241383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Solars have access to Mastery 100%, while whether that is true or not for Sidereals is yet to be seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mastery is binary. They either have mastery or they don't. Solars have mastery. Sidereals are stated to have mastery. However, DB's and lunars don't.<br /> <br /> I would be interested to find out how lunars interact with native charms and ma but so far solars and dragon blooded have almost zero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 08-01-2018, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:32:30-07:00","id":1241407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241393#post1241393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mastery is binary. They either have mastery or they don't. Solars have mastery. Sidereals are stated to have mastery. However, DB's and lunars don't.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Mastery is not a binary state.<br /> <br /> And no it isn't stated that Sidereals have Mastery on all the time. It is stated they have esotheric methods to access Mastery. Which can be something like what DB IMAs do to avoid the Terrestrial keyword.<br /> <br /> I asked Vance on the Dev Thread, and, like I said, nothing is set in stone yet.<br /> <br /> From what I understood of his answer, he is trying to make the &quot;esotheric method&quot; into something cool.<br /> <br /> So it also goes to say that if they have to employ the &quot;esotheric method&quot; to access Mastery, they don't have 100% on all the time, like Solaroids.<br /> <br /> All subject to change, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T12:50:48-07:00","id":1241458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241376#post1241376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tried to bring it back around. It is interesting that the stamina lunar charm doesn't rely on abilities. They'll probably be able to combo native charms with ma if it's a feature and not an exception. Unless the charms mention specific brawl attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Charm definitely encourages you to use Fire Dragon Style unarmed, with or without magical claws.<br /> <br /> But if you want to use Fire Dragon and Steel Devil together, you\u2019re going to want a Dexterity build.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T13:07:15-07:00","id":1241465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241458#post1241458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Charm definitely encourages you to use Fire Dragon Style unarmed, with or without magical claws.<br /> <br /> But if you want to use Fire Dragon and Steel Devil together, you\u2019re going to want a Dexterity build.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps but I'm moreso wondering what kind of interactions they'll have compared to solars and DBs who only have the ability to add die from exellencies and no unique charms in MA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T13:24:22-07:00","id":1241471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241386#post1241386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to talk about how Lunars stand up against Sidereals, or how they stand up against Solars, that'd fit. But if you want to talk about Solars vs Sidereals, you should probably start a new thread. It doesn't have anything to do with the Lunar playtest.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, though the context of the argument was that of Sidereal vs Lunars, and one of the balance points mentioned was that of Sidereal mastery of MAs that should be counterbalanced by Lunar mastery of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> So the understanding of how the MA relationship of Sidereals and Solars works is tangential to the point being argued.<br /> <br /> So it was a triangulated argument.<br /> <br /> Understanding that Sidereals have a special relationship with MAs without necessarily overshadowing Solars helps understanding that Lunars can have a similar relationship with Sorcery.<br /> <br /> It avoids the fallacy of &quot;Sidereals are better at MAs than Solars, so Lunars should be better at Sorcery than both!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T14:18:07-07:00","id":1241493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241471#post1241471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It avoids the fallacy of &quot;Sidereals are better at MAs than Solars, so Lunars should be better at Sorcery than both!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>,<br /> Even conditional access to Mastery, means that most times, a master martial artist sidereal will be objectively better than a master martial artist solar, especially with SMA. Which, unlike mastery, solars will never be able to get the sutra bonuses of SMA. And while Solars are better at sorcery it doesn't mean that lunars won't have tricks that make them conditionally better. That shadow spell shaping charm certainly seems to make them the best combat sorcerers. However, it seems like this edition lunars will be more than ever working on their shapeshifting and what exactly they can do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T14:46:09-07:00","id":1241502,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"116\" data-vbnamecard=\"116\">Epimetheus</a><br /> <br /> Not really.<br /> <br /> It goes back to what I first stated. Sidereals will be better at SMAs, as they should be. Solar(oid)s will be better at MAs, as they have non-conditional Mastery for it. Also don't be so quick in assuming things about the Sutras.<br /> <br /> This is Vance on the matter, not so long ago:<br /> <br /> &quot;A Solar martial artist can boast knowledge of all of Snake style, or blend powerful techniques from multiple styles, right out of character creation. They will be as devastatingly powerful in combat, generally speaking, as a Solar who's devoted themselves to any of the other combat Abilities. This is as it should be. The Solar Exalted are unquestionably the mightiest of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> This does not mean that a Sidereal must be overshadowed when it comes to being a martial artist. Their are all sorts of advantages they could have (I say could because we haven't started on their mechanics) which Solars don't get: easier access to Martial Arts, native Charms that synergize with Martial Arts styles, the ability to teach themselves Sidereal Martial Arts and invent new styles without need of a tutor.&quot;<br /> <br /> For all we know there might be a way for a Solar to activate the power of the Sutras, as the Sidereals have a way to access Mastery, or there may not be, like IMAs and Aura. But Sidereals can be peerless MAs when looked at hollistically rather than some clear cut thing.<br /> <br /> Don't be so certain about uncertain things, that leads to disappointment.<br /> <br /> As for Sorcery, Solars have Solar Circle access, with it's spells, additional Shaping Ritual, and ease of Workings that come with it. They also have Sorcery Charms with no pre-requisites, so they are the ones that can most easily dip into Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Lunar Sorcery access Charms will have pre-reqs, though fewer than DB's.<br /> <br /> I see no problem with Lunars having Sorcery tricks that Solars just can't replicate or do better. But this will be a subjective &quot;better&quot;.<br /> <br /> Who is the &quot;better&quot; combat sorcerer the Lunar shadow casting Cantata of Empty Voices, or a Solar blasting away with Death Ray? The scenarios are just too varied for this to be a useful discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 08-01-2018, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T14:57:50-07:00","id":1241507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241502#post1241502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"116\" data-vbnamecard=\"116\">Epimetheus</a><br /> <br /> For all we know there might be a way for a Solar to activate the power of the Sutras, as the Sidereals have a way to access Mastery, or there may not be, like IMAs and Aura. But Sidereals can be peerless MAs when looked at hollistically rather than some clear cut thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's like saying Solars can craft fate or shapeshift. There are a number of things solars just can't do no matter how much they want to. We'll have to see how lunars and sidereals work before more setting assumptions can be made, but regardless the fact is, that solars can't do everything. They can do almost everything but that doesn't mean you can just give them stuff that's out of theme like shadow shaping just because lunars have it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T15:05:59-07:00","id":1241511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241507#post1241507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's like saying Solars can craft fate or shapeshift. There are a number of things solars just can't do no matter how much they want to. We'll have to see how lunars and sidereals work before more setting assumptions can be made, but regardless the fact is, that solars can't do everything. They can do almost everything but that doesn't mean you can just give them stuff that's out of theme like shadow shaping just because lunars have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This will be the last that I speak on this matter on this thread, because it is getting to a derail point.<br /> <br /> I'm not an expert on past editions, but I remember skimming through SMAs in the past, and I thought that before there were two levels of Sutras, and that Solars could access the first level.<br /> <br /> Now, we don't know at all how things will turn out this edition, but if what I remember is true, then your statement doesn't hold water, as it is something that historically Solars have had the ability to touch.<br /> <br /> Again, don't invest certainty on uncertain things so you don't get upset later. Keep an open mind and trust that the people involved will deliver the best they can, and we can discuss minutiae when we have a solid base from which to launch, instead of my or your assumptions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T15:18:49-07:00","id":1241519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241511#post1241511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not an expert on past editions, but I remember skimming through SMAs in the past, and I thought that before there were two levels of Sutras, and that Solars could access the first level.</div> </div> </div> </div>They had no access to it, ever. There are some things solars just can't do, nor should they. Perhaps with an N/A artifact like the mantle they could but that's like giving a Celestial the mantle of Brigid. Though it would be interesting to see what Raksi would to get damn thing. Speaking of which, why wouldn't someone who's that old not know about it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T17:44:16-07:00","id":1241591,"title":"","content":"Do Lunars get anything akin to Wound-Mastering Body Evolution?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T19:49:13-07:00","id":1241647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241519#post1241519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They had no access to it, ever. There are some things solars just can't do, nor should they. Perhaps with an N/A artifact like the mantle they could but that's like giving a Celestial the mantle of Brigid. Though it would be interesting to see what Raksi would to get damn thing. Speaking of which, why wouldn't someone who's that old not know about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if she knows about it, but is losing the &quot;I'm striving to do something canonically impossible in a sort of pitiful and insane way, and am therefore a bit hard to take seariously&quot; bit where she's trying to get Solar Circle Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T20:05:20-07:00","id":1241652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241386#post1241386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So back to that: Does the stuff revealed in the playtest inspire anyone with any particular concepts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Magpie\u2019s Nest Resourcefulness should be inspiring every Lunar to wear a trench coat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T20:06:15-07:00","id":1241653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241376#post1241376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tried to bring it back around. It is interesting that the stamina lunar charm doesn't rely on abilities. They'll probably be able to combo native charms with ma if it's a feature and not an exception. Unless the charms mention specific brawl attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>As did I. The point in my case was by analogy in regards to the Lunar sorcery complaints. Solars are excellent at everything they do, but they are always excellent in a Solar fashion. They cannot be excellent at things Solars do not do at all. Solar themes tend to be straightforward, supernatural applications of the base ability. While they don't do esoteric things, often they can get similar results through raw power.<br /> <br /> So a Lunar can be tricky and capture a few motes in their anima. Solars can accomplish the same by making MORE motes, and not sweating the loss if they need to pause for a round.<br /> <br /> It's akin to how a Solar can't turn into a bird, but they can fly by jumping so hard they forget to come back down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T04:24:08-07:00","id":1241754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1241652#post1241652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Magpie\u2019s Nest Resourcefulness should be inspiring every Lunar to wear a trench coat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or a long feathered cloak with many pockets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/513-gatts","name":"Gatts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T05:05:31-07:00","id":1241767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-ex