":"2018-08-03T04:52:09-07:00","id":1242299,"title":"","content":"Do Lunars have Charms to make illusions?<br /> <br /> I've been thinking about some things that were probably dropped or revised as time went on and the developers changed. Illusions seems like an old bugaboo that would have been ripe for such a change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T06:50:14-07:00","id":1242339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1242299#post1242299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Lunars have Charms to make illusions?<br /> <br /> I've been thinking about some things that were probably dropped or revised as time went on and the developers changed. Illusions seems like an old bugaboo that would have been ripe for such a change.</div> </div> </div> </div>By leaning into the idea that higher Lunar Charms start emulating the miracles of Luna, Lunars could create illusions at least on par with that Water-aspected eidolons thing, if the writers want.<br /> <br /> Maybe Lunars could finally have an equivalent of Phantom-Conjuring Performance.<br /> <br /> But it doesn\u2019t matter much to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T07:04:59-07:00","id":1242340,"title":"","content":"I'd be very surprised if they didn't. Ex3 provides ample ground for use of illusions. The Lunar in the comic basically did one as a distraction gambit. If I remember right Tale-Spinning Mastery gave Eska double 9s on instill actions by creating them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T07:24:45-07:00","id":1242346,"title":"","content":"It was really kind of a question for the people that have seen the Charms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T07:52:43-07:00","id":1242354,"title":"","content":"Lol, true. I was hoping folks at Gencon would poke us with stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T08:55:55-07:00","id":1242375,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll see what I can dig up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T09:05:46-07:00","id":1242381,"title":"","content":"There were a couple of hits on a search for \u201cillus\u201d through the text. One supplements a go to ground action, helping you essentially disappear. The other can grant you some illusory features while trying to disguise yourself as another type of Essence-being.<br /> <br /> Are there other words I could search for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T09:37:25-07:00","id":1242390,"title":"","content":"phantasmal, maybe?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T09:40:04-07:00","id":1242391,"title":"","content":"My friend suggests a search for Wasp.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if Claws of the Silver Moon is back or something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T10:32:22-07:00","id":1242409,"title":"","content":"No to phantasmal and wasp...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T10:35:37-07:00","id":1242414,"title":"","content":"Dream-Weaving Voice didn\u2019t weave illusions in the sense of holograms in the physical world, but rather hallucinations in the mind of the listener.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T10:40:59-07:00","id":1242419,"title":"","content":"Oh, you wanted holograms, I was thinking hallucinations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T13:28:38-07:00","id":1242473,"title":"","content":"To potentially save some effort, Lunars don't have anything that works like minor image in D&amp;D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T00:31:10-07:00","id":1242894,"title":"","content":"After seeing the official preview and the Charms that require a Major or Defining intimacy to use, I'm wondering, how easy is it for Lunars to give intimacies of that level to others? It seems like they'll be good with intimacies in general, but I wonder if a Lunar with significant investment in the right social Charms will be able to use things like Heart-Drinking Allure and Stalking Nightmare Hunter more or less freely, or if they'll be situational or require a non-trivial amount of setup.<br /> <br /> I'm particularly interested in what Charms Lunars have that jump right to Defining-level effects, since I like Changing Moons and I'm excited to see what experienced social Lunars can pull off in this edition. I doubt that even elder Lunars can just hand out intimacies of that strength like candy, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T07:53:11-07:00","id":1243207,"title":"","content":"I'm curious if Lunars can do something with their Strength Charms that Solars cannot do, since their Athletics and Brawl Charms are separate.<br /> <br /> Does Mighty Ram Practice or any other &quot;knockback&quot; Charm throw a target back according to the number of range bands that a Lunar did or could have traveled?<br /> <br /> Like, if the Lunar uses their equivalent of Mountain-Crossing Leap Technique or Godspeed Steps, which would let them cross two or three range bands with a single movement action, but they attack a target who was in close or short range, is the target sent flying away a number of range bands equal to the distance that the Lunar didn't?<br /> <br /> One version would be for the Lunar to tackle and grapple the target, continuing to move forward while carrying their victim with them.<br /> <br /> The other is simply striking the target to send them flying while the Lunar stops in the range band where she struck the target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T18:03:59-07:00","id":1243347,"title":"","content":"Also, would Mighty Ram Practice be a Brawl or Brawl/MA exclusive attack Charm, rather than an Ability-agnostic Charm? Since both Solars and Terrestrials both lack Charms to inflict knockback with Melee weapons, and Sidereals also never had such a trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T23:03:57-07:00","id":1243411,"title":"","content":"I'd think that's just an advantage of Lunar charms. And it makes sense to me to use it with tetsubos, etc.<br /> <br /> Might be reasonable to say it doesn't work with non-unarmed light weapons though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T06:08:25-07:00","id":1243475,"title":"","content":"If Lunar Strength Charms can inflict knockback/down without a smash attack but with a weapon, why can\u2019t Dragon-Blooded and Solar Melee Charms do the same?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T07:04:14-07:00","id":1243490,"title":"","content":"Probably just because knockback/down were already in Brawl and they didn't want them to feel too similar. What I mean is, I think there's some deliberate avoidance of putting similar effects in Melee and Brawl. There's no particular reason why Solars have a bunch of Melee charms that do Holy stuff, but not Brawl.* Nor is there a particular reason why Brawl has the charm for rushing towards people really fast and attacking them before they have time to act (after all, that seems pretty appropriate for a duelist or knife-wielder).<br /> *Other than Paladins are generally depicted with swords. But there's no real reason why a Solar brawler shouldn't be good at punching demons with his sun-blessed fists.<br /> <br /> As Lunars just have the one tree, they don't really need to worry about it. There's no need to make Lunar melee and brawl different, when you're concentrating instead on making Dexterity and Strength different (and I'm very sure Dexterity won't have any knockback/down).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-07-2018, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T18:37:06-07:00","id":1243672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1243475#post1243475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Lunar Strength Charms can inflict knockback/down without a smash attack but with a weapon, why can\u2019t Dragon-Blooded and Solar Melee Charms do the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory? No reason at all. But the corebook wants to keep the different abilities feeling different and that's respectable.<br /> <br /> Wizard of Oz already mentioned holy anti-creature-of-darkness stuff in one and not the other. To a certain point that's a reasonable domain for custom charms and/or evocations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T14:41:01-07:00","id":1252356,"title":"","content":"In honour of the Lunars' new ability to access Labyrinth Circle of Necromancy, I thought I'd bring this back. <br /> <br /> PneumaPilot, now you've had some more time with the playtest, are there any charms you didn't pay much attention to before, but now think are really cool?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T19:03:35-07:00","id":1252419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1252356#post1252356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In honour of the Lunars' new ability to access Labyrinth Circle of Necromancy, I thought I'd bring this back. <br /> <br /> PneumaPilot, now you've had some more time with the playtest, are there any charms you didn't pay much attention to before, but now think are really cool?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t know the Labyrinth circle thing was confirmed. <br /> <br /> My word, was it in one of the previews and I just missed it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T19:07:20-07:00","id":1252422,"title":"","content":"Nah, it was just something Vance said as a current set-up for it. But considering we won't see Necromancy for like 2 years its just a neat idea at this point. It can easily change in the mean-time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T19:52:13-07:00","id":1252424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1252422#post1252422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, it was just something Vance said as a current set-up for it. But considering we won't see Necromancy for like 2 years its just a neat idea at this point. It can easily change in the mean-time.</div> </div> </div> </div>2 years is a generous timetable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T15:06:36-07:00","id":1253390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1236126#post1236126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of feel that Legendary Size, particularly if it's accessible at Essence 1, <i>needs</i> to be expensive to be balanced. The benefits of Legendary Size are pretty extensive:<br /> 1) You can't be crashed except by very big attacks (10+ <i>post soak</i> damage pools),<br /> 2) You can't take more than (attacker's Str)+3 levels of damage (before charms).<br /> 3) You can't be grappled, and your own grappling attacks are made unopposed, barring special magic that makes the opponent capable of grappling huge creatures.<br /> 4) You don't take onslaught penalties to your defense from smaller creatures.<br /> 5) You can't be smashed or knocked back.<br /> <br /> All of that is <i>pretty potent</i>. That said, I could see it getting less impressive at higher Essence. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12730_4.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12730\" data-vbnamecard=\"12730\">PneumaPilot</a> , was there anything in the playtest document you noticed about making the Legendary Size charm cheaper at higher Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>It worries me, not that the initial investment is high (warstriders cost 15m), but you can start with a warstrider, sure it's expensive but as far as I know it doesn't penalize your mote recovery heavily for it's use. The only reason that cost makes sense to me is that Warstriders require a Greater Hearthstone to be implanted into them to get them to run, but you're talking a warstrider versus a legendary sized animal. Now I don't know much about Tyrant Lizards, but I don't imagine that they require a greater hearthstone implanted in them to live.<br /> <br /> So if it's not because of the hearthstone then it might be to constrict the rate that Lunars gain motes, but it's handled in a weird way. I thought Lunar shapeshifting was supposed to be a one-and-done thing, but it seems that Lunars strain to maintain the size of larger creatures? Thematically it kind of feels like it takes away from things a bit.<br /> <br /> I realize that a Legendarily sized creature is great and all, but it sounds like it costs basically all of your charms to do so which sounds like<b> the more combat charms you have the worse of a trade it is.</b> It's a good way to cheaply make say a No Moon scary with minimal investment into combat, but why would someone who has lots of combat charms want to use it? They simply will have no mote economy, and that's a pretty big deal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Someone mentioned using the creatures die pools as a reason for the high cost, but here's the thing: <b>High die pools doesn't necessarily equate to legendary size</b>, there's bound to be animals with really good die pools that just don't have legendary size. So the only thing you can reasonably charge for on Legendary Size is the cost of the merit itself, since a Warstrider gets things like a lot of free damage boxes with minimal investment, devastating actions, and evocations.<br /> <br /> It seems really counter-intuitive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Side question:</b><br /> Are Lunars still +1personal/+4peripheral per essence still (Same as Deebs)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 09-11-2018, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T16:52:23-07:00","id":1253415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253390#post1253390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It worries me, not that the initial investment is high (warstriders cost 15m), but you can start with a warstrider, sure it's expensive but as far as I know it doesn't penalize your mote recovery heavily for it's use. The only reason that cost makes sense to me is that Warstriders require a Greater Hearthstone to be implanted into them to get them to run,</div> </div> </div> </div>That <i>does </i>penalize your mote recovery, though, compared to someone who's bought another Artifact 5 and a greater Hearthstone, because the warstrider pilot doesn't get the benefit of the hearthstone while it's plugged into the warstrider. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Lunar shapeshifting was supposed to be a one-and-done thing, but it seems that Lunars strain to maintain the size of larger creatures?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, it seems to me that the devs are having to balance three desires that are, to a greater or lesser extent, conflicting. First, people want legendary-size creatures available as spirit shapes. It's too cool not to be able to say &quot;My <i>real</i> form is a TYRANT LIZARD! RAR!&quot; and blow the roof off the teahouse where someone just spilled your jasmine tea on your new tunic. Second, people want these forms to be useful in combat, and to <i>feel</i> like you're the actual creature in question, not just a cheap knockoff. If you can transform into a tyrant lizard, but you're only 8 feet tall and your bite isn't that much better than someone with a daiklaive, people are going to get upset. And, finally, there's the desire for people who <i>don't</i> choose such an enormous spirit shape to not be completely left behind, combat-wise. It shouldn't be a massive penalty to have a hummingbird as a spirit shape, as opposed to the tyrant lizard.<br /> <br /> Given the need to satisfy these desires, something's got to give, mechanically. If maintaining a full Legendary Size tyrant lizard form is something a character can do <i>in addition</i> to a bunch of other Lunar combat charms, well, it's going to suck to be a <i>non</i>-Legendary Size form, because they're getting a bunch of huge combat bonuses that you probably just can't access, in addition to whatever combat charms you've got. So, we get what's been presented: you can turn into a Legendary Sized creature, and indeed maintain it indefinitely, but you can't throw a bunch of other combat charms on top of it and still maintain it forever. Note that you <i>can</i> throw a bunch of combat charms! It just reduces the duration you can maintain the form. And, in fact, since it's slightly <i>less</i> than the mote-regeneration rate, you can actually build up your reserves again, and potentially unleash your fight-ending wombo-combo if you want, you just need to wait a bit to do so, doing &quot;nothing&quot; except being a gigantic beast stomping around the battlefield who's almost impossible to significantly hinder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>EDIT:</b> Someone mentioned using the creatures die pools as a reason for the high cost, but here's the thing: <b>High die pools doesn't necessarily equate to legendary size</b>, there's bound to be animals with really good die pools that just don't have legendary size.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that you'll be hard-pressed to find animals with the combination of good die pools, good damage, and good soak/hardness that a Legendary Size creature has. In the core book, for example, of the seven creatures with Legendary Size, only three (the ox-dragon, the siege lizard, and the yeddim) have less than 9 dice for their most damaging attack (and those three all have 7 or 8 dice, which is <i>not</i> nothing), and all except the yeddim have damage rolls of 15+, with minimum damage that starts at 3 and goes up. All of them have soak of 10+ (20 in the case of the siege lizard!). And all except the emperor sloth, ox-dragon, and tyrant lizard have hardness 10. <br /> <br /> Compare all that to the other animals - some get comparable dice to roll for the attack, or damage, but very few get minimum damage (I only count two that do), and soak rarely goes above about 6, and hardness is usually limited to about 2 or 3, if they get it at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T22:25:04-07:00","id":1253492,"title":"","content":"The other issue with comparing the Legendary Size Lunar charm to a Warstrider is that they have very different accessibility issues.<br /> <br /> Putting on a Warstrider requires doing the following:<br /> <br /> 1. Going to where the Warstrider currently is.<br /> 2. Inserting a Greater Hearthstone into the socket.<br /> 3. Suiting up, which takes ten minutes and help from another person. Charms can potentially get it down to one minute or ten combat rounds. I don\u2019t know that I\u2019ve been in a 3e combat that\u2019s lasted ten rounds.<br /> 4. Once you\u2019ve suited up, walked back to the fight, and done any mopping up that might be required (because, as noted, the fight is probably already over by now), you\u2019ll have to spend an hour maintaining the thing which requires a large wagon\u2019s worth of supplies and tools that you\u2019re carrying around in addition to the Warstrider.<br /> <br /> The Lunar charm presumably requires doing the following:<br /> <br /> 1. Spend a single combat action to turn into Gojira. <br /> 2. Proceed to rampage through the area with abandon and collapse the Manse housing the Warstrider on top of the guy still trying to boot up the Dynatherm Connection Sequence.<br /> 3. ????<br /> 4. Profit!<br /> <br /> So, yeah. The Warstrider has a fair number of advantages over a Tyrant Lizard...but being able to turn into a Tyrant Lizard anytime you want has a fair number of advantages on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T22:26:53-07:00","id":1253493,"title":"","content":"Also, I\u2019m pretty sure they said on the podcast that there was a higher essence upgrade that removed the 4m per turn cost of the base charm. So, that\u2019ll be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T22:28:34-07:00","id":1253494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253415#post1253415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That <i>does </i>penalize your mote recovery, though, compared to someone who's bought another Artifact 5 and a greater Hearthstone, because the warstrider pilot doesn't get the benefit of the hearthstone while it's plugged into the warstrider.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, Hearthstones don't generate additional motes in combat, so you're not really losing out on anything unless you're talking about your out of combat regeneration, which is okay fine. But as far as I know, a Lunar with a hearthstone doesn't get to offset these costs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253415#post1253415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, it seems to me that the devs are having to balance three desires that are, to a greater or lesser extent, conflicting. First, people want legendary-size creatures available as spirit shapes. It's too cool not to be able to say &quot;My <i>real</i> form is a TYRANT LIZARD! RAR!&quot; and blow the roof off the teahouse where someone just spilled your jasmine tea on your new tunic. Second, people want these forms to be useful in combat, and to <i>feel</i> like you're the actual creature in question, not just a cheap knockoff. If you can transform into a tyrant lizard, but you're only 8 feet tall and your bite isn't that much better than someone with a daiklaive, people are going to get upset. And, finally, there's the desire for people who <i>don't</i> choose such an enormous spirit shape to not be completely left behind, combat-wise. It shouldn't be a massive penalty to have a hummingbird as a spirit shape, as opposed to the tyrant lizard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the problem is that while these forms may be useful in combat, they inhibit charm usage due to ruining your mote economy. Give how much everyone and their mother says you should be very careful about letting exalts get more motes per turn in recovery, I'd imagine that the same goes for gaining less. The problem with lowing the mote economy is that you cannot sustain many other combat charms other than your giant size. Which unless you want Kaiju Lunars to have all the depth of one charm, I don't see it working too well.<br /> <br /> Also, that last point is sort of irrelevant as there's a charm to make a smaller form massive, so that doesn't really apply. You can also take those forms at a later date without issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253415#post1253415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the need to satisfy these desires, something's got to give, mechanically. If maintaining a full Legendary Size tyrant lizard form is something a character can do <i>in addition</i> to a bunch of other Lunar combat charms, well, it's going to suck to be a <i>non</i>-Legendary Size form, because they're getting a bunch of huge combat bonuses that you probably just can't access, in addition to whatever combat charms you've got. So, we get what's been presented: you can turn into a Legendary Sized creature, and indeed maintain it indefinitely, but you can't throw a bunch of other combat charms on top of it and still maintain it forever. Note that you <i>can</i> throw a bunch of combat charms! It just reduces the duration you can maintain the form. And, in fact, since it's slightly <i>less</i> than the mote-regeneration rate, you can actually build up your reserves again, and potentially unleash your fight-ending wombo-combo if you want, you just need to wait a bit to do so, doing &quot;nothing&quot; except being a gigantic beast stomping around the battlefield who's almost impossible to significantly hinder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean a 15 mote commitment is already pretty hefty investment. 4m a turn is just excessive in my eyes. And no, you cannot keep throwing combat charms, and you cannot regenerate it in a reasonable time span. 1m/turn is pitiful, that's only 20% the base rate.<br /> <br /> Also, the thing is, with <b>huge combat bonuses</b> the bonuses are more meaningful the <b>less</b> invested you are into combat. This means that as far as combat viability goes, this one charm far out does any other individual charm, whilst at the same time interfering with any other charms too. So this creates a new problem instead: <b>Non-Combat focused characters get the most benefit</b> from the current way it works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253415#post1253415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that you'll be hard-pressed to find animals with the combination of good die pools, good damage, and good soak/hardness that a Legendary Size creature has. In the core book, for example, of the seven creatures with Legendary Size, only three (the ox-dragon, the siege lizard, and the yeddim) have less than 9 dice for their most damaging attack (and those three all have 7 or 8 dice, which is <i>not</i> nothing), and all except the yeddim have damage rolls of 15+, with minimum damage that starts at 3 and goes up. All of them have soak of 10+ (20 in the case of the siege lizard!). And all except the emperor sloth, ox-dragon, and tyrant lizard have hardness 10.<br /> <br /> Compare all that to the other animals - some get comparable dice to roll for the attack, or damage, but very few get minimum damage (I only count two that do), and soak rarely goes above about 6, and hardness is usually limited to about 2 or 3, if they get it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, again, <b>characters who already have really good die pools get less benefit</b> than those with very small die pools. However, the main thing is that if you can find a really good &quot;normal&quot; sized animal with amazing die pools or abilities, you can mix those <b>considerably more easily</b> with lunar combat charms. Even then, the more animals that are printed, the more options there will be for a non-legendary size animal that's amazing. Which means you gotta make non-legendary sized animals non-threatening for meta concerns so Lunars cannot take them, or you will inevitably make a powerful non-legendary size animal that's far lower cost will beat whatever benefits you get out of a Kaiju lunar.<br /> <br /> <br /> The issue I have is that, in short, the worse you are at combat, the better Kaiju lunar is, as you will have no room for any other supplemental charms, and massive die pool bonuses only are meaningful if your die pools aren't large already.<br /> <br /> It's concerning, because this sounds like it'll become the DBT meta... again. Why? Because shapeshifting into animals is already restricting you to essentially Lunar charms and maybe armor evocations, further restricting it to nothing but raw die pools and monster attacks seems like it'll make it non-viable in the long run. Compared to DBT, which gets everything, on top of a nice power boost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253492#post1253492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other issue with comparing the Legendary Size Lunar charm to a Warstrider is that they have very different accessibility issues.<br /> <br /> Putting on a Warstrider requires doing the following:<br /> <br /> 1. Going to where the Warstrider currently is.<br /> 2. Inserting a Greater Hearthstone into the socket.<br /> 3. Suiting up, which takes ten minutes and help from another person. Charms can potentially get it down to one minute or ten combat rounds. I don\u2019t know that I\u2019ve been in a 3e combat that\u2019s lasted ten rounds.<br /> 4. Once you\u2019ve suited up, walked back to the fight, and done any mopping up that might be required (because, as noted, the fight is probably already over by now), you\u2019ll have to spend an hour maintaining the thing which requires a large wagon\u2019s worth of supplies and tools that you\u2019re carrying around in addition to the Warstrider.<br /> <br /> The Lunar charm presumably requires doing the following:<br /> <br /> 1. Spend a single combat action to turn into Gojira.<br /> 2. Proceed to rampage through the area with abandon and collapse the Manse housing the Warstrider on top of the guy still trying to boot up the Dynatherm Connection Sequence.<br /> 3. ????<br /> 4. Profit!<br /> <br /> So, yeah. The Warstrider has a fair number of advantages over a Tyrant Lizard...but being able to turn into a Tyrant Lizard anytime you want has a fair number of advantages on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, I'm just stating that they're not a 1:1. From what I know the Lunar does not inherit the health boxes of the creature they turn into, whereas a Warstrider always has something like 25+ boxes. In terms of investment to get a Warstrider, it's a 5 dot artifact, and a 4 dot hearthstone, versus a charm to get the creature, and several charms to get the health on par with the creature.<br /> <br /> So Warstrider's cheaper, but generally more powerful, but it's more fiddly to use. Okay, fine. I think that's a good trade off.<br /> <br /> Then you add an additional 4m tax and I think that's where it becomes excessive. Sure if it can be removed at high essence with another charm that makes it less problematic... but by then Kaiju's probably fallen off a bit and if you're focused on combat, you'll probably have invested resources into charms or evocations that don't work in Kaiju/animal form.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, it goes back to what I said before, the characters who can use it best are those who aren't focused on combat. Changing and No Moons probably get the most mileage out of it, which is counter intuitive, at least to me. They have more opportunities to get it into places where it can do the most damage, but the combat-focused full moon is probably going to get little benefit out of it since they're probably actually good at fighting natively (Thus going from 10 to 14 dice isn't as large of a difference than going from say 6 to 14 dice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 09-12-2018, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T00:06:03-07:00","id":1253511,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, dice bonuses due to using animal stats count as bonuses from charms. So, a non-combat Lunar might not be able to use a Tyrant Lizard to the fullest.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also the question of \u201cHow did you get this form anyway?\u201d A non-combat focused Lunar prolly isn\u2019t going to take a Tyrant Lizard as their totem and the other main way to gain forms requires that you hunt and kill the animal in question, which is certainly not an easy fight and might be impossible if you\u2019re not combat focused.<br /> <br /> Another consideration is that these forms are ...well, of Legendary Size. They\u2019re huge. If turning into a Kaiju is your only combat trick, then a fight indoors or one where you don\u2019t want to reveal yourself as a Shapeshifting Monster will create complications. <br /> <br /> Another aspect of Lunars is that they\u2019re adaptable. Solars tend to come at you with overwhelming power, capable of using all their might together at once. Lunars seem like they\u2019re the ones with all the options. If one option doesn\u2019t work, they\u2019ll just try another one. So, even if it\u2019s hard to use a complex combat suite together with a Kaiju form, it sounds like having both options isn\u2019t that hard to get and having a big hammer in the toolbox is never useless.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, I think we\u2019ll just need to wait and see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T02:18:00-07:00","id":1253524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253511#post1253511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly, dice bonuses due to using animal stats count as bonuses from charms. So, a non-combat Lunar might not be able to use a Tyrant Lizard to the fullest.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also the question of \u201cHow did you get this form anyway?\u201d A non-combat focused Lunar prolly isn\u2019t going to take a Tyrant Lizard as their totem and the other main way to gain forms requires that you hunt and kill the animal in question, which is certainly not an easy fight and might be impossible if you\u2019re not combat focused.<br /> <br /> Another consideration is that these forms are ...well, of Legendary Size. They\u2019re huge. If turning into a Kaiju is your only combat trick, then a fight indoors or one where you don\u2019t want to reveal yourself as a Shapeshifting Monster will create complications.<br /> <br /> Another aspect of Lunars is that they\u2019re adaptable. Solars tend to come at you with overwhelming power, capable of using all their might together at once. Lunars seem like they\u2019re the ones with all the options. If one option doesn\u2019t work, they\u2019ll just try another one. So, even if it\u2019s hard to use a complex combat suite together with a Kaiju form, it sounds like having both options isn\u2019t that hard to get and having a big hammer in the toolbox is never useless.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, I think we\u2019ll just need to wait and see.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm unsure how you'd calculate if it's beyond what you can add from dice. Guessing there'd be a metric. But as Lunars can add most any attribute on top of the most obvious one, getting to the full bonus is probably still possible. That's assuming you're not just given those dice even if it goes past your excellency capacity.<br /> <br /> I mean there are other ways to gain a form other than fighting and killing this, that's already been established. So a Lunar can gain forms by playing to their strengths.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you're playing someone who relies on their Kaiju as their stick, then they're probably very focused on being good with the carrot. As combat's usually a last resort in such cases, what does it matter at that point?<br /> <br /> The problem with lots of options is that takes lots of investment, and that's a lot harder to ask of someone to do to be equally good in human form, DBT, and Kaiju. I mean sure it's possible, but nobody has endless XP, so to achieve it it'd come at the cost of... everything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T03:02:50-07:00","id":1253532,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m wondering what the Charm investment for Daikaiju Combat vs DBT is? If it\u2019s shallow in the Charm tree, there isn\u2019t any reason you couldn\u2019t take both and round out your character as well. (Which is a scary thought)<br /> <br /> I mean, you wouldn\u2019t use all of it at once of course, but having an anti battle group and close quarter form at character creation seems to play to the Lunar\u2019s versatility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 09-12-2018, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T08:58:49-07:00","id":1253601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253524#post1253524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm unsure how you'd calculate if it's beyond what you can add from dice. Guessing there'd be a metric. But as Lunars can add most any attribute on top of the most obvious one, getting to the full bonus is probably still possible. That's assuming you're not just given those dice even if it goes past your excellency capacity.<br /> <br /> I mean there are other ways to gain a form other than fighting and killing this, that's already been established. So a Lunar can gain forms by playing to their strengths.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you're playing someone who relies on their Kaiju as their stick, then they're probably very focused on being good with the carrot. As combat's usually a last resort in such cases, what does it matter at that point?<br /> <br /> The problem with lots of options is that takes lots of investment, and that's a lot harder to ask of someone to do to be equally good in human form, DBT, and Kaiju. I mean sure it's possible, but nobody has endless XP, so to achieve it it'd come at the cost of... everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that the dice cap is just [Attribute] when it comes to shapeshifting. So if you've got Dex 3 normally, you only get Dex 6 at maximum from whatever form you turn into. While you're in that form you can stunt using str to boost your dex, but I think then extra dice would then have to come from your normal excellency rather than from the form. Best to Ask the Devs on this one.<br /> <br /> Regardless, your abilities remain the same. If you have brawl 1, you still suck at brawl as a kaiju, regardless of what the original creature could do. I feel like you're making a mountain out of a molehill with this whole 'non-combat focused people get the most benefit' because I really don't think they get as much as you imply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T09:13:45-07:00","id":1253613,"title":"","content":"I asked Vance a year ago about excellencies, but I just checked again to make sure it hadn't changed:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>When I asked you a year ago Vance, you said Lunar excellencies are based on the Lunar's own stats (though you hadn't quite decided about Strength to damage and Stamina to soak).</i><br /> <i>So if you have Dex 4, then you can use the Dex excellency to add 4 dice to your attack whether in the form of a turtle or a tiger or a tyrant lizard (unlike in 2nd ed, where if their dice pool was bigger than yours it took away from your dice cap).</i><br /> <br /> <i>Is that still true?</i></div> </div> </div> </div><i><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep.</div> </div> </div> </div></i><br /> <br /> Also, he said you can use their dice pool if it's better than the animals.<br /> <br /> So, I'd say having a big animal form for combat is a slightly better investment for low-dice pool Lunars, as they're increasing their dice pool more, but a Lunar with a big natural set of attributes is still going to be a more dangerous Tyrant Lizard as she can add more dice.<br /> Also, while you're in the form of, say, a bear, a Lunar with better natural pools in some areas (say, combat movement, which bears don't have such a good dice pool in) would have better dice pools than a bear normally does.<br /> <br /> So in the end I don't think it's a big issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m wondering what the Charm investment for Daikaiju Combat vs DBT is? If it\u2019s shallow in the Charm tree, there isn\u2019t any reason you couldn\u2019t take both and round out your character as well. (Which is a scary thought)</div> </div> </div> </div>As they're both things you can take at character gen, I expect both of them to have minimal investment. I suspect DBT will simply require HBT and Strength 3 or 4, and the charm for taking Legendary size creatures will probably have 0-3 prereqs, all Essence 1, and require Strength or Stamina 3 or 4.<br /> <br /> The Essence 4 charm to ignore the 4m per turn cost of being in Legendary Size, however, I expect to have a lot of investment required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T09:51:25-07:00","id":1253628,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if Towering Beast Form had a Strength 5 minimum, because it\u2019s clearly the Charm choice for someone interested in maxing out Strength beyond Strength.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a niche Charm that not even all characters based on brute strength will want to learn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T10:41:29-07:00","id":1253642,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't think so, because it's a charm that needs to be taken for certain character concepts. If your character is a Roc-totem sailor who got lost at sea and had various adventures, or a big fat whale-sage, or a slow-but-tough Yeddim-lady, or the elephant colonialist King of the jungle, you <i>need</i> that charm.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say the rules won't say you have to have Strength 5, but I'd expect 3 or 4.<br /> <br /> Or possibly it'll have the Totem charm, and let you take it with a lower attribute if you have a Legendary Size totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T11:17:18-07:00","id":1253651,"title":"","content":"Why would a whale lord, a yeddim lady, or an elephant man NOT have Strength 5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T11:54:11-07:00","id":1253657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253651#post1253651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a whale lord, a yeddim lady, or an elephant man NOT have Strength 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they ALSO want Stamina 5 and ran out of attribute dots at chargen?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T12:38:53-07:00","id":1253666,"title":"","content":"Also, generally speaking I don't think it's good for the game to force people to start with 5s via charm prerequisites. I'm sure the upgrades will be Strength 5, and that's fine, but I don't think all elephant-totem Lunars should need Strength 5.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you're playing a Ganeshi-Elephant-Sage, with great wisdom, not to mention that Elephants never forget, then you might well be mental primary and physical tertiary. Which is maybe 7 dots? (Might be 6, like Solars, but I heard Lunars get a fat 9/7/5.)<br /> So if you need Strength 5, you'll have maybe Stamina 3 and Dexterity 2. Which is not, like, terrible. But I don't see it as something the game should demand.<br /> I think Strength 4 is fine, for an Essence 1 charm that probably doesn't have many prerequisites.<br /> <br /> Or it could be, say, Strength 5 but if you have a totem with Legendary Size you can take it at Stamina 3, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T12:42:23-07:00","id":1253669,"title":"","content":"There are multiple ways to express the mythical archetypes associated with any animal. Ex3 is moving away from one true builds for Lunar and part of that is the freedom to do whatever you want. <br /> <br /> Towering Beast Form is probably the first charm in the tree so it's easy for people to snag their totem and move on. It costs that much to use because it comes with a lot of benefits at essence 1and like 1 or 2 charms deep right out of the gate. It's not going to autowin a fight, but it definitely sends a message and provides tons of shapeshifting stunt-fodder.<br /> <br /> Unless I've misread the clarifications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":717,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","user":"Monghani","date":". 09-12-2018, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T12:44:36-07:00","id":1253670,"title":"","content":"Doublepost!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":717,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","user":"Monghani","date":". 09-12-2018, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T15:48:41-07:00","id":1253730,"title":"","content":"Re: Legendary Size, yes, it <i>is </i>pretty good, although not as great against Exalted-scale foes as one might hope. This is based off playing a Solar sorceress who did a working to allow her to assume such a large form (only in the Wyld or in an uncapped Demense she owned, although she could maintain it away from those places so long as she was prepared to be huge); Lunars would have even easier access so the mote tax is fairly important, I'd say. Warstriders have more setup but Legendary Size is really the least of their benefits; if you're investing into evocations at all the evocations of the striders in <i>Arms</i> are of far more interest.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T18:03:53-07:00","id":1253758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253601#post1253601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that the dice cap is just [Attribute] when it comes to shapeshifting. So if you've got Dex 3 normally, you only get Dex 6 at maximum from whatever form you turn into. While you're in that form you can stunt using str to boost your dex, but I think then extra dice would then have to come from your normal excellency rather than from the form. Best to Ask the Devs on this one.<br /> <br /> Regardless, your abilities remain the same. If you have brawl 1, you still suck at brawl as a kaiju, regardless of what the original creature could do. I feel like you're making a mountain out of a molehill with this whole 'non-combat focused people get the most benefit' because I really don't think they get as much as you imply.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I know, you can just use the attack pool of the animal you take the form of, as well as their soak, damage totals, etc. When Vance says you calculate using excellency well that has some issues innately: First is calculating where the creature's die pools come from so you know how to properly account for it (do they get the +4/+5 because it's an unarmed attack?) and it may just mean you cannot excellency if it's higher than what you normally could excellency.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253613#post1253613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked Vance a year ago about excellencies, but I just checked again to make sure it hadn't changed:<br /> <br /> [/I]<br /> <br /> Also, he said you can use their dice pool if it's better than the animals.<br /> <br /> So, I'd say having a big animal form for combat is a slightly better investment for low-dice pool Lunars, as they're increasing their dice pool more, but a Lunar with a big natural set of attributes is still going to be a more dangerous Tyrant Lizard as she can add more dice.<br /> Also, while you're in the form of, say, a bear, a Lunar with better natural pools in some areas (say, combat movement, which bears don't have such a good dice pool in) would have better dice pools than a bear normally does.<br /> <br /> So in the end I don't think it's a big issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> As they're both things you can take at character gen, I expect both of them to have minimal investment. I suspect DBT will simply require HBT and Strength 3 or 4, and the charm for taking Legendary size creatures will probably have 0-3 prereqs, all Essence 1, and require Strength or Stamina 3 or 4.<br /> <br /> The Essence 4 charm to ignore the 4m per turn cost of being in Legendary Size, however, I expect to have a lot of investment required.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there lies the issue: The combat focused person who wants to boost their stats with an excellency will find they don't get anywhere near enough motes to work with. Whereas, someone getting upscaled by having poor die pools to begin with will not have any problems because it's not like they were going to have much of an excellency anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T18:39:54-07:00","id":1253765,"title":"","content":"I recall seeing that grappling rolls are unopposed against Legendary Sized Creatures by mortal sized Exalted. Also the Tyrant Lizard has some nice tricks in the grapple department. <br /> <br /> Unopposable Combat Style that deals oodles of Damage, I wonder if it might be a legit combat style for them?<br /> <br /> Edit: Regarding Daikaiju and the endurance of mote drip in fights, I always recall when playing Lunars in 2nd ed, they had powerful effects (more powerful than Solars sometimes) but were nowhere near as efficient. <br /> <br /> With perfect/paranoia combat, this was an inherent weakness, but with that aspect gone, I look forward to something similar in 3rd Ed. Frighteningly deadly effects that activate quickly but are expensive. <br /> <br /> Maybe, we\u2019ll see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 09-12-2018, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T19:12:38-07:00","id":1253771,"title":"","content":"My understanding of this is that, if the animal has, say, a feat of strength die pool of 7, then a Lunar with Str 3 and Ath 0 can only use 6 dice of that pool, a Lunar with Str 3 and Ath 1 has hit their dice cap, a Lunar with Str 3 and Ath 3 can only add 2 dice, and a Lunar with Str 3 and Ath 4 or 5 can add their full 3 dice to the pool.<br /> <br /> Basically, animals act sorta like scene length dice adders but can\u2019t break the cap. That said, because animals just have a pool of dice, you can buy up the correct ability to free up more excellency dice instead of boosting an Attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T19:17:54-07:00","id":1253772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253771#post1253771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding of this is that, if the animal has, say, a feat of strength die pool of 7, then a Lunar with Str 3 and Ath 0 can only use 6 dice of that pool, a Lunar with Str 3 and Ath 1 has hit their dice cap, a Lunar with Str 3 and Ath 3 can only add 2 dice, and a Lunar with Str 3 and Ath 4 or 5 can add their full 3 dice to the pool.<br /> <br /> Basically, animals act sorta like scene length dice adders but can\u2019t break the cap. That said, because animals just have a pool of dice, you can buy up the correct ability to free up more excellency dice instead of boosting an Attribute.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do the dice cap take into consideration the second attribute you can get on a stunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T19:45:52-07:00","id":1253775,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that a Lunar enjoys an animal form's FULL DICE POOLS, even if that would break their dice-adding limit. The trade-off being that they can't add any more dice to such pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T19:51:59-07:00","id":1253777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253775#post1253775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that a Lunar enjoys an animal form's FULL DICE POOLS, even if that would break their dice-adding limit. The trade-off being that they can't add any more dice to such pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the current discussion in the ask the devs thread, this does not seem to be the case.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ah, no, you are correct. I saw pool and thought Cap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 09-12-2018, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T20:19:56-07:00","id":1253782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253775#post1253775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that a Lunar enjoys an animal form's FULL DICE POOLS, even if that would break their dice-adding limit. The trade-off being that they can't add any more dice to such pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Confusingly (I apologise) it appears I was right the first time:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1253780#post1253780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dex 3, Brawl 3 Lunar has a default dice cap of +3 on attacks. Her normal attack pool is 6, +3 Charm dice brings that up to 9. 11 is higher than 9. She only rolls nine dice to attack, because she can't go over her dice limit.<br /> <br /> Dex 5, Brawl 5 Lunar has a default dice cap of +5 on attacks. Her normal attack pool is 10, +5 Charm dice brings that up to 15. 11 is lower than 15. She rolls 11 dice for attacks, and could add up to +4 more with the Dexterity Excellency or other Charms.<br /> <br /> (Stunting might change the above math)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 09-12-2018, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T06:25:15-07:00","id":1253856,"title":"","content":"I personally wouldn't compare kaiju form to a warstrider, but to a supernal Survival Solar with such a familiar.<br /> <br /> I would hope that a Lunar who invests in kicking ass as a Tyrant Lizard is not <i>vastly</i> outperformed by a Solar who invests in kicking ass alongside his or her Tyrant Lizard pet. Currently playing such a Solar and looking at those Lunar dice caps, plus knowing the survival &amp; ride charms I doubt the Lunar will actually compare favorably to a Solar's familiar. <br /> <br /> And then of course the Solar him- or herself can still take actions and the comparison could turn really ugly?<br /> <br /> Of course I hope this is not the case, but it might be worth playtesting. Not measuring up to a pet would suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T06:52:24-07:00","id":1253862,"title":"","content":"I'm just confused by how animal dice pools and their caps work at this point, so I'm not going to comment on that...<br /> <br /> I will just say though:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always recall when playing Lunars in 2nd ed, they had powerful effects (more powerful than Solars sometimes) but were nowhere near as efficient. </div> </div> </div> </div>I actually found them the other way, because they had so many really cheap scene-long buffs (based on either Gift or Fury-okay stuff). But on individual attacks, they couldn't throw so much in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T08:04:42-07:00","id":1253886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253758#post1253758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I know, you can just use the attack pool of the animal you take the form of, as well as their soak, damage totals, etc. When Vance says you calculate using excellency well that has some issues innately: First is calculating where the creature's die pools come from so you know how to properly account for it (do they get the +4/+5 because it's an unarmed attack?) and it may just mean you cannot excellency if it's higher than what you normally could excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually mistaken in what I was thinking the stats would be.<br /> <br /> You just use the QC stats of the animal with no distinction between Attribute, ability or accuracy bonuses. This makes things much faster in play as you simply need to know your character's maximum dice pool with excellency cap and you compare that to the form's pool. <br /> <br /> This approach does have some drawbacks, however. Let's use the example of the Quoll-Lion:<br /> <br /> 1. as I confirmed in the Ask the Devs thread, your ability is equally important to your dice cap when calculating how much excellency you can throw at a problem while in a form. So with the Quoll-Lion form which has a bite (7 dice [ damage 14]) and a claw (11 dice [damage 10]) attacks, if you were playing a lunar with Dex 5, brawl 1, your normal dice cap would be 11 dice. This means you'd be at your cap for the claw attack but be able to boost your bite attack up to 11 as well. A lunar with Dex 5, Brawl 3, on the other hand. Would have a cap of 13 dice, so this second lunar would be able to boost up both attacks to 13 dice. Now you can look at this two ways. Either this means that the lunar is capped based on what their ability is, or as I've come to view it, the first lunar is simply compensating for their lack of of skill by building excellency use into the transformation. <br /> <br /> 2. Accuracy becomes an issue. If we look at the Quoll-Lion, it's two attacks can be matched exactly by a melee combatant with str 3, Dex 5 and brawl 2 using a light weapon (claw) and a heavy weapon (bite) both mortal. However, a lunar in their own form with such a build would be:<br /> <br /> Dex 5, str 3, Brawl 2, heavy weapon (7 dice [14 damage]) (no-stunt die cap: 12)<br /> Dex 5, str 3, brawl 2, light weapon (11 dice [10 damage]) (<b>no-stunt die cap: 16</b>)<br /> <br /> vs Quoll-Lion<br /> <br /> Bite (7 dice [damage 14]) (lunar form die cap: 12)<br /> claw (11 dice [damage 10]) (<b>lunar form die cap: 12</b>)<br /> <br /> Notice the difference here? Accuracy from weapons is normally non-charm dice, but when using QC stats there's no way to effectively separate it out and thus everything above your base stats is counted as dice from charms.<br /> <br /> This one I'm not sure is easy to explain away, but it does provide a tradeoff - you get the extra accuracy for free. You're still rolling 11 dice without spending any motes. The tradeoff is that you simply <i>cannot</i> achieve the same dice pools that you could if you were using a light weapon. The one thing I'm not sure on, though, is damage. Vance has stated that you can use your own pools if they're better than the form's but does this include damage? Can you use the form's 11 dice accuracy and then if you had str 5, would your damage be 12 since that's your regular unarmed damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T14:44:28-07:00","id":1254010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1253886#post1253886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually mistaken in what I was thinking the stats would be.<br /> <br /> You just use the QC stats of the animal with no distinction between Attribute, ability or accuracy bonuses. This makes things much faster in play as you simply need to know your character's maximum dice pool with excellency cap and you compare that to the form's pool.<br /> <br /> This approach does have some drawbacks, however. Let's use the example of the Quoll-Lion:<br /> <br /> 1. as I confirmed in the Ask the Devs thread, your ability is equally important to your dice cap when calculating how much excellency you can throw at a problem while in a form. So with the Quoll-Lion form which has a bite (7 dice [ damage 14]) and a claw (11 dice [damage 10]) attacks, if you were playing a lunar with Dex 5, brawl 1, your normal dice cap would be 11 dice. This means you'd be at your cap for the claw attack but be able to boost your bite attack up to 11 as well. A lunar with Dex 5, Brawl 3, on the other hand. Would have a cap of 13 dice, so this second lunar would be able to boost up both attacks to 13 dice. Now you can look at this two ways. Either this means that the lunar is capped based on what their ability is, or as I've come to view it, the first lunar is simply compensating for their lack of of skill by building excellency use into the transformation.<br /> <br /> 2. Accuracy becomes an issue. If we look at the Quoll-Lion, it's two attacks can be matched exactly by a melee combatant with str 3, Dex 5 and brawl 2 using a light weapon (claw) and a heavy weapon (bite) both mortal. However, a lunar in their own form with such a build would be:<br /> <br /> Dex 5, str 3, Brawl 2, heavy weapon (7 dice [14 damage]) (no-stunt die cap: 12)<br /> Dex 5, str 3, brawl 2, light weapon (11 dice [10 damage]) (<b>no-stunt die cap: 16</b>)<br /> <br /> vs Quoll-Lion<br /> <br /> Bite (7 dice [damage 14]) (lunar form die cap: 12)<br /> claw (11 dice [damage 10]) (<b>lunar form die cap: 12</b>)<br /> <br /> Notice the difference here? Accuracy from weapons is normally non-charm dice, but when using QC stats there's no way to effectively separate it out and thus everything above your base stats is counted as dice from charms.<br /> <br /> This one I'm not sure is easy to explain away, but it does provide a tradeoff - you get the extra accuracy for free. You're still rolling 11 dice without spending any motes. The tradeoff is that you simply <i>cannot</i> achieve the same dice pools that you could if you were using a light weapon. The one thing I'm not sure on, though, is damage. Vance has stated that you can use your own pools if they're better than the form's but does this include damage? Can you use the form's 11 dice accuracy and then if you had str 5, would your damage be 12 since that's your regular unarmed damage?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah, that's something that came to my mind and made me a bit worried. Clawstrider is the same way, and with how Lunar excellency seems to be limited to 5 dice, that means you can only ever get up to 5 dice above your natural die pool in animal form which is.. weird (And highly limiting). Honestly I think it'd be easier if it was just &quot;use the die pools of the animal&quot; and if it's over your cap then you can only use stunt+other attribute excellencies. I am <b>hoping</b> that the unarmed accuracy bonus does get added to what the animals to-hit rate is, before calculating whatever the excellency limits are. Else I'm unsure how animals could compete with using manufactured weapons if your accuracy doesn't matter but it does matter in animals (but is entirely unlisted).<br /> <br /> <br /> This also means that if you want to use animal forms for any combat at all you <b>have</b> to have Brawl (Since it doesn't seem to care if you're better at melee because animals cannot use melee and thus don't contribute to the die pool).<br /> <br /> <br /> All of the limitations that animal forms get are making me really lukewarm about them for combat. Making me think that DBT will be the big thing for 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 09-13-2018, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T16:55:04-07:00","id":1254028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1254010#post1254010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the limitations that animal forms get are making me really lukewarm about them for combat. Making me think that DBT will be the big thing for 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair a big chunk of the combat use of animal forms is going to rely on what exactly the protean keyword does for them as far as extra effects.<br /> <br /> I am expecting one or two animal forms to be able to hold their own while the rest fall off into trap options, its unfortunate but a eagle,bear,hellboar,wolf and giant cat are not equal combatants even though they have the same &quot;cost&quot; to shape shift in.<br /> <br /> Though on the note of DBT being the one true build it should be noted that it does lower your evocation resonance a step, so if there is a sweet combo based off of lunar charms and some evocations that might be enough too open a second combat option.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T17:21:58-07:00","id":1254033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1254028#post1254028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair a big chunk of the combat use of animal forms is going to rely on what exactly the protean keyword does for them as far as extra effects.<br /> <br /> I am expecting one or two animal forms to be able to hold their own while the rest fall off into trap options, its unfortunate but a eagle,bear,hellboar,wolf and giant cat are not equal combatants even though they have the same &quot;cost&quot; to shape shift in.<br /> <br /> Though on the note of DBT being the one true build it should be noted that it does lower your evocation resonance a step, so if there is a sweet combo based off of lunar charms and some evocations that might be enough too open a second combat option.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Evocations are designed by the players/GM so it's effect might not even be that strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T17:48:41-07:00","id":1254037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1254033#post1254033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Evocations are designed by the players/GM so it's effect might not even be that strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be but we have all the evocations in the core, arms of the chosen and what else is dropped in lunars proper to work with and I do not think that should be ignored.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T17:59:46-07:00","id":1254039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1254028#post1254028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair a big chunk of the combat use of animal forms is going to rely on what exactly the protean keyword does for them as far as extra effects.<br /> <br /> I am expecting one or two animal forms to be able to hold their own while the rest fall off into trap options, its unfortunate but a eagle,bear,hellboar,wolf and giant cat are not equal combatants even though they have the same &quot;cost&quot; to shape shift in.<br /> <br /> Though on the note of DBT being the one true build it should be noted that it does lower your evocation resonance a step, so if there is a sweet combo based off of lunar charms and some evocations that might be enough too open a second combat option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m thinking what will be on par with DBT, Combat wise, will not be the regular shapes, which might have more specific and specialist utility, but the Kaiju forms, which have the one no-sell grapple trick that I can see basically letting you dominate a single opponent if they don\u2019t have the answer for it. (Solar Brawl or perfect defences at the moment if I am not mistaken)<br /> <br /> Didn\u2019t the form that let you take the Kaiju form also let you do it with all shapes you had? Like Kaiju fieldmouse or Kaiju Scorpion? I wonder how that will work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T18:46:19-07:00","id":1254048,"title":"","content":"It applies the Legendary Merit to any form you're wearing and negates the Tiny/Miniscule Merit if a form has that. It can get pretty insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T18:48:23-07:00","id":1254050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1254048#post1254048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It applies the Legendary Merit to any form you're wearing and negates the Tiny/Miniscule Merit if a form has that. It can get pretty insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm but it might not specifically give the killer grapple called out in existing creatures with the Legendary Size Merit. Troubling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T19:41:14-07:00","id":1254064,"title":"","content":"The problem is that when you're charging so much for Legendary Size, and all the other limitations with animal forms, I'm really concerned this will turn into 2e again where Deadly Beastman Transformation was the meta. This doesn't mean DBT needs more nerfs, this means I'm concerned animals will simply be far far too weak under the proposed rules. Highly limited, less options, etc. sounds like they're going to be pretty meh in combat especially compared to HBT and DBT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T19:46:22-07:00","id":1254065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1254064#post1254064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that when you're charging so much for Legendary Size, and all the other limitations with animal forms, I'm really concerned this will turn into 2e again where Deadly Beastman Transformation was the meta. This doesn't mean DBT needs more nerfs, this means I'm concerned animals will simply be far far too weak under the proposed rules. Highly limited, less options, etc. sounds like they're going to be pretty meh in combat especially compared to HBT and DBT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with the \u201cI Win\u201d grapple strategy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T20:03:48-07:00","id":1254072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1254065#post1254065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even with the \u201cI Win\u201d grapple strategy?</div> </div> </div> </div>If that is the one characteristic that makes legendary size forms applicable in the &quot;meta&quot; then that is not a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T20:11:30-07:00","id":1254075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1254072#post1254072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that is the one characteristic that makes legendary size forms applicable in the &amp;quot;meta&amp;quot; then that is not a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it\u2019s not the only thing Legendary Size gives you. It also makes you real tanky so you can hug people to death in peace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T21:30:25-07:00","id":1254092,"title":"","content":"Whatever world you\u2019re living in where \u201c39 motes left (after activating Towering Beast Form)\u201d = \u201ccan\u2019t use any other charms that fight,\u201d I\u2019d like to stay far away from it thank you very much.<br /> <br /> No accuracy bonus could be a problem, but the way I see it the real strength of animal forms isn\u2019t the dice bonuses, it\u2019s the special attacks and animal merits. So many of those are CRAZY good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T22:37:29-07:00","id":1254101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1254092#post1254092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever world you\u2019re living in where \u201c39 motes left (after activating Towering Beast Form)\u201d = \u201ccan\u2019t use any other charms that fight,\u201d I\u2019d like to stay far away from it thank you very much.<br /> <br /> No accuracy bonus could be a problem, but the way I see it the real strength of animal forms isn\u2019t the dice bonuses, it\u2019s the special attacks and animal merits. So many of those are CRAZY good.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 39 motes with only 20% the base more recovery rate. That's also assuming motes aren't being committed elsewhere which they likely will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T05:28:37-07:00","id":1254145,"title":"","content":"I'm particularly looking forward to the Protean Charisma Charms that will allow Lunars with fowl shapes to automatically succeed at Persuade actions to make people think that the sky is falling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T06:09:32-07:00","id":1254153,"title":"","content":"The reduced mote regen is a huge cost, but all in all, beasties with Legendary Size do come with very nice perks and vastly better stats. To bridge the difference between a wolf or big cat in both defenses, soak, damage and durability, as well as access to special abilities would cost a great deal more than 4 motes per turn imho.<br /> <br /> The lousy accuracy is what makes the animal forms of dubious utility, I fear. <br /> <br /> The familiars of Supernal Survival Solars can compensate by raising their dex by 2 and ability 5, adding in a (cap-breaking?) cha+wisdom super-cheap pseudo excellency and then stack on the successes from Deadly Predator Method, so yeah, hopefully Lunars have other tricks beyond their excellency to improve their accuracy in animal shape.<br /> <br /> Besides applying to be a Solar's familiar obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T09:15:21-07:00","id":1254235,"title":"","content":"If a character lower in the initiative clashes your character and crashes yours, and an initiative shift occurs, do they get to make two follow up attacks? One on the turn of the clash when the shift occurs, and again because they're now at the top of the initiative tracker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T10:05:53-07:00","id":1254246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1254235#post1254235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a character lower in the initiative clashes your character and crashes yours, and an initiative shift occurs, do they get to make two follow up attacks? One on the turn of the clash when the shift occurs, and again because they're now at the top of the initiative tracker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you mean to ask this in this thread? This seems more like an 'Ask a question get an answer' or 'ask the devs' question","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T10:27:28-07:00","id":1254249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1254050#post1254050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm but it might not specifically give the killer grapple called out in existing creatures with the Legendary Size Merit. Troubling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the devs mentioned a little after warstriders were released that the unopposed grapple rule was inherent to legendary size, it just made the most sense to put it near the other grapple rules on each creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23912-scottsman","name":"Scottsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T10:46:10-07:00","id":1254253,"title":"","content":"I think you'll save yourself, and most other people, a lot of headache if you don't compare Supernal Solar purchases to any other splat outside of Abyssals and Infernals. If you're a Lunar you start at essence 1 so, if you must, compare them to Solar and DB charms of essence 1. Also, why are you comparing Familiar charms to self-boosting charms? Right now we just know Lunars have the ability to change their familiars' size, grant them mutations, and given them human intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T06:12:20-07:00","id":1255238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1254253#post1254253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you'll save yourself, and most other people, a lot of headache if you don't compare Supernal Solar purchases to any other splat outside of Abyssals and Infernals. If you're a Lunar you start at essence 1 so, if you must, compare them to Solar and DB charms of essence 1. Also, why are you comparing Familiar charms to self-boosting charms? Right now we just know Lunars have the ability to change their familiars' size, grant them mutations, and given them human intelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the only times I've ever played single-splat is times like these, when we started a campaign and there was only the basic Solar book available. So, yes, I compare with Solars, with their Supernals, because they will be there in the same group as the Lunar and the Dragon Blooded and the game must somehow not unravel and remain fun for all involved.<br /> <br /> From what we've seen planning our next game it's Supernal actually that is causing most of the headaches for multi-splat play. Probably need to give that the boot, or at least some really strict restrictions on what can be taken as Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T06:24:46-07:00","id":1255239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1255238#post1255238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and the game must somehow not unravel and remain fun for all involved....</div> </div> </div> </div>You speak as if supernals are inherently hazardous to any mixed table.<br /> By that logic, wouldn't the same apply to a pure table as well? You just need two characters built differently for the same purpose.<br /> And are you sure it's in supernals the problem? One certainly can achieve lofty heights with it, but how conducive it actually is compared simply to different optimizations? One player can easily be a chump compared to other early in the same-essence charms.<br /> <br /> So... how are you measuring it? How does that separate variables like the supernal flag?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T07:39:14-07:00","id":1255254,"title":"","content":"There is some mild optimizers at my table, so, yes, the players with weakest system-fu get some assistance to avoid true chump builds. The fact that players can start the game with <i>wildly </i>different powerlevels has proven problematic in the past. This issue is not limited to Exalted obviously, but this system certainly exacerbates it, which is by no means a criticism, just stating facts. Not everyone enjoys hunting for synergies among close to 1k charms yet still want to play in the same league.<br /> <br /> Now, back to the issue at hand, no, to be honest I am far from sure that eliminating Supernals will solve anything. After two campaigns, if I look at the sheets, most of the characters would have their Supernal mastered somewhere halfway E3. Some sooner, some later, but that's about the point where they have on of the capstones an the essential Charms. After that they start branching out. <br /> <br /> Now, anyway, at least Supernal makes sure lots of their Charms get sucked into their 'niche', leaving some breathing space at the lower essence levels. Might get tricky around E3 and the Solar's branching out phase, but getting rid of Supernal might make that happen sooner.<br /> <br /> Alternatively strict niche-protection and/or giving everyone the Solar's Supernals and free excellencies might work better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T07:46:20-07:00","id":1255256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1255239#post1255239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but how conducive it actually is compared simply to different optimizations?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but supernal gives you an area to optimise even more. And those players who optimise more will get the most out of it.<br /> <br /> Imagine if Ferocious Lawyer of Statistics takes supernal Resistance and starts the game with stuff like Adamant Skin and Ruin-Abasing Shrug*, while Expositor of Versimillitudian Enjoyment takes Supernal Linguistics, takes 5 Linguistic charms (including Essence 2 charms... but no Essence 3 because he didn't have enough prereq charms), and 10 other charms.<br /> Without Supernal abilities, Ferocious Lawyer of Statistics would probably have been a more optimised character than Expositor of Versimillitudian Enjoyment anyway, but Supernal allows her to do so even more.<br /> <br /> <br /> *My Night once hit a Resistance-Supernal Dawn with a <i><b>53-damage dice</b></i> decisive. He went from unwounded to... in his -1s. Then he chopped off my hand, knocked me out, and crucified me. That's the power of Resistance-Supernal + optimised stats + heavy artefact armour.<br /> <br /> Saying that, while Lunars don't get Supernals, they do generally start with more applicable excellencies, and the ability to turn into a whole bunch of useful animals. That'll improve over time as they eat more, but not as significantly as charms. So I think that might to some extent counter the Supernal bonus.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Lunars are different enough that you can probably focus on a different niche (or being an all-rounder) and so not need to compete with Supernals per-se.<br /> <br /> What I mean is, if you have a Full Moon berzerker, a Night thief, a Twilight craftsman, and a Changing Moon trickster, everyone has different strengths and weaknesses and probably no-one feels that other people's min-maxed characters make their character a lame copy.<br /> <br /> I used to play a No Moon sorcerer and shapeshifter. None of the Solars were better at me at shapeshifting, I'll tell you that! And while occasionally other players had sorcerers, they had different spells, so I never felt like my character was a worse version of theirs.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is not to say it's okay to make Lunars rubbish. It'd be pretty lame if Lunars just were massively inferior to Solars.<br /> I think Angwe's point that, in theory, it'd be rubbish if a Lunar who turned into a Tyrant Lizard was rubbish compared to the (non-Exalt) Tyrant Lizard familiar of a Solar. I don't think that'll actually happen (the Lunar just has so many more charm options), but it's not a ridiculous point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that players can start the game with <i>wildly </i>different powerlevels has proven problematic in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found that as well. It doesn't help that the more optimised players tend to understand their own charms and how to use them best better than other players anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-18-2018, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T08:17:27-07:00","id":1255264,"title":"","content":"Yes! The Wizard of Oz made my point better than me! Don't get me wrong, in Ex 2.X I usually gravitated towards the other splats, Lunars in particular. I never had too much problems giving my characters their place in the group, but supernals, well, they change the equation.<br /> <br /> Currently playing a supernal survival solar, and I <i>seriously</i> doubt a Lunar can shift into a similar beastform and come close to comparing, at least in the E2 range, and I doubt the E3 range either. I mean, sure, it's not shapeshifting per se, but with the possession it's pretty damn close. I mean, there's a cat, a rat, 2 wolves, a hawk and a tyrant lizard around and they basically have <i>Solar</i> charms, both for combat and stealth.<br /> <br /> I mean, this is just one build obviously, and one which deliberately attempted to channel the Lunar vibe and trample over their niche, but we're struggling with the Dragonblooded already, in a way they feel <i>weaker </i>relative to Solars than in second edition, and I hope Lunars avoid that. Definitely wish to put my finger on why though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T08:28:38-07:00","id":1255265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1255264#post1255264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes! The Wizard of Oz made my point better than me! Don't get me wrong, in Ex 2.X I usually gravitated towards the other splats, Lunars in particular. I never had too much problems giving my characters their place in the group, but supernals, well, they change the equation.<br /> <br /> Currently playing a supernal survival solar, and I <i>seriously</i> doubt a Lunar can shift into a similar beastform and come close to comparing, at least in the E2 range, and I doubt the E3 range either. I mean, sure, it's not shapeshifting per se, but with the possession it's pretty damn close. I mean, there's a cat, a rat, 2 wolves, a hawk and a tyrant lizard around and they basically have <i>Solar</i> charms, both for combat and stealth.<br /> <br /> I mean, this is just one build obviously, and one which deliberately attempted to channel the Lunar vibe and trample over their niche, but we're struggling with the Dragonblooded already, in a way they feel <i>weaker </i>relative to Solars than in second edition, and I hope Lunars avoid that. Definitely wish to put my finger on why though!</div> </div> </div> </div>If supernal is an issue you could just depower or remove it in favor of something else. I honestly don't like supernal. It's kind of bullshit in a mixed game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T08:47:58-07:00","id":1255268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1255264#post1255264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, this is just one build obviously, and one which deliberately attempted to channel the Lunar vibe and trample over their niche, but we're struggling with the Dragonblooded already, in a way they feel <i>weaker </i>relative to Solars than in second edition, and I hope Lunars avoid that. Definitely wish to put my finger on why though!</div> </div> </div> </div>2nd ed Solars' lack of free reflexives? Against a Solar without a paranoia combo, DBs could sometimes get the advantage over Solars from being able to use free reflexives.<br /> Also, they got far more artefacts and hearthstones.<br /> <br /> (I'd say overall DBs were way weaker, because they didn't have paranoia combos. But that might be why they feel weaker.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Currently playing a supernal survival solar, and I </i><i>seriously</i><i> doubt a Lunar can shift into a similar beastform and come close to comparing, at least in the E2 range, and I doubt the E3 range either.</i> </div> </div> </div>I think the Lunars' excellencies and charms are what will make them more powerful. Of course, we haven't seen much of their charms yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-18-2018, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T09:09:53-07:00","id":1255273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1255268#post1255268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Lunars' excellencies and charms are what will make them more powerful. Of course, we haven't seen much of their charms yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>And of course nothing stopping a Lunar having like two Tyrant Lizards as familiars and boosting them with Lunar Familiar Charms, and then becoming a Tyrant Lizard themselves. Supernal Survival Solars will always be at least one Tyrant Lizard behind an equivalent Lunar. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T17:02:02-07:00","id":1255366,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think that there ought to be a &quot;supernal&quot; variant for Sidereals and Lunars, but make it lesser in effect, like choose one attribute/ability for which you can buy charms as if your essence were one higher than normal. It's a decent enough boost to your options, though still far less than what Supernal gives. But as you're playing a character with limited xp to spend on charms it should balance it out by making the sids/lunars be more varied, if for no other reason than they can only become so good in combat so fast.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1255256#post1255256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, this is not to say it's okay to make Lunars rubbish. It'd be pretty lame if Lunars just were massively inferior to Solars.<br /> I think Angwe's point that, in theory, it'd be rubbish if a Lunar who turned into a Tyrant Lizard was rubbish compared to the (non-Exalt) Tyrant Lizard familiar of a Solar. I don't think that'll actually happen (the Lunar just has so many more charm options), but it's not a ridiculous point.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've found that as well. It doesn't help that the more optimised players tend to understand their own charms and how to use them best better than other players anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I will say that is a concern, a Lunar is one character who can turn into a tyrant lizard, a Solar can potentially be a Tyrant Lizard and a solar demigod and both have better than fair chance of being outright better than whatever the Lunar can do. This is partially why I'm really uncertain about giving Legendary Size forms such a high cost to them. If the Lunar can find themselves hard pressed to compete with the Solar's Familiar in a Kaiju battle, then I'd say there's significant risk of them being the second wheel.<br /> <br /> One thing that the high cost of the current charm does is that it makes the Lunar's charm usage while a giant stompy monster very <b>limited</b> unlike what a Solar can do for their familiar. So them having more charm options hardly matters when they'll have little ability to upkeep the energy required to power the charms whilst the Solar's completely unhindered in that regard.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1255265#post1255265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If supernal is an issue you could just depower or remove it in favor of something else. I honestly don't like supernal. It's kind of bullshit in a mixed game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the problem is that there's high costs associated with a Kaiju Lunar that a boosted Familiar of the Solar's doesn't need to worry about. The familiar doesn't impact the rate that they solar gains charms, and the solar's able to boost it's pet with said charms. The Lunar's hefty restrictions upon Kaiju forms makes it highly limited on what it can do with their own charms. So even if it's a Solar's pet against the Lunar and the Solar does nothing but watch, the Lunar's still at a massive disadvantage, and I'm not sure that'll ever abate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 09-18-2018, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T20:11:30-07:00","id":1255409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1255366#post1255366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem is that there's high costs associated with a Kaiju Lunar that a boosted Familiar of the Solar's doesn't need to worry about. The familiar doesn't impact the rate that they solar gains charms, and the solar's able to boost it's pet with said charms. The Lunar's hefty restrictions upon Kaiju forms makes it highly limited on what it can do with their own charms. So even if it's a Solar's pet against the Lunar and the Solar does nothing but watch, the Lunar's still at a massive disadvantage, and I'm not sure that'll ever abate.</div> </div> </div> </div>...wait, is this actually a thing people are worrying about?!<br /> <br /> OK. First, go read Prototype's post right above yours, because it is both right and also quite funny.<br /> <br /> Second...don't worry. Lunar T Rexes will be cooler than Solar Pet T Rexes, I promise. In fact, I am willing to wager that if you build a starting Solar with a pet T Rex and Survival Supernal, and I build a starting Lunar built to turn into a T Rex, the Lunar's gonna beat the Solar's pet, ESPECIALLY if the Lunar gets to play with all his toys and the Solar does nothing but watch! Lunars have lots of nasty tricks that Pet Reptar just won't have the counters for. Until the rules come out speculation is a little pointless, but seriously. You and me. Neutral ST. Giant Dino Deathmatch. Let our Big Mouth and Tiny Hands Kung Fu answer this question once and for all!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T02:13:10-07:00","id":1255447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1255409#post1255409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and me. Neutral ST. Giant Dino Deathmatch. Let our Big Mouth and Tiny Hands Kung Fu answer this question once and for all!</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do I buy tickets to this event?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T03:05:26-07:00","id":1255453,"title":"","content":"I applaud Dino Kaiju death matches! Perhaps the playtesters can run one and give us the narrative result!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1255268#post1255268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Lunars' excellencies and charms are what will make them more powerful. Of course, we haven't seen much of their charms yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, yes, but excellencies will definitely not be where they will have the edge! I mean, I think you underestimate just how wide the gap is. It would have to be other charms! Or simply avoiding this fight. Not easy to get away from a supernal survival solar with a Tyrant Lizard pet, but I still give better odds ;-)<br /> <br /> If we assume we take just the minimum charms to DPM, nothing fancy or special. We increase our favorite dino's attack ability and dex once through Bestial Traits Technique, and activate Sage Beast Virtue for a +1 bump to all attributes and defenses. Solar Tyrant Dino's attacks will be 3 higher than the Lunar for the scene, so in the 14 to 16 range. That's where the Lunar gets if they use their excellency, but Solar Dino also adds +ess successes from Deadly Predator Method on top of that. If we look at defenses they will be 2 or 3 higher than the baseline, depending what you set it's abilities and attributes at, so that also matches the Lunar's excellency. <br /> <br /> Soak is 10 above base-line, with immunity to decisive damage. Damage is 1 + ess higher than baseline. 2 if solar drops 2x in increasing their pet's strength, and, oh, hey, decisive attacks don't reset initiative.<br /> <br /> All of the above is scene length for 20 motes and 2 wp committed (and through spirit-tied pet this is actually 15 motes, 1 wp), and of course Lunar Dino has to pay 4 motes per round just to be a Tyrant Lizard and 15 motes committed, and needs to use their excellency just to match Solar Dino's attack and defense pools.<br /> <br /> We haven't even accounted for Solar pet's master actually spending motes in combat on charms such as Familiar-Honing Instruction or Ambush Predator Style. Or stuff like having the charm to give access to stealth charms when possessing. Even the above gap is insanely hard to bridge, and will have the Lunar absolutely draining motes like a lunatic, so let's assume the Solar wanders off for a smoke after sending in Solar Dino. And stuff like the 'immunity from decisive damage', and 'decisive attacks don't reset initiative' bits will be impossible to compensate for at the lower essence ranges and so expensive mote-wise as to be unaffordable in such a fight even if they were!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T07:21:01-07:00","id":1255479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1255453#post1255453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much exactly this, like the fact that a lunar will have more combat charms means nothing when they can't hit and can't do any damage because the raw dice gap is too high. Like I have played with a supernal survival solar and its cool but it straight up turns the pet into localized &quot;I win&quot; button to anything less than another solar. Which is cool but kind of makes the combat shapeshifting thing kind of a irrelevant side show when another players 3 dot familiar outshines you and then the solar themselves can be off doing there own thing.<br /> <br /> Though honestly I feel the bigger problem is why people keep pushing the idea that Lunars can keep up with a all solar circle instead of showing the benefits of running a all lunar game like you can do with dragonblooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T08:53:22-07:00","id":1255499,"title":"","content":"I would like to run an all-Lunar game. But in practice, I think they'll mostly be used in a mixed game (or as NPCs, of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T09:39:21-07:00","id":1255514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1255453#post1255453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I applaud Dino Kaiju death matches! Perhaps the playtesters can run one and give us the narrative result!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm, yes, but excellencies will definitely not be where they will have the edge! I mean, I think you underestimate just how wide the gap is. It would have to be other charms! Or simply avoiding this fight. Not easy to get away from a supernal survival solar with a Tyrant Lizard pet, but I still give better odds ;-)<br /> <br /> If we assume we take just the minimum charms to DPM, nothing fancy or special. We increase our favorite dino's attack ability and dex once through Bestial Traits Technique, and activate Sage Beast Virtue for a +1 bump to all attributes and defenses. Solar Tyrant Dino's attacks will be 3 higher than the Lunar for the scene, so in the 14 to 16 range. That's where the Lunar gets if they use their excellency, but Solar Dino also adds +ess successes from Deadly Predator Method on top of that. If we look at defenses they will be 2 or 3 higher than the baseline, depending what you set it's abilities and attributes at, so that also matches the Lunar's excellency. <br /> <br /> Soak is 10 above base-line, with immunity to decisive damage. Damage is 1 + ess higher than baseline. 2 if solar drops 2x in increasing their pet's strength, and, oh, hey, decisive attacks don't reset initiative.<br /> <br /> All of the above is scene length for 20 motes and 2 wp committed (and through spirit-tied pet this is actually 15 motes, 1 wp), and of course Lunar Dino has to pay 4 motes per round just to be a Tyrant Lizard and 15 motes committed, and needs to use their excellency just to match Solar Dino's attack and defense pools.<br /> <br /> We haven't even accounted for Solar pet's master actually spending motes in combat on charms such as Familiar-Honing Instruction or Ambush Predator Style. Or stuff like having the charm to give access to stealth charms when possessing. Even the above gap is insanely hard to bridge, and will have the Lunar absolutely draining motes like a lunatic, so let's assume the Solar wanders off for a smoke after sending in Solar Dino. And stuff like the 'immunity from decisive damage', and 'decisive attacks don't reset initiative' bits will be impossible to compensate for at the lower essence ranges and so expensive mote-wise as to be unaffordable in such a fight even if they were!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not worried. There's more to fights than dice pools in a white room. If the Solar wanders off for a smoke, and it's buffed pet vs Lunar, I am betting on the Lunar. <br /> <br /> If the Solar's there and actively participating in the fight ((my T-Rex wielding Survival Solar took Ride and Archery for extra murdery/mobility shenanigans)), then...yeah. A Solar and his pet are probably going to win a fight with an outnumbered Lunar unless the Lunar also brings friends!<br /> <br /> But talk is cheap. Once the rules are out, let's do some test matches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T10:24:22-07:00","id":1256502,"title":"","content":"Something I feel worth mentioning in the Dino Cage Match is what actually happens before the fight: getting your tyrant lizard there.<br /> There is no subtle way to have a tyrant lizard follow you. These are, to my knowledge, untameable death machines that can potentially wipe a village off the map. People will know you're coming, know you have a tyrant lizard, so you better be ready for them to react accordingly.<br /> But for the Lunar, they have an easier time hiding they can turn into a tyrant lizard than most folks have hiding a dagger. You're getting to fight this big old bastard when HOLY HELL THAT'S A TYRANT LIZARD HOW!?<br /> A solar can bring a tyrant lizard to a siege. A lunar can bring one to a fist fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23912-scottsman","name":"Scottsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T10:45:20-07:00","id":1256510,"title":"","content":"That's true... for a little while.<br /> <br /> But when you combine their speed with Solar Ride charms, you can cover a lot of ground on your Tyrant lizard mount very quickly. Like, you can't just be chilling in Nexus and pull a T Rex outta your pocket (unless you're a Twilight maybe? I don't remember the limits on their familiar anima trick), but you can probably show up over the horizon and be in the middle of town with your T Rex before Nexus can prepare a response.<br /> <br /> ...also? Sometimes Tyrant Lizard Fly.<br /> <br /> Edit: None of these options are subtle, but they are fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T11:00:17-07:00","id":1256513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256510#post1256510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true... for a little while.<br /> <br /> But when you combine their speed with Solar Ride charms, you can cover a lot of ground on your Tyrant lizard mount very quickly. Like, you can't just be chilling in Nexus and pull a T Rex outta your pocket (unless you're a Twilight maybe? I don't remember the limits on their familiar anima trick), but you can probably show up over the horizon and be in the middle of town with your T Rex before Nexus can prepare a response.<br /> <br /> ...also? Sometimes Tyrant Lizard Fly.<br /> <br /> Edit: None of these options are subtle, but they are fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh these are great options, but only usable if you're expecting a Tyrant Lizard level fight from the get go. I think the main difference we'll see is that a Solar can bring more force to bear if he knows he'll need it ahead of time, a Lunar will always have that force available, in case a massive threat catches you by surprise. As usual, the advantage for Lunars will be their flexibility. Not to mention, any essence 1 Lunar with sufficient stats can pull this off, while the horrendously strong charms for familiars requires either supernal survival or higher essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23912-scottsman","name":"Scottsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T12:38:38-07:00","id":1256526,"title":"","content":"One of our PCs had a Tyrant Lizard familiar.<br /> <br /> It was pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> Until the fight where it ended up on the opposite side of the battlefield to its owner (who was not, tbh, very tough, being an archer and Tyrant Lizard-handler), and a Lunar smacked the Solar round the back of the head, killing him. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>unless you're a Twilight maybe? I don't remember the limits on their familiar anima trick</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Spirits only, I'm afraid.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T15:01:56-07:00","id":1256559,"title":"","content":"So, reading the comparison of supernatural survival Solar vs Lunar and fining something weird. You are pitting a solar with +15 (if you have Deadly predator method you invested 13 charms) charms vs a lunar that only uses an excellency and the charm to get legendary size. Is obvious that the solar will win in this conditions, but im sure that the lunar will have more tools to use in that kind of fights.<br /> So this kind of theory crafting right now is invalid because have a very big lack of information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12483-ale137","user":"ale137","date":". 09-22-2018, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12483-ale137","name":"ale137","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T15:40:59-07:00","id":1256564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ale137</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256559#post1256559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, reading the comparison of supernatural survival Solar vs Lunar and fining something weird. You are pitting a solar with +15 (if you have Deadly predator method you invested 13 charms) charms vs a lunar that only uses an excellency and the charm to get legendary size. Is obvious that the solar will win in this conditions, but im sure that the lunar will have more tools to use in that kind of fights.<br /> So this kind of theory crafting right now is invalid because have a very big lack of information.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was more just a observation on a potential problem.<br /> <br /> We haven't seen nearly enough of the lunar charmset to actually make a character though I would presume someone who wanted to fight as a tyrant lizard would have more than just the excellency.<br /> <br /> You are correct it is a bit of a moot point though but until we get more information there isn't that much else to discuss.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T16:34:22-07:00","id":1256575,"title":"","content":"It does seem to me that a Lunar who is faced with a tyrant lizard that has been raised and trained and invested with power by a dedicated Solar animal trainer, and opts to fight it by turning into another tyrant lizard and getting into a straight up brawl, might be doing it because they feel as though they have something to prove. I suspect that a fairly advanced Lunar might be able to prove it fairly well, but in most other cases the Lunar might be better off turning into something small enough for the dinosaur to have a hard time seeing or hitting, and then poisoning them, or getting behind them to attack the Solar.<br /> <br /> Still, that's probably not the most pressing comparison; I can see how the people that have raised concern are looking at things more in terms of how either of them utilise the form of a tyrant lizard to exert themselves against other obstacles.<br /> <br /> In which case, it may be that at the end of things, the Solar produces the superior tyrant lizard; they're still the mightiest of the Exalted. The Lunar advantage would strike me as being able to place the tyrant lizard more readily among a variety of other options, that Charms to benefit the tyrant lizard form will also be able to benefit a variety of other functions (whereas a Solar who has put a lot into empowering their animal is giving up the opportunity to learn things that directly benefit themselves, and becomes a bit dependent on the animal being around), and the Lunar doesn't need to worry about some of the practical concerns (such as housing, movement and feeding) that really ought to be attached to the issue of a tyrant lizard familiar. <br /> <br /> Besides all of that, as far as I know, we thus far only have an entry level Lunar Charm for turning into huge animals, which is being compared to the result of a whole suite of Solar Charms being applied at once. That seems like a necessary limit when we're comparing a published book to snippets being furtively glimpsed through a key hole, but it should probably be acknowledged as such.<br /> <br /> And overall, this is information coming from a playtest, the purpose of which is to figure out whether or not ideas work. Pointing out possible flaws or emergent issues is all well and good, but it should be kept in perspective, and hold short of being acrimonious about it not being its best the first time around (no published work is), or authoritatively declaring it to be terrible and doomed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T01:38:05-07:00","id":1256660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256575#post1256575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does seem to me that a Lunar who is faced with a tyrant lizard that has been raised and trained and invested with power by a dedicated Solar animal trainer, and opts to fight it by turning into another tyrant lizard and getting into a straight up brawl, might be doing it because they feel as though they have something to prove. I suspect that a fairly advanced Lunar might be able to prove it fairly well, but in most other cases the Lunar might be better off turning into something small enough for the dinosaur to have a hard time seeing or hitting, and then poisoning them, or getting behind them to attack the Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess, but I think turning into a Tyrant Lizard is still the way to go. Then activate your Appearance and Wits charms. Seduce that sexy tyrant lizard. The Solar master will be so horrified by the gargantuan obscene mating before his eyes that he'll run away and join a monastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T06:16:38-07:00","id":1256699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256660#post1256660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess, but I think turning into a Tyrant Lizard is still the way to go. Then activate your Appearance and Wits charms. Seduce that sexy tyrant lizard. The Solar master will be so horrified by the gargantuan obscene mating before his eyes that he'll run away and join a monastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that reminds me to research how hard it is to disrupt or damage the loyalty of familiars to see what kind of extra. powers it takes to keep them loyal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T07:40:20-07:00","id":1256709,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Solars have lots of charms to make their familiar immune to fear...but not so much seduction. And Lunars have charms for talking to animals, which presumably means they could bring social influence to bear against the tyrant lizard. So long as they're not trying threaten actions it might work- thing's social defenses aren't massive. Might be able to talk it down or trick it into doing something stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T10:31:50-07:00","id":1256746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cryo-Seraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256699#post1256699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, that reminds me to research how hard it is to disrupt or damage the loyalty of familiars to see what kind of extra. powers it takes to keep them loyal</div> </div> </div> </div>Innately... Familiars actually don't come with any particular loyalty. But there is a charm where you can give them a Defining Intimacy of loyalty for 2xp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T11:25:15-07:00","id":1256765,"title":"","content":"Although anything that wasn't at least fond you wouldn't become your familiar in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T12:01:26-07:00","id":1256775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256709#post1256709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Solars have lots of charms to make their familiar immune to fear...but not so much seduction. And Lunars have charms for talking to animals, which presumably means they could bring social influence to bear against the tyrant lizard. So long as they're not trying threaten actions it might work- thing's social defenses aren't massive. Might be able to talk it down or trick it into doing something stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>The charm Spirit-Tied Pet, generates a defining intimacy for loyalty in your familiar. The charm reads that &quot;no influence of any kind, other then the Solar, can make the familiar act against this intimacy&quot;. All of the Solar survival buffing charms branch off this charm. So a Lunar who can talk to animals better have a plan B.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T12:02:10-07:00","id":1256776,"title":"","content":"You'd assume so, yeah. I personally would have a familiar start with a Major Intimacy to its owner, which could go up or down. Clearly they don't automatically have a Defining Intimacy (since otherwise why have the charm?), but it would seem odd to start with a mystic bond with your pet dog, except your dog doesn't give two hoots about you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T12:07:17-07:00","id":1256779,"title":"","content":"And now I\u2019m imagining a Lunar in Tyrant Lizard form psychoanalyzing the Tyrant Lizard Familar, complete with couch and everything. \u201cSo, tell me, how do you really feel about this human ordering you around?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T13:11:34-07:00","id":1256785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256775#post1256775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The charm Spirit-Tied Pet, generates a defining intimacy for loyalty in your familiar. The charm reads that &amp;quot;no influence of any kind, other then the Solar, can make the familiar act against this intimacy&amp;quot;. All of the Solar survival buffing charms branch off this charm. So a Lunar who can talk to animals better have a plan B.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not gonna talk the T Rex into turning on the Solar, but you might talk it out of fighting you. Just be all, 'Look, bro, your Solar friend over there is trying to impress potential mates. If you fight me for him, he's not showing any dominance or fitness! The best thing you can do for him here is let him face me on his own. I promise I won't kill him if I win.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, T-Rex! It is I, your Solar, and deeefinitely not a shapeshifter disguised as him down to his scent! I need you to play dead for me. Yes, that's right, lie down prone. Good boy! Now close your eyes for just a minute...&quot;<br /> <br /> Unbreakable Defining Intimacies are as much a weakness as a strength. Probably works on bound demons too...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T13:58:56-07:00","id":1256791,"title":"","content":"I don't know if you can spoof a magical connection between two beings like that. It might be worth asking in the Dev's thread though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T14:56:14-07:00","id":1256804,"title":"","content":"Why make it an Intimacy if it's not intended to be used with the socially system?<br /> <br /> Edit: Eating a bound demon and taking on its intimacy of loyalty seems like a good way to get close to a sorcerer...who will be very surprised indeed when you start disobeying orders and eating him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 09-23-2018, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T15:19:33-07:00","id":1256811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256804#post1256804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why make it an Intimacy if it's not intended to be used with the socially system?<br /> <br /> Edit: Eating a bound demon and taking on its intimacy of loyalty seems like a good way to get close to a sorcerer...who will be very surprised indeed when you start disobeying orders and eating him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a defining intimacy primarily to STOP people from using the social system on the pet. If a solar tells its tyrant lizard to eat you, you are not talking your way out of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T16:13:06-07:00","id":1256820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256811#post1256811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a defining intimacy primarily to STOP people from using the social system on the pet. If a solar tells its tyrant lizard to eat you, you are not talking your way out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but intimacies cut both ways. My love for my family might protect me from getting tricked into hurting them...but it makes me a lot easier to talk into doing something if you threaten them or if you convince me helping you will help them. Talking a demon bound to guard a sorcerer's hoard into helping you get into the hoard won't work...but preying upon it's loyalty to get it to accept a gift for addition to the hoard is a good way to smuggle in a bomb or a teleporter or something. Mechanics are best when they open story options, not just shut 'em down.<br /> <br /> And Tyrant Lizards are many things, but...well, bright is not usually one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T16:17:21-07:00","id":1256821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256820#post1256820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but intimacies cut both ways. My love for my family might protect me from getting tricked into hurting them...but it makes me a lot easier to talk into doing something if you threaten them or if you convince me helping you will help them. Talking a demon bound to guard a sorcerer's hoard into helping you get into the hoard won't work...but preying upon it's loyalty to get it to accept a gift for addition to the hoard is a good way to smuggle in a bomb or a teleporter or something. Mechanics are best when they open story options, not just shut 'em down.<br /> <br /> And Tyrant Lizards are many things, but...well, bright is not usually one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like you keep bringing up demons and I feel you are muddying the waters just a bit.<br /> <br /> A solar has just told their pet tyrant lizard to eat you. What social influence do you feel you can do with the defining intimacy in place to not having to fight the tyrant lizard.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T16:58:23-07:00","id":1256831,"title":"","content":"Be the Solar convincingly enough to fool the Tyrant Lizard. Give it conflicting orders-a Tyrant Lizard who won't listen to &quot;STOP!&quot; or &quot;Stand down!&quot; yelled in the Boss' voice isn't a great familiar!<br /> <br /> As a Lunar, it's not always about overwhelming force-there's no obligation to fight with honor if somebody's just sicced a Tyrant Lizard on you!<br /> <br /> You can use social influence in combat this edition. Heck, Lunars have a couple tricks for saying things to the Tyrant Lizard that it's boss can't understand. You don't need to win the whole fight that way, but if you can buy yourself a round or put your opponent in a disadvantageous position before you go in for the kill, why not?<br /> <br /> Edit: the Defining Loyalty intimacy is the one you USE, it's the only one you likely know the beast has anyway-who does checks to learn intimacies on a T Rex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T17:19:06-07:00","id":1256835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256820#post1256820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Tyrant Lizards are many things, but...well, bright is not usually one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That strikes me as a far stronger argument <b>against</b> being able to reach a tyrant lizard through sophisticated and occasionally convoluted arguments. I'll reserve full judgement for social interaction with animals until we see what kinds of powers Lunars might have for it*, but for the time being I find any argument based on acting as though these things have comprehension and communication comparable to those of a human to be spurious.<br /> <br /> Strictly speaking, you're not incorrect about Intimacies in principle, but I think context and common sense need to be applied, and those would generally preclude animals being susceptible to complex reasoning.<br /> <br /> I think the biggest risk that a Defining Intimacy brings to a familiar tyrant lizard is that it has been instilled with a will to act that can take priority over its survival instinct. I don't think it's an explicit part of the familiar or animal training rules, but I think it's reasonable to assume that, barring such an Intimacy, even being a familiar doesn't change the fact that a badly injured animal, even a tyrant lizard, will almost always elect to retreat.<br /> <br /> If a Solar orders a tyrant lizard with a Defining Intimacy to fight a Lunar, then its danger seems far more likely to be that the thing will be willing to fight a damn Lunar, and will continue doing so even past the point that the Lunar (in human form) punches it in the face and breaks its damn jaw.<br /> <br /> I'm all for diverse options for handling obstacles and challenges, but there is a reasonable limit, and I think that being able to talk down or around a raging dinosaur that a supernally powerful trainer has tamed, raised up, and commanded to attack you falls under it. Intimidating the thing to a degree that the command has difficulty spurring it over works. Magically instilling a state of calm, sure. Turning into the same animal of a sexually compatible type and putting its mind on something else? Well, it has mythic precedent. Not so much convincing it that the best interests of its master are best met by not following the command, I should think.<br /> <br /> * Although I honestly expect a lot of such things to be focused, limited and rather primal, rather than being able to hold a conversation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You can use social influence in combat this edition. Heck, Lunars have a couple tricks for saying things to the Tyrant Lizard that it's boss can't understand.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Perhaps, but under the assumption that a lot of things that could be said to try and manipulate its Tie won't make sense to it, I'd imagine that a lot of countermeasures to a Defining Intimacy require another, conflicting Defining Intimacy, and building that up from nothing under combat conditions would be hard enough even with a person. With an animal? Well, it's not outside the realms of possibility that you're carrying something extremely tasty, buuuutt\u2026<br /> <br /> Now, there may still be some Charms that function through a mechanism of treating a target, even an animal, as though it has a strong Intimacy, and that may be valid, but it's more a matter of Lunar magic than effectively leveraging the social system.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T18:22:47-07:00","id":1256854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256804#post1256804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why make it an Intimacy if it's not intended to be used with the socially system?<br /> <br /> Edit: Eating a bound demon and taking on its intimacy of loyalty seems like a good way to get close to a sorcerer...who will be very surprised indeed when you start disobeying orders and eating him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had no objections to leveraging it the first way. I was just thinking that you might not be able to pretend to be the familiar's master effectively, even if you had stolen their shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T18:33:47-07:00","id":1256856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256785#post1256785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not gonna talk the T Rex into turning on the Solar, but you might talk it out of fighting you. Just be all, 'Look, bro, your Solar friend over there is trying to impress potential mates. If you fight me for him, he's not showing any dominance or fitness! The best thing you can do for him here is let him face me on his own. I promise I won't kill him if I win.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, T-Rex! It is I, your Solar, and deeefinitely not a shapeshifter disguised as him down to his scent! I need you to play dead for me. Yes, that's right, lie down prone. Good boy! Now close your eyes for just a minute...&quot;<br /> <br /> Unbreakable Defining Intimacies are as much a weakness as a strength. Probably works on bound demons too...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the second option wouldn't work for our group. The devs have said it's up to the ST to decide if a simple disguise is enough to fool a familiar with a mystic bond. I'm of the opinion that it's not. Since I'm the ST, trying to fool the familiar with a disguise will end up with you getting eaten.<br /> <br /> As for the first option, it's something you could try. However, the familiar has absolute loyalty, so it's not going to stand by while you attack it's master. Your best bet would be to try and deceive it in a way that you're not calling it's loyalty into question. Something like convincing the Tyrant Lizard you just saw a herd of plump mountain goats on the other side of the hill, then attack the master while the familiar goes looking for a meal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T19:03:54-07:00","id":1256860,"title":"","content":"I have a question for those who've done the played the Lunar playtest, what reason is there to use moonsilver weapons if you're focused on Protean charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T19:08:18-07:00","id":1256861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256856#post1256856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the second option wouldn't work for our group. The devs have said it's up to the ST to decide if a simple disguise is enough to fool a familiar with a mystic bond. I'm of the opinion that it's not. Since I'm the ST, trying to fool the familiar with a disguise will end up with you getting eaten.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me that makes familiars very valuable. An animal capable of seeing through any mundane disguise in relation to their masters appearance is crazy good. I could see it being common practice for paranoid merchant princes to have a pet bird to validate their identity if that is how they worked. Possibly almost expected in some circles as an authentication method. While this could be seen as needed to protect the sanctity of the familiar merit it does have an impact on the world and does screw over those interested in disguise.<br /> <br /> If the familiar had abilities that explicity interacted with its master i could see that as a form of detection. However none exist that i can find. If issues do arise then a solar can directly take control of their familiar with spirit tied pet. Maybe a working for a telepathic bond with a familiar could also work as a way to ensure they are never tricked. Or more mundane options of training using an obscure language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T19:08:27-07:00","id":1256862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1235400-lunars-playtest?p=1256856#post1256856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the second option wouldn't work for our group. The devs have said it's up to the ST to decide if a simple disguise is enough to fool a familiar with a mystic bond. I'm of the opinion that it's not. Since I'm the ST, trying to fool the familiar with a disguise will end up with you getting eaten.<br /> <br /> As for the first option, it's something you could try. However, the familiar has absolute loyalty, so it's not going to stand by while you attack it's master. Your best bet would be to try and deceive it in a way that you're not calling it's loyalty into question. Something like convincing the Tyrant Lizard you just saw a herd of plump mountain goats on the other side of the hill, then attack the master while the familiar goes looking for a meal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair thing to rule. That said, if I'm the ST, which I usually am in my games, magical disguises don't get easily counteracted by ties like the Familiar bond or being a bound demon or, heck, the Solar/Lunar Bond. Disguises and mistaken identities and such just cause too much juicy drama to leave out of a game!<br /> <br /> If a Lunar is disguising herself as your Familiar, and you failed an opposed roll, I would say you're fooled until you try to use her senses or draw motes from her and it fails to work. If you're a Lunar and a Friend shows up disguised as your Solar Mate to convince you to do something and his Disguise roll beats you, I would say you're fooled until one of your Bond charms fails to work correctly on him.<br /> <br /> Defining Ties shouldn't be a perfect defense. They're also a &quot;I am vulnerable to this method of persuasion&quot; button that characters who are good at disguises can take advantage of.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the rules currently say a Night Caste can't go up to the Tyrant Lizard disguised as the Zenith who owns him and copy the Zenith's attack order to sic him on somebody without checking in with his circle mate...and the resulting drama is almost always gonna make for a better game.<br /> <br /> Familiars are cool animals, and the fact they have minds of their own means it's a bit harder to disarm you and hit you with your own medicine than if your weapon of choice is Volcano Cutter...but the thing about NPC pets and allies is that they do have minds of their own, and that means they'll do stuff sometimes that's not optimal, sometimes (intentionally or not) even stuff that goes against your best interests. I think that's half the fun!<br /> <br /> But since there's a bit of YMMV going on here, even putting aside impersonation of the Solar himself, there's probably going to be plenty of room in the Lunar charmset for social-fu tricks on animals, or during combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T05:25:07-07:00","id":1256935,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's also a difference between a disguise, and actual shapeshifting. Would definitely not let a familiar automatically detect that! Or bound demons for that matter. I mean, as a Lunar wearing a DB's form you should be able to swagger past his or her's loyal guard dogs or the summoned help, right?<br /> <br /> Is the Tell still around, by the way?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T06:22:26-07:00","id":1256942,"title":"","content":"Did the Survival training Charms include anything for giving direct commands? Because I'd say that the true master's compelling voice might be hard to imitate.<br /> <br /> It also might depend on how much object permanence one imagines a tyrant lizard to have; a shapeshifting Lunar might be able to imitate a scent perfectly enough to fool the keen senses of a tyrant lizard, but is it going to recognise that a scent that it was hunting has suddenly changed into a different one? Before even considering the improved acuity from being trained by a Solar.<br /> <br /> I think a Lunar who wants to try that tactic needs to come to the fight in the Solar's shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T06:26:38-07:00","id":1256943,"title":"","content":"It is. And generally speaking, it requires a Difficulty 7(!) Perception+Awareness roll to notice.<br /> <br /> We had some questions for Vance about exactly how it works (in terms of stuff like if I see a Lunar with a Tell I've never seen before, can I roll to notice it, or retroactively if I see another animal with the same strange feature later, etc) and he said there's a section in the book that addresses this kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}